   "<h2 id=\"Time-sharing-with-the-sum-constraint\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Time sharing with the sum constraint <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Time-sharing-with-the-sum-constraint\">#</a></h2>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.BroadcastChannel.isClosed_iUnion_thm7RegionOfLaw", "../.././",
   "The union over the joint laws of one fixed pair of auxiliary alphabets is closed.\x0a\x0aThe index is a space of probability measures on a finite ambient space, so it is compact once it\x0acarries the weak topology, and the union of a compact family of closed sets is closed as soon as\x0athe family has a closed graph. The graph is closed exactly when the twenty-five informations\x0adepend continuously on the joint law and the factorization cuts out a closed set of joint laws.\x0aEach information is a combination of entropies, whose continuity in the joint law is\x0a`continuous_entropy_of_discrete`; the missing piece is that the four clauses of the\x0afactorization cut out a closed set.\x0a\x0a@residual(plan:bc-computable-region-formalization) ",
   "<p>The union over the joint laws of one fixed pair of auxiliary alphabets is closed.</p><p>The index is a space of probability measures on a finite ambient space, so it is compact once it\x0acarries the weak topology, and the union of a compact family of closed sets is closed as soon as\x0athe family has a closed graph. The graph is closed exactly when the twenty-five informations\x0adepend continuously on the joint law and the factorization cuts out a closed set of joint laws.\x0aEach information is a combination of entropies, whose continuity in the joint law is\x0a<code>continuous_entropy_of_discrete</code>; the missing piece is that the four clauses of the\x0afactorization cut out a closed set.</p><p>@residual(plan:bc-computable-region-formalization)</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.channelCoding_entropy_exponent_eq", "./",
   "The entropy exponent identity for the i.i.d. ambient measure:\x0a`H(Z₀) - H(X₀) - H(Y₀) = -(mutualInfoOfChannel p W).toReal`,\x0awhere `(X₀, Y₀, Z₀)` are the 0-th marginals of the i.i.d. extension. ",
   "<p>The entropy exponent identity for the i.i.d. ambient measure:\x0a<code>H(Z₀) - H(X₀) - H(Y₀) = -(mutualInfoOfChannel p W).toReal</code>,\x0awhere <code>(X₀, Y₀, Z₀)</code> are the 0-th marginals of the i.i.d. extension.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.Channel", ".././",
   "A discrete memoryless channel (DMC) is just a (Markov) kernel `α → Measure β`.\x0aMarkov-ness is requested as a separate type-class hypothesis on the user side, so the\x0adefinition itself stays the bare `Kernel`. ",
   "<p>A discrete memoryless channel (DMC) is just a (Markov) kernel <code>α → Measure β</code>.\x0aMarkov-ness is requested as a separate type-class hypothesis on the user side, so the\x0adefinition itself stays the bare <code>Kernel</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.le_log_of_ceil_exp_le", "../.././",
   "If `⌈exp x⌉₊ ≤ M` then `x ≤ log M`, converting a message count into a rate bound.  From\x0a`exp x ≤ ⌈exp x⌉₊ ≤ M`, taking logs (both sides positive) gives `x = log (exp x) ≤ log M`. ",
   "<p>If <code>⌈exp x⌉₊ ≤ M</code> then <code>x ≤ log M</code>, converting a message count into a rate bound.  From\x0a<code>exp x ≤ ⌈exp x⌉₊ ≤ M</code>, taking logs (both sides positive) gives <code>x = log (exp x) ≤ log M</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCodingConverseGeneral.condMutualInfo_chain_rule_Y_2var", "./",
   "2-variable Y-axis conditional chain rule for `condMutualInfo`.\x0a\x0a```\x0aI(X; (A, B) | Wc) = I(X; A | Wc) + I(X; B | (Wc, A))\x0a```\x0a\x0aRequires `I(Wc; X) ≠ ∞`. ",
   "<p>2-variable Y-axis conditional chain rule for <code>condMutualInfo</code>.</p><pre><code>I(X; (A, B) | Wc) = I(X; A | Wc) + I(X; B | (Wc, A))\x0a</code></pre><p>Requires <code>I(Wc; X) ≠ ∞</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCodingFeedback.FeedbackCode", ".././",
   "A feedback code of length `n` with `M` messages. The encoder at time `i` takes\x0athe message and the prior outputs `Y_0, …, Y_{i-1}` to produce the input symbol\x0a`X_i ∈ α`. The decoder maps the full output block `Y^n` to a message guess.\x0a\x0a`X_i = encoder i m (y_0, …, y_{i-1})` — the causal structure is built into the type\x0asignature: `encoder i : Fin M → (Fin i.val → β) → α` only sees `Fin i.val → β`. ",
   "<p>A feedback code of length <code>n</code> with <code>M</code> messages. The encoder at time <code>i</code> takes\x0athe message and the prior outputs <code>Y_0, …, Y_{i-1}</code> to produce the input symbol\x0a<code>X_i ∈ α</code>. The decoder maps the full output block <code>Y^n</code> to a message guess.</p><p><code>X_i = encoder i m (y_0, …, y_{i-1})</code> — the causal structure is built into the type\x0asignature: <code>encoder i : Fin M → (Fin i.val → β) → α</code> only sees <code>Fin i.val → β</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.ShannonTheorem module doc 2", "../.././",
   "### Continuity of `I(p; W).toReal` in p ",
