  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.shannon_noisy_channel_coding_theorem_general", ".././",
   "**Shannon's noisy channel coding theorem** (general, max-error form): for `R < capacity W`\x0aand any `ε > 0`, there exists `N` such that for all `n ≥ N` there is a code with\x0a`M ≥ ⌈exp(nR)⌉` codewords achieving max-error less than `ε`. ",
   "<p><strong>Shannon's noisy channel coding theorem</strong> (general, max-error form): for <code>R &lt; capacity W</code>\x0aand any <code>ε &gt; 0</code>, there exists <code>N</code> such that for all <code>n ≥ N</code> there is a code with\x0a<code>M ≥ ⌈exp(nR)⌉</code> codewords achieving max-error less than <code>ε</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.highLLRSet", "../.././",
