  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Chernoff.Basic module doc 6", "./",
   "### Symmetry `Z_{P₁,P₂}(λ) = Z_{P₂,P₁}(1 - λ)` ",
   "<h3 id=\"Symmetry-Z-P₁-P₂-λ-=-Z-P₂-P₁-1-λ\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Symmetry <code>Z_{P₁,P₂}(λ) = Z_{P₂,P₁}(1 - λ)</code> <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Symmetry-Z-P₁-P₂-λ-=-Z-P₂-P₁-1-λ\">#</a></h3>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Chernoff.chernoffMediator", ".././",
   "The Chernoff mediator pmf `T_λ(a) := P₁(a)^(1-λ) · P₂(a)^λ / Z(λ)`. ",
   "<p>The Chernoff mediator pmf <code>T_λ(a) := P₁(a)^(1-λ) · P₂(a)^λ / Z(λ)</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Chernoff.Converse module doc 3", "../.././",
   "### Sanov lower bound and assembly\x0a\x0aThe headline of this section is\x0a\x0a`chernoff_converse : limsup_n -(1/n) log (bayesErrorMinPmf P₁ P₂ n) ≤ chernoffInfo P₁ P₂`.\x0a\x0aRoute: `chernoffMediator P₁ P₂ λ*` is the I-projection of `P₁` onto the half-space\x0a`{p : ∑ p_a log(P₂ a/P₁ a) ≥ 0}`; `csiszar_pythagoras_inequality` identifies\x0a`⨅_{p∈K} klDivPmf p P₁` with `klDivPmf (T_λ*) P₁ = chernoffInfo` (the variational identity\x0aabove). The error region `{x : P₁ⁿ(x) ≤ P₂ⁿ(x)}` is that half-space lifted to empirical type\x0aclasses, so `sanov_ldp_equality` supplies `(1/n) log P₁ⁿ(region) → -chernoffInfo`, and\x0a`bayesErrorMinPmf ≥ (1/2)·P₁ⁿ(region)` closes the converse. ",
   "<h3 id=\"Sanov-lower-bound-and-assembly\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Sanov lower bound and assembly <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Sanov-lower-bound-and-assembly\">#</a></h3><p>The headline of this section is</p><p><code>chernoff_converse : limsup_n -(1/n) log (bayesErrorMinPmf P₁ P₂ n) ≤ chernoffInfo P₁ P₂</code>.</p><p>Route: <code>chernoffMediator P₁ P₂ λ*</code> is the I-projection of <code>P₁</code> onto the half-space\x0a<code>{p : ∑ p_a log(P₂ a/P₁ a) ≥ 0}</code>; <code>csiszar_pythagoras_inequality</code> identifies\x0a<code>⨅_{p∈K} klDivPmf p P₁</code> with <code>klDivPmf (T_λ*) P₁ = chernoffInfo</code> (the variational identity\x0aabove). The error region <code>{x : P₁ⁿ(x) ≤ P₂ⁿ(x)}</code> is that half-space lifted to empirical type\x0aclasses, so <code>sanov_ldp_equality</code> supplies <code>(1/n) log P₁ⁿ(region) → -chernoffInfo</code>, and\x0a<code>bayesErrorMinPmf ≥ (1/2)·P₁ⁿ(region)</code> closes the converse.</p>"),
