  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Cramer.TiltedIID module doc 2", "../.././",
   "## Coordinate-eval family under the un-tilted base product ",
   "<h2 id=\"Coordinate-eval-family-under-the-un-tilted-base-product\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Coordinate-eval family under the un-tilted base product <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Coordinate-eval-family-under-the-un-tilted-base-product\">#</a></h2>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Cramer.TiltedLLN.tiltedMean_eq_deriv_cgf", "./",
   "The tilted mean equals the cgf derivative (cgf-derivative bridge).\x0a\x0aFor a bounded measurable `Y` under a probability measure `μ₀`, the tilted mean\x0a`∫ Y ∂(μ₀.tilted (lam·Y))` equals the first derivative of the cgf at `lam`:\x0a`∫ ω, Y ω ∂(μ₀.tilted (fun ω => lam * Y ω)) = deriv (cgf Y μ₀) lam`.\x0a\x0aThe interior side condition `lam ∈ interior (integrableExpSet Y μ₀)` holds\x0abecause boundedness of `Y` makes `exp (t·Y)` integrable for *every* `t`, so\x0a`integrableExpSet Y μ₀ = Set.univ` and its interior is again `Set.univ`.\x0a\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "<p>The tilted mean equals the cgf derivative (cgf-derivative bridge).</p><p>For a bounded measurable <code>Y</code> under a probability measure <code>μ₀</code>, the tilted mean\x0a<code>∫ Y ∂(μ₀.tilted (lam·Y))</code> equals the first derivative of the cgf at <code>lam</code>:\x0a<code>∫ ω, Y ω ∂(μ₀.tilted (fun ω =&gt; lam * Y ω)) = deriv (cgf Y μ₀) lam</code>.</p><p>The interior side condition <code>lam ∈ interior (integrableExpSet Y μ₀)</code> holds\x0abecause boundedness of <code>Y</code> makes <code>exp (t·Y)</code> integrable for <em>every</em> <code>t</code>, so\x0a<code>integrableExpSet Y μ₀ = Set.univ</code> and its interior is again <code>Set.univ</code>.</p><p>@audit:ok</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.CsiszarProjection module doc 0", ".././",
   "# Csiszár I-projection and the Pythagorean inequality\x0a\x0aFor a finite alphabet `α`, a full-support reference pmf `Q : α → ℝ`, and a closed convex\x0aset `K ⊆ stdSimplex ℝ α`:\x0a\x0a- Existence: there is `Q* ∈ K` minimizing `klDivPmf · Q` over `K`.\x0a- Uniqueness: the minimizer is unique.\x0a- The Pythagorean inequality (Cover-Thomas 11.6.1): for all `P ∈ K`,\x0a  `klDivPmf P Q ≥ klDivPmf P Q* + klDivPmf Q* Q`.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `klDivPmf P Q := ∑ a, Q a * klFun (P a / Q a)` — real-valued finite-alphabet KL divergence.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `csiszar_projection_exists` — existence via extreme value theorem.\x0a* `csiszar_projection_unique` — uniqueness via strict convexity.\x0a* `csiszar_pythagoras_inequality` — Pythagorean inequality via the first-order condition.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aProof strategy for the Pythagorean inequality: the first-order condition\x0a`∑ (P - Q*)(log Q* - log Q) ≥ 0` is derived from the right derivative of\x0a`t ↦ klDivPmf ((1-t)Q* + tP) Q` at `t = 0` being non-negative (minimality of `Q*`).\x0aCombined with the algebraic identity\x0a`klDivPmf P Q = klDivPmf P Q* + ∑ P·(log Q* - log Q)` and the expansion of\x0a`klDivPmf Q* Q`, this gives the inequality.\x0a\x0a## References\x0a\x0a* T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, *Elements of Information Theory* (2nd ed.), Wiley, 2006.\x0a  Theorem 11.6.1.\x0a",
   "<h1 id=\"Csiszár-I-projection-and-the-Pythagorean-inequality\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Csiszár I-projection and the Pythagorean inequality <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Csiszár-I-projection-and-the-Pythagorean-inequality\">#</a></h1><p>For a finite alphabet <code>α</code>, a full-support reference pmf <code>Q : α → ℝ</code>, and a closed convex\x0aset <code>K ⊆ stdSimplex ℝ α</code>:</p><ul><li>Existence: there is <code>Q* ∈ K</code> minimizing <code>klDivPmf · Q</code> over <code>K</code>.</li><li>Uniqueness: the minimizer is unique.</li><li>The Pythagorean inequality (Cover-Thomas 11.6.1): for all <code>P ∈ K</code>,\x0a<code>klDivPmf P Q ≥ klDivPmf P Q* + klDivPmf Q* Q</code>.</li></ul><h2 id=\"Main-definitions\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Main definitions <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Main-definitions\">#</a></h2><ul><li><code>klDivPmf P Q := ∑ a, Q a * klFun (P a / Q a)</code> — real-valued finite-alphabet KL divergence.</li></ul><h2 id=\"Main-statements\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Main statements <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Main-statements\">#</a></h2><ul><li><code>csiszar_projection_exists</code> — existence via extreme value theorem.</li><li><code>csiszar_projection_unique</code> — uniqueness via strict convexity.</li><li><code>csiszar_pythagoras_inequality</code> — Pythagorean inequality via the first-order condition.</li></ul><h2 id=\"Implementation-notes\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Implementation notes <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Implementation-notes\">#</a></h2><p>Proof strategy for the Pythagorean inequality: the first-order condition\x0a<code>∑ (P - Q*)(log Q* - log Q) ≥ 0</code> is derived from the right derivative of\x0a<code>t ↦ klDivPmf ((1-t)Q* + tP) Q</code> at <code>t = 0</code> being non-negative (minimality of <code>Q*</code>).\x0aCombined with the algebraic identity\x0a<code>klDivPmf P Q = klDivPmf P Q* + ∑ P·(log Q* - log Q)</code> and the expansion of\x0a<code>klDivPmf Q* Q</code>, this gives the inequality.</p><h2 id=\"References\" class=\"markdown-heading\">References <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#References\">#</a></h2><ul><li>T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, <em>Elements of Information Theory</em> (2nd ed.), Wiley, 2006.\x0aTheorem 11.6.1.</li></ul>"),
