  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPICase1RatioLimit.isRescaledPathRegular_of_methodX", "../.././",
   "Discharge `IsRescaledPathRegular` from method-X regularity.\x0a\x0aGiven a Gaussian noise `B` (`P.map B = gaussianReal 0 v_B`, `v_B ≠ 0`) independent of\x0athe input `A` (`hAB : IndepFun A B P`), with `A` measurable + finite-second-moment\x0adata threaded as `varA`-regularity, construct the per-`t` regularity bundle\x0a`IsRescaledPathRegular A B P varA v_B`.\x0a\x0aThe key insight: the fibre of\x0a`condDistrib (B + A/√t) (A/√t) P` is the translated Gaussian `gaussianReal z v_B` (the\x0alaw of `B + z` by `affineShiftKernel`/Gaussian translation). This avoids the\x0adensity-witness obstruction for the general fibre: the fibre identification\x0a`condDistrib (B + A/√t) (A/√t) P =ᵐ affineShiftKernel (P.map B) 1` (`h_fibre_ae`) and\x0athe per-fibre a.c. `condDistrib z ≪ volume` (`hκ_v`, via `gaussianReal z v_B`) are both\x0aclosed — exactly the conjuncts that are intractable in the general case.\x0a\x0aPreconditions only (NOT load-bearing): measurability, `IndepFun A B P`, the\x0aGaussian noise law, finite-second-moment `h_mom_A` + `varA`-regularity (`h_var_bound`).\x0aThe bundle being constructed is itself regularity (audited non-load-bearing at its def\x0asite §3).\x0a\x0aAll 9 integrability conjuncts are supplied. The 3 conditional-KL integrabilities are\x0asupplied via the extracted standalone lemmas in `EPI/G2/ConvEntropyDensity.lean`\x0a(`convCrossEntropy_perFibre_integrable` / `convCrossEntropy_zAvg_integrable` /\x0a`convJointLlr_integrable`), instantiated here with the\x0aGaussian fibre `q := gaussianPDFReal 0 v_B` (translated by `z`) and the target\x0aconvolution density `g := convDensityAdd pX g_{v_B}`. No signature change was needed:\x0abecause the fibre is Gaussian (not the input density), the joint-llr branch (b)\x0aabs-entropy `∫ q·|log q|` is the Gaussian self-entropy (finite via\x0a`integrable_density_log_density_of_gaussian`), so the inventory's suspected `hpX_ent`\x0ainput-density-entropy precondition is not required (the `X`/`Z` roles are swapped vs.\x0athe density template, where the fibre is the input). All preconditions:\x0a`hA_ac : P.map A ≪ volume` (case-1 a.c. input, NOT load-bearing — consumed only for the\x0adensity witness and `P.map (A/√t) ≪ volume`), `h_mom_A` (finite second moment, feeds the\x0aGaussian-fibre moment domination), the Gaussian noise law, `h_var_bound`.\x0a\x0a- The regularity conjuncts (closed here): `IndepFun B (A/√t)` (`h_indep`), a.c. of `B + A/√t`\x0a  and `A/√t + B` (`hW_ac`/`hμ_ac`), the fibre identification `h_fibre_ae` + per-fibre a.c.\x0a  `hκ_v`, the variance bound (threaded `h_var_bound`), joint-≪-product, the fibre/path\x0a  self-entropy + log-density integrabilities, the squared-deviation, and the **3\x0a  cross-entropy conjuncts** (per-z cross integrand, z-averaged cross-term, joint llr).\x0a- The cross-entropy analytic core (`condDifferentialEntropy_le`'s\x0a  `h_int`/`hκ_cross_int`/`h_cross_int`): integrability of the path-density `log g` against\x0a  each Gaussian fibre, dominated by the `convDensityAdd_logFactor_poly_majorant`\x0a  `|log g| ≤ (A+1)+B·x²` and the Gaussian-fibre quadratic moments.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "<p>Discharge <code>IsRescaledPathRegular</code> from method-X regularity.</p><p>Given a Gaussian noise <code>B</code> (<code>P.map B = gaussianReal 0 v_B</code>, <code>v_B ≠ 0</code>) independent of\x0athe input <code>A</code> (<code>hAB : IndepFun A B P</code>), with <code>A</code> measurable + finite-second-moment\x0adata threaded as <code>varA</code>-regularity, construct the per-<code>t</code> regularity bundle\x0a<code>IsRescaledPathRegular A B P varA v_B</code>.</p><p>The key insight: the fibre of\x0a<code>condDistrib (B + A/√t) (A/√t) P</code> is the translated Gaussian <code>gaussianReal z v_B</code> (the\x0alaw of <code>B + z</code> by <code>affineShiftKernel</code>/Gaussian translation). This avoids the\x0adensity-witness obstruction for the general fibre: the fibre identification\x0a<code>condDistrib (B + A/√t) (A/√t) P =ᵐ affineShiftKernel (P.map B) 1</code> (<code>h_fibre_ae</code>) and\x0athe per-fibre a.c. <code>condDistrib z ≪ volume</code> (<code>hκ_v</code>, via <code>gaussianReal z v_B</code>) are both\x0aclosed — exactly the conjuncts that are intractable in the general case.</p><p>Preconditions only (NOT load-bearing): measurability, <code>IndepFun A B P</code>, the\x0aGaussian noise law, finite-second-moment <code>h_mom_A</code> + <code>varA</code>-regularity (<code>h_var_bound</code>).\x0aThe bundle being constructed is itself regularity (audited non-load-bearing at its def\x0asite §3).</p><p>All 9 integrability conjuncts are supplied. The 3 conditional-KL integrabilities are\x0asupplied via the extracted standalone lemmas in <code><a href=\"../.././EPI/G2/ConvEntropyDensity.html\">EPI/G2/ConvEntropyDensity.lean</a></code>\x0a(<code>convCrossEntropy_perFibre_integrable</code> / <code>convCrossEntropy_zAvg_integrable</code> /\x0a<code>convJointLlr_integrable</code>), instantiated here with the\x0aGaussian fibre <code>q := gaussianPDFReal 0 v_B</code> (translated by <code>z</code>) and the target\x0aconvolution density <code>g := convDensityAdd pX g_{v_B}</code>. No signature change was needed:\x0abecause the fibre is Gaussian (not the input density), the joint-llr branch (b)\x0aabs-entropy <code>∫ q·|log q|</code> is the Gaussian self-entropy (finite via\x0a<code>integrable_density_log_density_of_gaussian</code>), so the inventory's suspected <code>hpX_ent</code>\x0ainput-density-entropy precondition is not required (the <code>X</code>/<code>Z</code> roles are swapped vs.\x0athe density template, where the fibre is the input). All preconditions:\x0a<code>hA_ac : P.map A ≪ volume</code> (case-1 a.c. input, NOT load-bearing — consumed only for the\x0adensity witness and <code>P.map (A/√t) ≪ volume</code>), <code>h_mom_A</code> (finite second moment, feeds the\x0aGaussian-fibre moment domination), the Gaussian noise law, <code>h_var_bound</code>.</p><ul><li>The regularity conjuncts (closed here): <code>IndepFun B (A/√t)</code> (<code>h_indep</code>), a.c. of <code>B + A/√t</code>\x0aand <code>A/√t + B</code> (<code>hW_ac</code>/<code>hμ_ac</code>), the fibre identification <code>h_fibre_ae</code> + per-fibre a.c.\x0a<code>hκ_v</code>, the variance bound (threaded <code>h_var_bound</code>), joint-≪-product, the fibre/path\x0aself-entropy + log-density integrabilities, the squared-deviation, and the <strong>3\x0across-entropy conjuncts</strong> (per-z cross integrand, z-averaged cross-term, joint llr).</li><li>The cross-entropy analytic core (<code>condDifferentialEntropy_le</code>'s\x0a<code>h_int</code>/<code>hκ_cross_int</code>/<code>h_cross_int</code>): integrability of the path-density <code>log g</code> against\x0aeach Gaussian fibre, dominated by the <code>convDensityAdd_logFactor_poly_majorant</code>\x0a<code>|log g| ≤ (A+1)+B·x²</code> and the Gaussian-fibre quadratic moments.\x0a@audit:ok</li></ul>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPICase1TwoTime.IsMatchedTimePath.cont", "./",
   "The path is continuous on `[0, ∞)`. ",
   "<p>The path is continuous on <code>[0, ∞)</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPI.Conv.Density module doc 0", ".././",
   "# Convolution density apparatus\x0a\x0a`p_Z(z) = ∫ x, p_X(x) · p_Y(z - x) ∂volume` (sum density of independent `X, Y`),\x0aits pointwise differentiability, and the `logDeriv p_Z` representation. This is\x0athe common foundational helper for the density-route Stam and de Bruijn arguments.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aThe 6 Mathlib `HasCompactSupport.*_convolution_*` lemmas require the smooth factor\x0ato have compact support, which the Gaussian heat kernel does not have. We go\x0athrough `hasDerivAt_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_deriv_le`\x0a(`Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/ParametricIntegral.lean`): differentiation under the\x0aintegral sign, with the Gaussian-tail domination supplied as regularity\x0apreconditions.\x0a\x0a`convDensityAdd` is defined as a Bochner `∫` (not `⋆ₗ` / `⋆[L,μ]`), matching the\x0aconclusion shape of the parametric-integral gateway\x0a`HasDerivAt (fun z ↦ ∫ a, F z a ∂μ) (∫ a, F' x₀ a ∂μ) x₀`.\x0a",
   "<h1 id=\"Convolution-density-apparatus\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Convolution density apparatus <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Convolution-density-apparatus\">#</a></h1><p><code>p_Z(z) = ∫ x, p_X(x) · p_Y(z - x) ∂volume</code> (sum density of independent <code>X, Y</code>),\x0aits pointwise differentiability, and the <code>logDeriv p_Z</code> representation. This is\x0athe common foundational helper for the density-route Stam and de Bruijn arguments.</p><h2 id=\"Implementation-notes\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Implementation notes <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Implementation-notes\">#</a></h2><p>The 6 Mathlib <code>HasCompactSupport.*_convolution_*</code> lemmas require the smooth factor\x0ato have compact support, which the Gaussian heat kernel does not have. We go\x0athrough <code>hasDerivAt_integral_of_dominated_loc_of_deriv_le</code>\x0a(<code><a href=\".././Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/ParametricIntegral.html\">Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/ParametricIntegral.lean</a></code>): differentiation under the\x0aintegral sign, with the Gaussian-tail domination supplied as regularity\x0apreconditions.</p><p><code>convDensityAdd</code> is defined as a Bochner <code>∫</code> (not <code>⋆ₗ</code> / <code>⋆[L,μ]</code>), matching the\x0aconclusion shape of the parametric-integral gateway\x0a<code>HasDerivAt (fun z ↦ ∫ a, F z a ∂μ) (∫ a, F' x₀ a ∂μ) x₀</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPI.Conv.DensityNormalization module doc 0", "../.././",
   "# Normalization of the convolution density (EPI A-5 precondition (2))\x0a\x0a`∫ z, convDensityAdd pX g_t z ∂volume = 1` when `pX` is a normalized probability\x0adensity and `g_t = gaussianPDFReal 0 ⟨t, _⟩` is a Gaussian heat kernel (`t > 0`).\x0a\x0a## Route\x0a\x0a`convDensityAdd pX g z = ∫ x, pX x * g (z - x) = (pX ⋆[ContinuousLinearMap.mul ℝ ℝ, volume] g) z`\x0a(definitional match: `(mul ℝ ℝ) a b = a * b`). We then apply\x0a`MeasureTheory.integral_convolution`, which gives\x0a`∫ z, (pX ⋆[L,ν] g) z = L (∫ pX) (∫ g) = (∫ pX) * (∫ g) = 1 * 1 = 1`.\x0a\x0a- `∫ pX = 1` from `hpX_norm`.\x0a- `∫ g = 1` from `ProbabilityTheory.integral_gaussianPDFReal_eq_one`.\x0a- Gaussian integrability `Integrable g` from `ProbabilityTheory.integrable_gaussianPDFReal`.\x0a",
   "<h1 id=\"Normalization-of-the-convolution-density-EPI-A-5-precondition-2\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Normalization of the convolution density (EPI A-5 precondition (2)) <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Normalization-of-the-convolution-density-EPI-A-5-precondition-2\">#</a></h1><p><code>∫ z, convDensityAdd pX g_t z ∂volume = 1</code> when <code>pX</code> is a normalized probability\x0adensity and <code>g_t = gaussianPDFReal 0 ⟨t, _⟩</code> is a Gaussian heat kernel (<code>t &gt; 0</code>).</p><h2 id=\"Route\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Route <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Route\">#</a></h2><p><code>convDensityAdd pX g z = ∫ x, pX x * g (z - x) = (pX ⋆[ContinuousLinearMap.mul ℝ ℝ, volume] g) z</code>\x0a(definitional match: <code>(mul ℝ ℝ) a b = a * b</code>). We then apply\x0a<code>MeasureTheory.integral_convolution</code>, which gives\x0a<code>∫ z, (pX ⋆[L,ν] g) z = L (∫ pX) (∫ g) = (∫ pX) * (∫ g) = 1 * 1 = 1</code>.</p><ul><li><code>∫ pX = 1</code> from <code>hpX_norm</code>.</li><li><code>∫ g = 1</code> from <code>ProbabilityTheory.integral_gaussianPDFReal_eq_one</code>.</li><li>Gaussian integrability <code>Integrable g</code> from <code>ProbabilityTheory.integrable_gaussianPDFReal</code>.</li></ul>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPI.G2.ConvEntropyDensity module doc 0", "./",
   "# EPI G2 — (β) density-only lower bound\x0a\x0aThis file packages the Ω-level (β) lower bound\x0a`negMulLog_convDensity_entropy_ge` (`EPI/G2/ConvEntropyMonotone.lean`) into a\x0adensity-only wrapper: given just a probability density `pX` (plus minimal\x0aregularity), no abstract independent pair is required.\x0a\x0a  `∫ negMulLog pX ≤ ∫ negMulLog (pX ∗ g_{u n})`.\x0a\x0aThe Ω-level theorem requires an independent pair `X ⊥ Z` (with `Z ∼ 𝒩(0, v_Z)`) on\x0asome probability space together with 8 per-`n` regularity/integrability preconditions.\x0aWe instantiate the canonical product space `Ω := ℝ × ℝ`,\x0a`μ := (volume.withDensity (ofReal ∘ pX)).prod (gaussianReal 0 v_Z)`,\x0a`X := Prod.fst`, `Z := Prod.snd`. Then `X ⊥ Z` (product independence),\x0a`μ.map X = withDensity pX`, `μ.map Z = gaussianReal 0 v_Z`, and the 8 preconditions are\x0adischarged here.\x0a\x0a## Status — proof done (0 sorry / 0 residual)\x0a\x0aAll 8 per-`n` preconditions of the Ω-level (β) lower bound are discharged here\x0afrom the canonical construction:\x0a\x0a* per-fiber absolute continuity, `p log p` integrability, fiber-entropy integrability\x0a  (translation invariance: each fiber is a translate `pX(· − √s·z)` of `μ.map X`);\x0a* joint absolute continuity (per-fiber `≪ volume ≪ μ.map W`, the marginal having a\x0a  strictly positive density);\x0a* the two cross terms (per-fiber (5) + outer (7)): closed via the `s`-uniform\x0a  polynomial majorant `|log p_t| ≤ A + B·x²`\x0a  (`convDensityAdd_logFactor_poly_majorant`, made public in\x0a  `FisherInfoDeBruijnAssembly`) integrated against `pX`'s translate moments\x0a  (the standalone `convCrossEntropy_perFibre_integrable` / `convCrossEntropy_zAvg_integrable`,\x0a  fed the a.e. identifications `hLog` / `hfib_eq` in the proof body);\x0a* marginal log-density integrability (`∫ negMulLog p_t < ∞`, the\x0a  `convDensityAdd_negMulLog_integrable`);\x0a* joint llr integrability `h_int` (= KL finiteness `D(joint ‖ product) < ∞`): closed\x0a  via `MeasureTheory.Measure.integrable_compProd_iff`.  The slice identity\x0a  `rnDeriv_compProd_eq_kernel_rnDeriv` + `Kernel.rnDeriv_eq_rnDeriv_measure` identify the\x0a  joint `llr` a.e. with the per-fiber `llr (κ_z) (μ.map W)`, which the density split\x0a  `llr_eq_log_density_sub_log_density` rewrites as `log p_z − log p_t`.  The per-fiber\x0a  branch reuses the fiber-entropy + cross-term integrabilities (via\x0a  `integrable_toReal_rnDeriv_mul_iff`); the outer branch dominates\x0a  `∫ ‖log p_z − log p_t‖ ∂κ_z` by `C0 + (A+1) + 2B·M2 + 2B·s·z²` (Gaussian-integrable),\x0a  using `∫ pX·|log pX| < ∞` (from `Integrable f ↔ Integrable ‖f‖` on `hpX_ent`) plus the\x0a  `s`-uniform majorant.\x0a\x0a`#print axioms negMulLog_convDensity_entropy_ge_density` = `[propext, Classical.choice,\x0aQuot.sound]` (sorryAx-free).  This completes the EPI G2 (β) density-only lower bound.\x0a",
   "<h1 id=\"EPI-G2-β-density-only-lower-bound\" class=\"markdown-heading\">EPI G2 — (β) density-only lower bound <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#EPI-G2-β-density-only-lower-bound\">#</a></h1><p>This file packages the Ω-level (β) lower bound\x0a<code>negMulLog_convDensity_entropy_ge</code> (<code><a href=\"./EPI/G2/ConvEntropyMonotone.html\">EPI/G2/ConvEntropyMonotone.lean</a></code>) into a\x0adensity-only wrapper: given just a probability density <code>pX</code> (plus minimal\x0aregularity), no abstract independent pair is required.</p><p><code>∫ negMulLog pX ≤ ∫ negMulLog (pX ∗ g_{u n})</code>.</p><p>The Ω-level theorem requires an independent pair <code>X ⊥ Z</code> (with <code>Z ∼ 𝒩(0, v_Z)</code>) on\x0asome probability space together with 8 per-<code>n</code> regularity/integrability preconditions.\x0aWe instantiate the canonical product space <code>Ω := ℝ × ℝ</code>,\x0a<code>μ := (volume.withDensity (ofReal ∘ pX)).prod (gaussianReal 0 v_Z)</code>,\x0a<code>X := Prod.fst</code>, <code>Z := Prod.snd</code>. Then <code>X ⊥ Z</code> (product independence),\x0a<code>μ.map X = withDensity pX</code>, <code>μ.map Z = gaussianReal 0 v_Z</code>, and the 8 preconditions are\x0adischarged here.</p><h2 id=\"Status-proof-done-0-sorry-0-residual\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Status — proof done (0 sorry / 0 residual) <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Status-proof-done-0-sorry-0-residual\">#</a></h2><p>All 8 per-<code>n</code> preconditions of the Ω-level (β) lower bound are discharged here\x0afrom the canonical construction:</p><ul><li>per-fiber absolute continuity, <code>p log p</code> integrability, fiber-entropy integrability\x0a(translation invariance: each fiber is a translate <code>pX(· − √s·z)</code> of <code>μ.map X</code>);</li><li>joint absolute continuity (per-fiber <code>≪ volume ≪ μ.map W</code>, the marginal having a\x0astrictly positive density);</li><li>the two cross terms (per-fiber (5) + outer (7)): closed via the <code>s</code>-uniform\x0apolynomial majorant <code>|log p_t| ≤ A + B·x²</code>\x0a(<code>convDensityAdd_logFactor_poly_majorant</code>, made public in\x0a<code>FisherInfoDeBruijnAssembly</code>) integrated against <code>pX</code>'s translate moments\x0a(the standalone <code>convCrossEntropy_perFibre_integrable</code> / <code>convCrossEntropy_zAvg_integrable</code>,\x0afed the a.e. identifications <code>hLog</code> / <code>hfib_eq</code> in the proof body);</li><li>marginal log-density integrability (<code>∫ negMulLog p_t &lt; ∞</code>, the\x0a<code>convDensityAdd_negMulLog_integrable</code>);</li><li>joint llr integrability <code>h_int</code> (= KL finiteness <code>D(joint ‖ product) &lt; ∞</code>): closed\x0avia <code>MeasureTheory.Measure.integrable_compProd_iff</code>.  The slice identity\x0a<code>rnDeriv_compProd_eq_kernel_rnDeriv</code> + <code>Kernel.rnDeriv_eq_rnDeriv_measure</code> identify the\x0ajoint <code>llr</code> a.e. with the per-fiber <code>llr (κ_z) (μ.map W)</code>, which the density split\x0a<code>llr_eq_log_density_sub_log_density</code> rewrites as <code>log p_z − log p_t</code>.  The per-fiber\x0abranch reuses the fiber-entropy + cross-term integrabilities (via\x0a<code>integrable_toReal_rnDeriv_mul_iff</code>); the outer branch dominates\x0a<code>∫ ‖log p_z − log p_t‖ ∂κ_z</code> by <code>C0 + (A+1) + 2B·M2 + 2B·s·z²</code> (Gaussian-integrable),\x0ausing <code>∫ pX·|log pX| &lt; ∞</code> (from <code>Integrable f ↔ Integrable ‖f‖</code> on <code>hpX_ent</code>) plus the\x0a<code>s</code>-uniform majorant.</li></ul><p><code>#print axioms negMulLog_convDensity_entropy_ge_density</code> = <code>[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]</code> (sorryAx-free).  This completes the EPI G2 (β) density-only lower bound.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.convDensityAdd_negMulLog_integrable_pub", ".././",
   "Per-time entropy-integrand integrability.\x0aFor each `t > 0`, `negMulLog (convDensityAdd pX g_t)` is `volume`-integrable.\x0a\x0aDelegates verbatim to the in-tree asset\x0a`FisherInfo.convDensityAdd_negMulLog_integrable` (same conclusion type); pure\x0aplumbing, no new analytic content.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "<p>Per-time entropy-integrand integrability.\x0aFor each <code>t &gt; 0</code>, <code>negMulLog (convDensityAdd pX g_t)</code> is <code>volume</code>-integrable.</p><p>Delegates verbatim to the in-tree asset\x0a<code>FisherInfo.convDensityAdd_negMulLog_integrable</code> (same conclusion type); pure\x0aplumbing, no new analytic content.\x0a@audit:ok</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPIInfiniteVarianceTruncation.rnDeriv_map_condTrunc_sum_ae", "../.././",
   "The conditioned sum density is the convolution of the conditioned marginal densities: the\x0arnDeriv of the law of `X + Y` under `condTrunc P X Y n` equals\x0a`convDensityAdd p_n q_n` a.e., where `p_n := (condTrunc.map X).rnDeriv volume |>.toReal` and\x0a`q_n := (condTrunc.map Y).rnDeriv volume |>.toReal`. Obtained by applying `indepSum_density_ae`\x0awith `condTrunc P X Y n` in place of `P` (independence from `indepFun_condTrunc`, absolute\x0acontinuity from `map_condTrunc_absolutelyContinuous`).\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "<p>The conditioned sum density is the convolution of the conditioned marginal densities: the\x0arnDeriv of the law of <code>X + Y</code> under <code>condTrunc P X Y n</code> equals\x0a<code>convDensityAdd p_n q_n</code> a.e., where <code>p_n := (condTrunc.map X).rnDeriv volume |&gt;.toReal</code> and\x0a<code>q_n := (condTrunc.map Y).rnDeriv volume |&gt;.toReal</code>. Obtained by applying <code>indepSum_density_ae</code>\x0awith <code>condTrunc P X Y n</code> in place of <code>P</code> (independence from <code>indepFun_condTrunc</code>, absolute\x0acontinuity from <code>map_condTrunc_absolutelyContinuous</code>).\x0a@audit:ok</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPI.L3Integration module doc 1", "./",
   "## Integrated pipeline predicate ",
   "<h2 id=\"Integrated-pipeline-predicate\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Integrated pipeline predicate <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Integrated-pipeline-predicate\">#</a></h2>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPIL3Integration.IsDeBruijnTailHyp.h_inf", ".././",
   "The asymptotic value of the heat-flow entropy; EReal-valued to allow\x0adivergent (`⊤`) limits. ",
   "<p>The asymptotic value of the heat-flow entropy; EReal-valued to allow\x0adivergent (<code>⊤</code>) limits.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EntropyPowerInequality.entropyPower_map_mul_const", "../.././",
   "`entropyPower (μ.map (· * c)) = |c|² · entropyPower μ`. ",
   "<p><code>entropyPower (μ.map (· * c)) = |c|² · entropyPower μ</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.StamConditionalCauchySchwarz.stam_jensen_sq_le", "./",
   "Two-point Jensen `(E)² ≤ E(²)` for a convex combination.\x0a\x0aFor weights `λ, 1-λ ≥ 0` summing to `1` and values `u, v`,\x0a`(λ u + (1-λ) v)² ≤ λ u² + (1-λ) v²`. Identical content to `stam_convex_cs` but\x0aphrased as the conditional-Jensen squared-mean inequality consumed in Step 2. ",
