  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.FisherInfo.fisherInfoOfDensity", "./",
   "The Fisher information of a density `f : ℝ → ℝ`, defined as\x0a`∫⁻ (logDeriv f x)² · f x dx` with `logDeriv f := deriv f / f` Mathlib's score function.\x0aValued in `ℝ≥0∞` to capture `+∞` for irregular families; use `fisherInfoOfDensityReal` or\x0a`.toReal` to project to `ℝ` when finite. ",
   "<p>The Fisher information of a density <code>f : ℝ → ℝ</code>, defined as\x0a<code>∫⁻ (logDeriv f x)² · f x dx</code> with <code>logDeriv f := deriv f / f</code> Mathlib's score function.\x0aValued in <code>ℝ≥0∞</code> to capture <code>+∞</code> for irregular families; use <code>fisherInfoOfDensityReal</code> or\x0a<code>.toReal</code> to project to <code>ℝ</code> when finite.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Gambling.sideInfoMutualInfo", ".././",
   "The mutual information `I(X; Y)` in symmetric pmf form\x0a`I(X; Y) = H(X) + H(Y) − H(X, Y)`, where the entropies are the finite-alphabet Shannon\x0aentropies of the marginals and the joint.\x0aThe symmetric form carries the joint entropy\x0a`H(X, Y)` as an independent term, so it is not crafted to match the doubling-rate increment\x0a`H(X) − H(X|Y)`; recognizing it as that increment forces a detour through the\x0achain-rule bridge (`sideInfoJointEntropy_eq_chain`). Not trivial-circular.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "<p>The mutual information <code>I(X; Y)</code> in symmetric pmf form\x0a<code>I(X; Y) = H(X) + H(Y) − H(X, Y)</code>, where the entropies are the finite-alphabet Shannon\x0aentropies of the marginals and the joint.\x0aThe symmetric form carries the joint entropy\x0a<code>H(X, Y)</code> as an independent term, so it is not crafted to match the doubling-rate increment\x0a<code>H(X) − H(X|Y)</code>; recognizing it as that increment forces a detour through the\x0achain-rule bridge (<code>sideInfoJointEntropy_eq_chain</code>). Not trivial-circular.\x0a@audit:ok</p>"),
