   "<h2 id=\"IsBoundedUnder-≤-rate-bounded-above\" class=\"markdown-heading\"><code>IsBoundedUnder (· ≤ ·)</code>: rate bounded above <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#IsBoundedUnder-≤-rate-bounded-above\">#</a></h2>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Hoeffding.Tradeoff module doc 0", "./",
   "# Hoeffding tradeoff exponent — scaffolding and variational form\x0a\x0aScaffolding towards Cover-Thomas Theorem 11.7.x:\x0a\x0a```\x0a-(1/n) log β_n(alpha) → hoeffdingE2 P₁ P₂ alpha\x0a```\x0a\x0a`hoeffdingE2`, `hoeffdingE2_attained`, and `hoeffdingE2_unique` are published in\x0a`InformationTheory/Shannon/Chernoff/Basic.lean`. This file adds the pmf-form infrastructure\x0aand the Pythagoras-based minimizer bound.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `pmfToMeasure` — lift a pmf vector to `Measure α` via `PMF.ofFintype`.\x0a* `steinBetaSet_pmf` — set of achievable Type II errors at Type I level `alpha` (pmf form).\x0a* `steinTypeII_at_level_pmf` — optimal Type II error (pmf form).\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `hoeffdingConstraintSet_convex` — the Hoeffding constraint set is convex.\x0a* `hoeffding_minimizer_ge` — Csiszar Pythagoras gives `klDivPmf Qstar P₂ ≤ klDivPmf P P₂`\x0a  for any `P ∈ K` with full support, when `Qstar` is the minimizer.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0a* This file provides the variational scaffolding; the full sandwich `Tendsto`\x0a  (achievability from Sanov LDP + converse from Stein typicality) is in\x0a  `Hoeffding/TradeoffExp.lean`.\x0a* The pmf ↔ Measure bridge uses `PMF.ofFintype` + `PMF.toMeasure` (~4 lemmas).\x0a",
   "<h1 id=\"Hoeffding-tradeoff-exponent-scaffolding-and-variational-form\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Hoeffding tradeoff exponent — scaffolding and variational form <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Hoeffding-tradeoff-exponent-scaffolding-and-variational-form\">#</a></h1><p>Scaffolding towards Cover-Thomas Theorem 11.7.x:</p><pre><code>-(1/n) log β_n(alpha) → hoeffdingE2 P₁ P₂ alpha\x0a</code></pre><p><code>hoeffdingE2</code>, <code>hoeffdingE2_attained</code>, and <code>hoeffdingE2_unique</code> are published in\x0a<code><a href=\"./InformationTheory/Shannon/Chernoff/Basic.html\">InformationTheory/Shannon/Chernoff/Basic.lean</a></code>. This file adds the pmf-form infrastructure\x0aand the Pythagoras-based minimizer bound.</p><h2 id=\"Main-definitions\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Main definitions <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Main-definitions\">#</a></h2><ul><li><code>pmfToMeasure</code> — lift a pmf vector to <code>Measure α</code> via <code>PMF.ofFintype</code>.</li><li><code>steinBetaSet_pmf</code> — set of achievable Type II errors at Type I level <code>alpha</code> (pmf form).</li><li><code>steinTypeII_at_level_pmf</code> — optimal Type II error (pmf form).</li></ul><h2 id=\"Main-statements\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Main statements <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Main-statements\">#</a></h2><ul><li><code>hoeffdingConstraintSet_convex</code> — the Hoeffding constraint set is convex.</li><li><code>hoeffding_minimizer_ge</code> — Csiszar Pythagoras gives <code>klDivPmf Qstar P₂ ≤ klDivPmf P P₂</code>\x0afor any <code>P ∈ K</code> with full support, when <code>Qstar</code> is the minimizer.</li></ul><h2 id=\"Implementation-notes\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Implementation notes <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Implementation-notes\">#</a></h2><ul><li>This file provides the variational scaffolding; the full sandwich <code>Tendsto</code>\x0a(achievability from Sanov LDP + converse from Stein typicality) is in\x0a<code><a href=\"./Hoeffding/TradeoffExp.html\">Hoeffding/TradeoffExp.lean</a></code>.</li><li>The pmf ↔ Measure bridge uses <code>PMF.ofFintype</code> + <code>PMF.toMeasure</code> (~4 lemmas).</li></ul>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.HoeffdingTradeoffExp.klDivPmf_eq_log_diff_sum_of_Q_pos", ".././",
   "`klDivPmf` log-diff form tolerant of count-0 atoms in `P`: requires only\x0a`Q` full support (and both sum to 1), not `P` full support. The `P a = 0` term\x0amatches on both sides (`Q a` vs `0 + Q a - 0`). ",
   "<p><code>klDivPmf</code> log-diff form tolerant of count-0 atoms in <code>P</code>: requires only\x0a<code>Q</code> full support (and both sum to 1), not <code>P</code> full support. The <code>P a = 0</code> term\x0amatches on both sides (<code>Q a</code> vs <code>0 + Q a - 0</code>).</p>"),
