  ("InformationTheory.Kolmogorov.universalProb_le_one", "./",
   "The universal probability is a subprobability: `P_U(x) ≤ 1`, because every\x0afinite subsum is a Kraft sum of valid self-delimiting programs.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "<p>The universal probability is a subprobability: <code>P_U(x) ≤ 1</code>, because every\x0afinite subsum is a Kraft sum of valid self-delimiting programs.\x0a@audit:ok</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.mul_log_succ_le", ".././",
   "`(c : ℝ) * Real.log (c + 1) ≤ (c : ℝ) * Real.log 2 + (c : ℝ) * Real.log c`:\x0athe per-phrase `+1`-shift slack, from `Real.log (c + 1) ≤ Real.log 2 + Real.log c`\x0a(via `Real.log (c + 1) ≤ Real.log (2 * c)` for `c ≥ 1`; trivial for `c = 0`). ",
   "<p><code>(c : ℝ) * Real.log (c + 1) ≤ (c : ℝ) * Real.log 2 + (c : ℝ) * Real.log c</code>:\x0athe per-phrase <code>+1</code>-shift slack, from <code>Real.log (c + 1) ≤ Real.log 2 + Real.log c</code>\x0a(via <code>Real.log (c + 1) ≤ Real.log (2 * c)</code> for <code>c ≥ 1</code>; trivial for <code>c = 0</code>).</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.factorial_two_pow_le_succ_pow", "../.././",
   "Factorial-power decay `c! · 2^c ≤ (c+1)^c` (real form). The per-`c`\x0astructure-Kraft term `c!/(c+1)^c` is geometrically small. Proved by induction;\x0athe step uses Bernoulli `2·(c+1)^(c+1) ≤ (c+2)^(c+1)`. ",
   "<p>Factorial-power decay <code>c! · 2^c ≤ (c+1)^c</code> (real form). The per-<code>c</code>\x0astructure-Kraft term <code>c!/(c+1)^c</code> is geometrically small. Proved by induction;\x0athe step uses Bernoulli <code>2·(c+1)^(c+1) ≤ (c+2)^(c+1)</code>.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.LZ78.ConverseAsymptotic module doc 3", "./",
