  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.jointEntropySubset_disjoint_union", "./",
   "Disjoint-union pair chain rule. If `s ∪ t = U` and `Disjoint s t`, then\x0a`H(X_U) = H(X_s) + H(X_t | X_s)`.\x0a\x0aProof: build `e : ((↥s → α) × (↥t → α)) ≃ᵐ (↥U → α)` directly from\x0a`subsetSplitMEquivAux` (Mathlib `MeasurableEquiv.piFinsetUnion` + cast), then apply\x0athe pair chain rule. ",
   "<p>Disjoint-union pair chain rule. If <code>s ∪ t = U</code> and <code>Disjoint s t</code>, then\x0a<code>H(X_U) = H(X_s) + H(X_t | X_s)</code>.</p><p>Proof: build <code>e : ((↥s → α) × (↥t → α)) ≃ᵐ (↥U → α)</code> directly from\x0a<code>subsetSplitMEquivAux</code> (Mathlib <code>MeasurableEquiv.piFinsetUnion</code> + cast), then apply\x0athe pair chain rule.</p>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Portfolio.StationaryWinfty module doc 0", ".././",
   "# Measurable selection of a log-optimal portfolio (Cover–Thomas §16.5)\x0a\x0aGateway lemma for the stationary-market `W_∞` AEP (Theorem 16.5.1): a concave Carathéodory\x0aobjective (measurable in the sample point, continuous and concave in the portfolio) admits a\x0ameasurable selection of an argmax over the standard simplex. This is a measurable-maximum\x0atheorem. Mathlib has no ready measurable-selection lemma (see\x0a`Mathlib/Probability/Decision/BayesEstimator.lean`, which notes selection theorems are not yet\x0ain Mathlib), so the selector is self-built by strictly-concave (Tikhonov) regularization: for\x0aeach `ε > 0` the perturbed objective `F ω · − ε ‖·‖²` has a unique maximizer `bEps ε ω`, which\x0ais measurable as a limit of finite near-maximizers; letting `ε → 0` gives a measurable genuine\x0amaximizer of `F ω` (the point of the argmax set nearest the origin).\x0a\x0a## References\x0a\x0a* T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, *Elements of Information Theory* (2nd ed.), Wiley, 2006.\x0a  §16.5.\x0a",
   "<h1 id=\"Measurable-selection-of-a-log-optimal-portfolio-Cover-Thomas-16-5\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Measurable selection of a log-optimal portfolio (Cover–Thomas §16.5) <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Measurable-selection-of-a-log-optimal-portfolio-Cover-Thomas-16-5\">#</a></h1><p>Gateway lemma for the stationary-market <code>W_∞</code> AEP (Theorem 16.5.1): a concave Carathéodory\x0aobjective (measurable in the sample point, continuous and concave in the portfolio) admits a\x0ameasurable selection of an argmax over the standard simplex. This is a measurable-maximum\x0atheorem. Mathlib has no ready measurable-selection lemma (see\x0a<code><a href=\".././Mathlib/Probability/Decision/BayesEstimator.html\">Mathlib/Probability/Decision/BayesEstimator.lean</a></code>, which notes selection theorems are not yet\x0ain Mathlib), so the selector is self-built by strictly-concave (Tikhonov) regularization: for\x0aeach <code>ε &gt; 0</code> the perturbed objective <code>F ω · − ε ‖·‖²</code> has a unique maximizer <code>bEps ε ω</code>, which\x0ais measurable as a limit of finite near-maximizers; letting <code>ε → 0</code> gives a measurable genuine\x0amaximizer of <code>F ω</code> (the point of the argmax set nearest the origin).</p><h2 id=\"References\" class=\"markdown-heading\">References <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#References\">#</a></h2><ul><li>T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, <em>Elements of Information Theory</em> (2nd ed.), Wiley, 2006.\x0a§16.5.</li></ul>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Portfolio.growingMemory_logWealth_tendsto_condOptGrowthInfty_concrete", "../.././",
   "Growing-memory `W_∞` AEP (Cover–Thomas Theorem 16.5.1) for the concrete two-sided market: the\x0agrowing-memory log-wealth average converges almost surely to the infinite-past optimal growth rate\x0a`W_∞ = condOptGrowthInfty`. The sequence space is `Ω = ∀ _ : ℤ, Fin m → ℝ`, the dynamics is the\x0atwo-sided shift `shiftZ`, the per-epoch price relative is the coordinate-0 projection `coord0`, and\x0athe filtration is the finite-past `pastFiltration`. The two shift/past coherences of the abstract\x0astatement are discharged internally; all remaining hypotheses are market-regularity/ergodicity\x0apreconditions (measure preservation, ergodicity, simplex membership, positivity, integrability,\x0aconditional dominance).\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "<p>Growing-memory <code>W_∞</code> AEP (Cover–Thomas Theorem 16.5.1) for the concrete two-sided market: the\x0agrowing-memory log-wealth average converges almost surely to the infinite-past optimal growth rate\x0a<code>W_∞ = condOptGrowthInfty</code>. The sequence space is <code>Ω = ∀ _ : ℤ, Fin m → ℝ</code>, the dynamics is the\x0atwo-sided shift <code>shiftZ</code>, the per-epoch price relative is the coordinate-0 projection <code>coord0</code>, and\x0athe filtration is the finite-past <code>pastFiltration</code>. The two shift/past coherences of the abstract\x0astatement are discharged internally; all remaining hypotheses are market-regularity/ergodicity\x0apreconditions (measure preservation, ergodicity, simplex membership, positivity, integrability,\x0aconditional dominance).\x0a@audit:ok</p>"),
