  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Sanov.MultinomialLowerBound module doc 0", "./",
   "# Multinomial lower bound (Stirling-free)\x0a\x0aThe Stirling-free multinomial lower bound for the type class cardinality\x0a(Cover-Thomas 11.1.3):\x0a`(n+1)^{-|α|} · n^n / ∏ c(a)^{c(a)} ≤ |T_c|`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `typeClassByCount_card_ge` — multinomial lower bound (Stirling-free):\x0a  `(n+1)^{-|α|} · n^n / ∏ c(a)^{c(a)} ≤ |T_c|`.\x0a* `typeClassByCount_Qn_ge` — lower bound on `Q^n(T_c)`:\x0a  `Q^n(T_c) ≥ (n+1)^{-|α|} · exp(-n · klDivIndex c n Q)`.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0a* The multinomial lower bound is proved without Stirling's approximation, using only\x0a  the per-letter inequality `c! · c^k ≤ k! · c^c`.\x0a\x0a## References\x0a\x0a* T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, *Elements of Information Theory* (2nd ed.),\x0a  Wiley, 2006. Theorem 11.1.3.\x0a",
   "<h1 id=\"Multinomial-lower-bound-Stirling-free\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Multinomial lower bound (Stirling-free) <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Multinomial-lower-bound-Stirling-free\">#</a></h1><p>The Stirling-free multinomial lower bound for the type class cardinality\x0a(Cover-Thomas 11.1.3):\x0a<code>(n+1)^{-|α|} · n^n / ∏ c(a)^{c(a)} ≤ |T_c|</code>.</p><h2 id=\"Main-statements\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Main statements <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Main-statements\">#</a></h2><ul><li><code>typeClassByCount_card_ge</code> — multinomial lower bound (Stirling-free):\x0a<code>(n+1)^{-|α|} · n^n / ∏ c(a)^{c(a)} ≤ |T_c|</code>.</li><li><code>typeClassByCount_Qn_ge</code> — lower bound on <code>Q^n(T_c)</code>:\x0a<code>Q^n(T_c) ≥ (n+1)^{-|α|} · exp(-n · klDivIndex c n Q)</code>.</li></ul><h2 id=\"Implementation-notes\" class=\"markdown-heading\">Implementation notes <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#Implementation-notes\">#</a></h2><ul><li>The multinomial lower bound is proved without Stirling's approximation, using only\x0athe per-letter inequality <code>c! · c^k ≤ k! · c^c</code>.</li></ul><h2 id=\"References\" class=\"markdown-heading\">References <a class=\"hover-link\" href=\"#References\">#</a></h2><ul><li>T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, <em>Elements of Information Theory</em> (2nd ed.),\x0aWiley, 2006. Theorem 11.1.3.</li></ul>"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ShannonCode.Basic module doc 6", ".././",
