  ("InformationTheory.Asymptotic module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Asymptotic / exponent framework\x0a\x0aThe exponent-equality relation `\\doteq` of Cover–Thomas and a closed-form rate-extraction\x0awrapper, forming the asymptotic / rate API layer.\x0a\x0a## Notation\x0a\x0a* `a ≐ b` (`DotEq a b`): `(Real.log ∘ a − Real.log ∘ b) =o[atTop] (·:ℝ)`.\x0a* The textbook `f(n) = o(n)` is `f =o[atTop] (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ))`.\x0a* The textbook `f(n) = o(1)` is `f =o[atTop] (fun _ => (1 : ℝ))`.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `DotEq` — exponent equality, defined directly as an `IsLittleO`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `dotEq_iff_tendsto_log_div` — the bridge to `(1/n) · log (a/b) → 0` under positivity.\x0a* `exp_decay_N_of_pos` — a closed-form block length for `exp(-n·g) < ε'`.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0a* `DotEq` is `ℝ`-valued; no `ℝ≥0∞` alias is published here.\x0a* The notation `≐` is `scoped[InformationTheory.Asymptotic]`, so only call sites that\x0a  `open InformationTheory.Asymptotic` see it.\x0a* Positivity is not built into the predicate (Mathlib's `Real.log` returns `0` for `x ≤ 0`,\x0a  so `DotEq` is well-defined for any `ℕ → ℝ`); it is required at the bridge / `mul` / `inv`\x0a  use sites instead.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Asymptotic / exponent framework\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The exponent-equality relation \"],[\"code\",[\"\\\\doteq\"]],[\"normal\",\" of Cover–Thomas and a closed-form rate-extraction\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"wrapper, forming the asymptotic / rate API layer.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Notation\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"a ≐ b\"]],[\"normal\",\" (\"],[\"code\",[\"DotEq a b\"]],[\"normal\",\"): \"],[\"code\",[\"(Real.log ∘ a − Real.log ∘ b) =o[atTop] (·:ℝ)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The textbook \"],[\"code\",[\"f(n) = o(n)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is \"],[\"code\",[\"f =o[atTop] (fun n : ℕ => (n : ℝ))\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The textbook \"],[\"code\",[\"f(n) = o(1)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is \"],[\"code\",[\"f =o[atTop] (fun _ => (1 : ℝ))\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main definitions\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"DotEq\"]],[\"normal\",\" — exponent equality, defined directly as an \"],[\"code\",[\"IsLittleO\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"dotEq_iff_tendsto_log_div\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the bridge to \"],[\"code\",[\"(1/n) · log (a/b) → 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" under positivity.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"exp_decay_N_of_pos\"]],[\"normal\",\" — a closed-form block length for \"],[\"code\",[\"exp(-n·g) < ε'\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Implementation notes\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"DotEq\"]],[\"normal\",\" is \"],[\"code\",[\"ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\"-valued; no \"],[\"code\",[\"ℝ≥0∞\"]],[\"normal\",\" alias is published here.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The notation \"],[\"code\",[\"≐\"]],[\"normal\",\" is \"],[\"code\",[\"scoped[InformationTheory.Asymptotic]\"]],[\"normal\",\", so only call sites that\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"open InformationTheory.Asymptotic\"]],[\"normal\",\" see it.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Positivity is not built into the predicate (Mathlib's \"],[\"code\",[\"Real.log\"]],[\"normal\",\" returns \"],[\"code\",[\"0\"]],[\"normal\",\" for \"],[\"code\",[\"x ≤ 0\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"so \"],[\"code\",[\"DotEq\"]],[\"normal\",\" is well-defined for any \"],[\"code\",[\"ℕ → ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\"); it is required at the bridge / \"],[\"code\",[\"mul\"]],[\"normal\",\" / \"],[\"code\",[\"inv\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"use sites instead.\"]]]]]]]]"),
