  ("InformationTheory.Fano.CondEntropy module doc 0", 8044,
   "# 3-variable joint and conditional entropy: chain rule + deterministic collapse\x0a\x0aWe work directly with raw mass functions `μ : X → E → Y → ℝ` rather than committing to a\x0astructured PMF type, because every chain rule becomes a `ring` identity at this level.\x0a\x0aThe two non-trivial outputs are:\x0a\x0a* the algebraic chain rules `H(X, E | Y) = H(E | Y) + H(X | E, Y)` and\x0a  `H(X, E | Y) = H(X | Y) + H(E | X, Y)`;\x0a* `H(E | X, Y) = 0` whenever `E` is a deterministic function of `(X, Y)`.\x0a\x0aTogether with `entropyOfFn_le_log_supportCard` and `binEntropy_jensen_finset`, these\x0aassemble the Fano core inequality.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aThis file's mass-function entropy/condEntropy are the form used by the `Fano.Core`\x0adevelopment. The measure-theoretic developments (`Fano.Measure`, `Shannon.Bridge.entropy`,\x0a`InformationTheory.MeasureFano.condEntropy`) use a parallel formalism; the two do not\x0adepend on each other.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"3-variable joint and conditional entropy: chain rule + deterministic collapse\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"We work directly with raw mass functions \"],[\"code\",[\"μ : X → E → Y → ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\" rather than committing to a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"structured PMF type, because every chain rule becomes a \"],[\"code\",[\"ring\"]],[\"normal\",\" identity at this level.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The two non-trivial outputs are:\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"the algebraic chain rules \"],[\"code\",[\"H(X, E | Y) = H(E | Y) + H(X | E, Y)\"]],[\"normal\",\" and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"H(X, E | Y) = H(X | Y) + H(E | X, Y)\"]],[\"normal\",\";\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"H(E | X, Y) = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" whenever \"],[\"code\",[\"E\"]],[\"normal\",\" is a deterministic function of \"],[\"code\",[\"(X, Y)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Together with \"],[\"code\",[\"entropyOfFn_le_log_supportCard\"]],[\"normal\",\" and \"],[\"code\",[\"binEntropy_jensen_finset\"]],[\"normal\",\", these\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"assemble the Fano core inequality.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Implementation notes\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"This file's mass-function entropy/condEntropy are the form used by the \"],[\"code\",[\"Fano.Core\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"development. The measure-theoretic developments (\"],[\"code\",[\"Fano.Measure\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"Shannon.Bridge.entropy\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"InformationTheory.MeasureFano.condEntropy\"]],[\"normal\",\") use a parallel formalism; the two do not\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"depend on each other.\"]]]]"),
