  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.TwoSided.pmfLogCondPast_tendsto_pmfLogCondInfty", 8044,
   "Forward Lévy upward convergence: per-step conditional log-likelihood on\x0alonger-and-longer finite past converges to `pmfLogCondInfty`. Application of\x0a`MeasureTheory.tendsto_ae_condExp` (one application per `a : α`, combined\x0aby continuity of `-log` and the inner-sum identity\x0a`∑ a, indicator(coord0=a) * f a = f (coord0 x)`).\x0a\x0aCaveat: convergence holds on the AE set where\x0a`condProbInfty (coord0 x) x > 0` (provided by `ae_condProbInfty_coord0_pos`);\x0aon the null set where the conditional probability of the realized coord0\x0avalue is `0`, `Real.log` is discontinuous, and we report\x0a`pmfLogCondPast/pmfLogCondInfty` as `0` by convention (`Real.log 0 = 0`). ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Forward Lévy upward convergence: per-step conditional log-likelihood on\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"longer-and-longer finite past converges to \"],[\"code\",[\"pmfLogCondInfty\"]],[\"normal\",\". Application of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"MeasureTheory.tendsto_ae_condExp\"]],[\"normal\",\" (one application per \"],[\"code\",[\"a : α\"]],[\"normal\",\", combined\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"by continuity of \"],[\"code\",[\"-log\"]],[\"normal\",\" and the inner-sum identity\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"∑ a, indicator(coord0=a) * f a = f (coord0 x)\"]],[\"normal\",\").\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Caveat: convergence holds on the AE set where\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"condProbInfty (coord0 x) x > 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" (provided by \"],[\"code\",[\"ae_condProbInfty_coord0_pos\"]],[\"normal\",\");\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"on the null set where the conditional probability of the realized coord0\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"value is \"],[\"code\",[\"0\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"Real.log\"]],[\"normal\",\" is discontinuous, and we report\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"pmfLogCondPast/pmfLogCondInfty\"]],[\"normal\",\" as \"],[\"code\",[\"0\"]],[\"normal\",\" by convention (\"],[\"code\",[\"Real.log 0 = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\").\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AEP.Basic module doc 0", 8044,
   "# AEP — Asymptotic Equipartition Property\x0a\x0aFormalization of the asymptotic equipartition property, Cover-Thomas Theorem\x0a3.1.1–3.1.2. This module re-exports the AEP core, the source-coding converse, and\x0athe achievability development from the `AEP.Basic.*` submodules.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `jointRV` — the block random variable `Ω → (Fin n → α)` built from an i.i.d.\x0a  sequence `Xs : ℕ → Ω → α`.\x0a* `typicalSet` — the typical set `T_ε^n`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `aep_ae` / `aep_inProbability` — the empirical entropy estimator\x0a  `(1/n) ∑ i, (-Real.log ((μ.map (Xs 0)).real {Xs i ω}))` converges to\x0a  `entropy μ (Xs 0)` almost surely and in probability.\x0a* `typicalSet_card_le` / `typicalSet_prob_tendsto_one` — size bound and\x0a  asymptotic probability of the typical set.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aMathlib has no `IsIID` predicate, so the i.i.d. hypothesis is taken in the same\x0atwo-part form as `strong_law_ae_real`:\x0a`Pairwise (fun i j => Xs i ⟂ᵢ[μ] Xs j)` and `∀ i, IdentDistrib (Xs i) (Xs 0) μ μ`.\x0aThe `(· ⟂ᵢ[μ] ·) on Xs` anonymous-lambda form fails to parse when combined with\x0a`on`, so the explicit `fun i j => …` form is used.\x0a",
