  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.awgnCapacity_ge_gaussian", 8044,
   "The AWGN capacity is bounded below by `(1/2) log(1 + P/N)`, achieved by the\x0aGaussian input via the closed-form mutual information hypothesis `h_bridge_gauss`.\x0a\x0a`@audit:superseded-by(awgn_capacity_closed_form_genuine)` ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The AWGN capacity is bounded below by \"],[\"code\",[\"(1/2) log(1 + P/N)\"]],[\"normal\",\", achieved by the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Gaussian input via the closed-form mutual information hypothesis \"],[\"code\",[\"h_bridge_gauss\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"@audit:superseded-by(awgn_capacity_closed_form_genuine)\"]]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.bind_eq_conv_of_translation_kernel", 8044,
   "For any kernel `κ : Kernel ℝ ℝ` whose every fiber is the translation map of a\x0afixed measure `ν` (`κ x = ν.map (x + ·)`), the Giry-monad composition with an\x0as-finite input `p` coincides with the additive convolution `p ∗ ν`. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"For any kernel \"],[\"code\",[\"κ : Kernel ℝ ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\" whose every fiber is the translation map of a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"fixed measure \"],[\"code\",[\"ν\"]],[\"normal\",\" (\"],[\"code\",[\"κ x = ν.map (x + ·)\"]],[\"normal\",\"), the Giry-monad composition with an\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"s-finite input \"],[\"code\",[\"p\"]],[\"normal\",\" coincides with the additive convolution \"],[\"code\",[\"p ∗ ν\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.outputMixtureDensity_log_abs_le", 8044,
   "Quadratic bound on `|log f_q|`: there exist `c₀, c₁ : ℝ` with\x0a`|log (f_q y).toReal| ≤ c₀ + c₁ · y²` for all `y`. Combines the constant upper bound\x0a`outputMixtureDensity_le_sup` with the quadratic lower bound\x0a`output_logDensity_lower_bound`. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Quadratic bound on \"],[\"code\",[\"|log f_q|\"]],[\"normal\",\": there exist \"],[\"code\",[\"c₀, c₁ : ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\" with\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"|log (f_q y).toReal| ≤ c₀ + c₁ · y²\"]],[\"normal\",\" for all \"],[\"code\",[\"y\"]],[\"normal\",\". Combines the constant upper bound\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"outputMixtureDensity_le_sup\"]],[\"normal\",\" with the quadratic lower bound\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"output_logDensity_lower_bound\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.outputDistribution_logDensity_integrable_joint", 8044,
   "Joint form of `outputDistribution_logDensity_integrable`:\x0a`log ((q.rnDeriv vol ·).toReal) ∘ snd` is integrable against the joint `p ⊗ₘ W`.\x0aLift along the snd-marginal: `q = (p ⊗ₘ W).map Prod.snd`, and `|log f_q| ≤ c₀ + c₁·y²`\x0ais integrable against `q` (finite second moment), so the snd-pullback is integrable\x0aagainst `p ⊗ₘ W`, via `integrable_map_measure` and `outputMixtureDensity_log_abs_le`.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Joint form of \"],[\"code\",[\"outputDistribution_logDensity_integrable\"]],[\"normal\",\":\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"log ((q.rnDeriv vol ·).toReal) ∘ snd\"]],[\"normal\",\" is integrable against the joint \"],[\"code\",[\"p ⊗ₘ W\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Lift along the snd-marginal: \"],[\"code\",[\"q = (p ⊗ₘ W).map Prod.snd\"]],[\"normal\",\", and \"],[\"code\",[\"|log f_q| ≤ c₀ + c₁·y²\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"is integrable against \"],[\"code\",[\"q\"]],[\"normal\",\" (finite second moment), so the snd-pullback is integrable\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"against \"],[\"code\",[\"p ⊗ₘ W\"]],[\"normal\",\", via \"],[\"code\",[\"integrable_map_measure\"]],[\"normal\",\" and \"],[\"code\",[\"outputMixtureDensity_log_abs_le\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.isAwgnChannelMeasurable", 8044,
   "The AWGN channel kernel `fun x : ℝ ↦ gaussianReal x N` is measurable on the Giry\x0amonad, discharging the `IsAwgnChannelMeasurable N` predicate. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The AWGN channel kernel \"],[\"code\",[\"fun x : ℝ ↦ gaussianReal x N\"]],[\"normal\",\" is measurable on the Giry\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"monad, discharging the \"],[\"code\",[\"IsAwgnChannelMeasurable N\"]],[\"normal\",\" predicate.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.integrable_sq_sub_gaussianReal", 8044,
   "Second moment of a real Gaussian is integrable. `(y − m)²` is integrable\x0aagainst `gaussianReal m' v'` (any mean / variance), since `id ∈ L²(gaussianReal)`\x0a(`memLp_id_gaussianReal`). Needed to discharge the Gaussian log-density\x0aintegrabilities (the log pdf is a constant plus a `(y − m)²` term). ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Second moment of a real Gaussian is integrable. \"],[\"code\",[\"(y − m)²\"]],[\"normal\",\" is integrable\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"against \"],[\"code\",[\"gaussianReal m' v'\"]],[\"normal\",\" (any mean / variance), since \"],[\"code\",[\"id ∈ L²(gaussianReal)\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(\"],[\"code\",[\"memLp_id_gaussianReal\"]],[\"normal\",\"). Needed to discharge the Gaussian log-density\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"integrabilities (the log pdf is a constant plus a \"],[\"code\",[\"(y − m)²\"]],[\"normal\",\" term).\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.ConverseCapacityBound module doc 1", 8044,
   "## Per-letter input second moment, Jensen, and the sum-form capacity bound\x0a\x0aThe capacity bound `∑ᵢ I(Xᵢ; Yᵢ) ≤ n · (1/2) log(1 + P/N)` is established in sum form via the\x0aper-letter Gaussian maximum-entropy bound and Jensen's inequality, rather than from a\x0aper-letter power constraint (which does not follow from the per-message power constraint). ",
   "[[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Per-letter input second moment, Jensen, and the sum-form capacity bound\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The capacity bound \"],[\"code\",[\"∑ᵢ I(Xᵢ; Yᵢ) ≤ n · (1/2) log(1 + P/N)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is established in sum form via the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"per-letter Gaussian maximum-entropy bound and Jensen's inequality, rather than from a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"per-letter power constraint (which does not follow from the per-message power constraint).\"]]]]"),
