  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.awgn_perLetter_klDiv_degenerate", 8044,
   "Degenerate per-letter KL vanishes (`P' = 0 ∨ N = 0`): in either degenerate case\x0athe per-letter KL `(klDiv J₁ Q₁).toReal = 0`. When `P' = 0` the input collapses to `Dirac 0`,\x0athe shear is the identity on `{0} × ℝ`, so `J₁ = Q₁` (`klDiv_self`). When `N = 0`\x0a(with `P' ≠ 0`) the joint `J₁` concentrates on the diagonal `{(x, x)}`, which is `Q₁`-null\x0a(positive-variance Gaussian product, atomless), so `¬ J₁ ≪ Q₁` ⇒ `klDiv = ⊤` ⇒ `toReal = 0`. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Degenerate per-letter KL vanishes (\"],[\"code\",[\"P' = 0 ∨ N = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\"): in either degenerate case\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the per-letter KL \"],[\"code\",[\"(klDiv J₁ Q₁).toReal = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\". When \"],[\"code\",[\"P' = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" the input collapses to \"],[\"code\",[\"Dirac 0\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the shear is the identity on \"],[\"code\",[\"{0} × ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\", so \"],[\"code\",[\"J₁ = Q₁\"]],[\"normal\",\" (\"],[\"code\",[\"klDiv_self\"]],[\"normal\",\"). When \"],[\"code\",[\"N = 0\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(with \"],[\"code\",[\"P' ≠ 0\"]],[\"normal\",\") the joint \"],[\"code\",[\"J₁\"]],[\"normal\",\" concentrates on the diagonal \"],[\"code\",[\"{(x, x)}\"]],[\"normal\",\", which is \"],[\"code\",[\"Q₁\"]],[\"normal\",\"-null\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(positive-variance Gaussian product, atomless), so \"],[\"code\",[\"¬ J₁ ≪ Q₁\"]],[\"normal\",\" ⇒ \"],[\"code\",[\"klDiv = ⊤\"]],[\"normal\",\" ⇒ \"],[\"code\",[\"toReal = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.awgn_capacity_closed_form_of_primitives", 8044,
   "The AWGN capacity closed form, re-published with the Gaussian mutual-information\x0afact reduced to the two primitives `IsAwgnOutputGaussian` and `IsAwgnMIDecomp`. The\x0aremaining hypotheses (`h_bdd`, `h_max_ent`) are unchanged.\x0a\x0a`@audit:superseded-by(awgn_capacity_closed_form_genuine)` ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The AWGN capacity closed form, re-published with the Gaussian mutual-information\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"fact reduced to the two primitives \"],[\"code\",[\"IsAwgnOutputGaussian\"]],[\"normal\",\" and \"],[\"code\",[\"IsAwgnMIDecomp\"]],[\"normal\",\". The\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"remaining hypotheses (\"],[\"code\",[\"h_bdd\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"h_max_ent\"]],[\"normal\",\") are unchanged.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"@audit:superseded-by(awgn_capacity_closed_form_genuine)\"]]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.AWGN.MutualInfoBridge module doc 0", 8044,
   "# AWGN output marginal is Gaussian\x0a\x0aThe AWGN channel output marginal under Gaussian input is itself Gaussian:\x0a\x0a```\x0aIsAwgnOutputGaussian P N h_meas\x0a  := (outputDistribution (gaussianReal 0 P.toNNReal) (awgnChannel N h_meas))\x0a        = gaussianReal 0 (P.toNNReal + N)\x0a```\x0a\x0athat is, for `Y = X + Z` with `X ∼ 𝒩(0, P)` and independent `Z ∼ 𝒩(0, N)` one has\x0a`Y ∼ 𝒩(0, P + N)`.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `IsAwgnBindEqConv` — the bridge identity stating that the AWGN kernel composition\x0a  equals additive convolution of measures.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `awgn_output_gaussian_of_bind_eq_conv` — the output marginal is `𝒩(0, P + N)`,\x0a  given the bind/conv bridge.\x0a* `awgn_capacity_closed_form_of_maxent_bindconv` — the capacity closed form with the\x0a  output-Gaussian fact reduced to the bind/conv bridge, the remaining mutual-information\x0a  facts taken as hypotheses.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aThe output marginal is computed in three structural steps: `outputDistribution` is\x0athe second marginal of the joint law (definitional), `(p ⊗ₘ W).snd = W ∘ₘ p` is the\x0aMarkov-kernel composition identity (`Measure.snd_compProd`), and\x0a`gaussianReal_conv_gaussianReal` collapses the convolution of two Gaussians into a\x0asingle Gaussian.\x0a\x0aThe middle step — that the AWGN kernel composition coincides with additive\x0aconvolution — is a generic translation-kernel identity that is independent of the\x0aAWGN specifics. Proving it inline through the characteristic-function route would\x0ainflate the file by roughly 80–100 lines (`lintegral` expansion, Fubini, change of\x0avariables), so it is exposed as the single named hypothesis `IsAwgnBindEqConv` and\x0aproved separately.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"AWGN output marginal is Gaussian\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The AWGN channel output marginal under Gaussian input is itself Gaussian:\"]]],[\"code\",[],[],\"`\",[\"IsAwgnOutputGaussian P N h_meas\",\"\\n\",\"  \",\":= (outputDistribution (gaussianReal 0 P.toNNReal) (awgnChannel N h_meas))\",\"\\n\",\"        \",\"= gaussianReal 0 (P.toNNReal + N)\",\"\\n\"]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"that is, for \"],[\"code\",[\"Y = X + Z\"]],[\"normal\",\" with \"],[\"code\",[\"X ∼ 𝒩(0, P)\"]],[\"normal\",\" and independent \"],[\"code\",[\"Z ∼ 𝒩(0, N)\"]],[\"normal\",\" one has\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"Y ∼ 𝒩(0, P + N)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main definitions\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"IsAwgnBindEqConv\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the bridge identity stating that the AWGN kernel composition\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"equals additive convolution of measures.\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"awgn_output_gaussian_of_bind_eq_conv\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the output marginal is \"],[\"code\",[\"𝒩(0, P + N)\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"given the bind/conv bridge.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"awgn_capacity_closed_form_of_maxent_bindconv\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the capacity closed form with the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"output-Gaussian fact reduced to the bind/conv bridge, the remaining mutual-information\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"facts taken as hypotheses.\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Implementation notes\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The output marginal is computed in three structural steps: \"],[\"code\",[\"outputDistribution\"]],[\"normal\",\" is\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the second marginal of the joint law (definitional), \"],[\"code\",[\"(p ⊗ₘ W).snd = W ∘ₘ p\"]],[\"normal\",\" is the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Markov-kernel composition identity (\"],[\"code\",[\"Measure.snd_compProd\"]],[\"normal\",\"), and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"gaussianReal_conv_gaussianReal\"]],[\"normal\",\" collapses the convolution of two Gaussians into a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"single Gaussian.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The middle step — that the AWGN kernel composition coincides with additive\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"convolution — is a generic translation-kernel identity that is independent of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"AWGN specifics. Proving it inline through the characteristic-function route would\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"inflate the file by roughly 80–100 lines (\"],[\"code\",[\"lintegral\"]],[\"normal\",\" expansion, Fubini, change of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"variables), so it is exposed as the single named hypothesis \"],[\"code\",[\"IsAwgnBindEqConv\"]],[\"normal\",\" and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"proved separately.\"]]]]"),
