  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.BackwardMartingale.ae_tendsto", 8044,
   "The **backward martingale convergence theorem**. If `f : ℕᵒᵈ → Ω → ℝ`\x0ais a martingale with respect to an antitone filtration `ℋ : Filtration ℕᵒᵈ m₀`\x0aand `f (toDual 0)` is integrable, then `n ↦ f (toDual n) ω` converges almost\x0aeverywhere as `n → ∞` to a `⨅ n, ℋ (toDual n)`-measurable limit `g`.\x0a\x0aThis is the reverse-time analogue of\x0a`MeasureTheory.Submartingale.ae_tendsto_limitProcess`\x0a(`Probability/Martingale/Convergence.lean:209`).\x0a\x0aProof: combines the L¹ bound + a.e. upcrossing finiteness +\x0a`tendsto_of_uncrossing_lt_top` to obtain pointwise convergence a.e., then\x0aconstructs the `⨅ n, ℋ (toDual n)`-measurable limit via the standard\x0a`aemeasurable_of_tendsto_metrizable_ae'` pattern with a tail-σ-algebra\x0aargument. The tail measurability step (which `Submartingale.ae_tendsto_limitProcess`\x0ahandles via `measurableSet_exists_tendsto` over `⨆ n, ℱ n`) is here a direct\x0amirror over `⨅ n, ℋ (toDual n)`. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The \"],[\"strong\",[[\"normal\",\"backward martingale convergence theorem\"]]],[\"normal\",\". If \"],[\"code\",[\"f : ℕᵒᵈ → Ω → ℝ\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"is a martingale with respect to an antitone filtration \"],[\"code\",[\"ℋ : Filtration ℕᵒᵈ m₀\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"and \"],[\"code\",[\"f (toDual 0)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is integrable, then \"],[\"code\",[\"n ↦ f (toDual n) ω\"]],[\"normal\",\" converges almost\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"everywhere as \"],[\"code\",[\"n → ∞\"]],[\"normal\",\" to a \"],[\"code\",[\"⨅ n, ℋ (toDual n)\"]],[\"normal\",\"-measurable limit \"],[\"code\",[\"g\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"This is the reverse-time analogue of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"MeasureTheory.Submartingale.ae_tendsto_limitProcess\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(\"],[\"code\",[\"Probability/Martingale/Convergence.lean:209\"]],[\"normal\",\").\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Proof: combines the L¹ bound + a.e. upcrossing finiteness +\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"tendsto_of_uncrossing_lt_top\"]],[\"normal\",\" to obtain pointwise convergence a.e., then\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"constructs the \"],[\"code\",[\"⨅ n, ℋ (toDual n)\"]],[\"normal\",\"-measurable limit via the standard\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"aemeasurable_of_tendsto_metrizable_ae'\"]],[\"normal\",\" pattern with a tail-σ-algebra\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"argument. The tail measurability step (which \"],[\"code\",[\"Submartingale.ae_tendsto_limitProcess\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"handles via \"],[\"code\",[\"measurableSet_exists_tendsto\"]],[\"normal\",\" over \"],[\"code\",[\"⨆ n, ℱ n\"]],[\"normal\",\") is here a direct\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"mirror over \"],[\"code\",[\"⨅ n, ℋ (toDual n)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
