  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.BroadcastChannel.BroadcastCode.padFirst", 8044,
   "A second receiver-1 message attached to a code that carries only one.  Both messages are sent\x0awith the single codeword of the original code, so receiver 1 cannot separate them, while receiver\x0a2 sees exactly the original code.  This is what puts a code of a nonpositive rate pair inside the\x0ascope of the converse, which asks for at least two messages per receiver.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"A second receiver-1 message attached to a code that carries only one.  Both messages are sent\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"with the single codeword of the original code, so receiver 1 cannot separate them, while receiver\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"2 sees exactly the original code.  This is what puts a code of a nonpositive rate pair inside the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"scope of the converse, which asks for at least two messages per receiver.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
