  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.BroadcastChannel.Marton.marton_errorProbAt₁_le_bonferroni", 8044,
   "Receiver-1 error decomposition at a fixed message pair: the error probability is at most the\x0aprobability that the transmitted auxiliary word fails to be jointly typical with the received word,\x0aplus the sum, over the auxiliary codewords of every other message row, of the probability that one\x0aof them is jointly typical with it.  Quantifying the covering index existentially is what keeps a\x0asecond typical index inside the transmitted row off the error event, so the alias sum ranges over\x0athe rows of the other messages only.\x0a\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Receiver-1 error decomposition at a fixed message pair: the error probability is at most the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"probability that the transmitted auxiliary word fails to be jointly typical with the received word,\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"plus the sum, over the auxiliary codewords of every other message row, of the probability that one\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"of them is jointly typical with it.  Quantifying the covering index existentially is what keeps a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"second typical index inside the transmitted row off the error event, so the alias sum ranges over\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the rows of the other messages only.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
