  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.BroadcastChannel.Marton.closure_convexHull_martonRegionUnion_eq_outerBounded", 8044,
   "The closed convex hull of Marton's inner bound is unchanged when the outer auxiliary alphabet\x0ais capped at `martonAuxBound α` letters, the size of the channel input alphabet.  No cap is placed\x0aon the inner auxiliary alphabet.\x0a\x0aOnly the closed convex hull is unchanged: a point of the uncapped union lies in the closed convex\x0ahull of the capped one, not necessarily in the capped union itself, which is not claimed to be\x0aconvex.  Capping the outer alphabet alone leaves the union ranging over every cardinality of the\x0ainner one, so it is not a union over finitely many indices.\x0a`closure_convexHull_martonRegionUnion_eq_bounded` caps both alphabets, and its union does run\x0aover finitely many indices.\x0a@audit:ok ",
