  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.Achievability.Main module doc 1", 8044,
   "### Pigeonhole (probabilistic-method form)\x0a\x0aCodebooks are drawn from `codebookMeasure p M n` rather than uniformly over\x0a`Codebook M n α`. The pigeonhole: if the expectation\x0a`∑ codebook, μ_codebook · f(codebook) ≤ B`, then some `codebook` in the support\x0ahas `f(codebook) ≤ B`. The proof uses the fact that the codebook measure is a\x0aprobability measure (mass sums to `1` over the finite space) so the weighted\x0aaverage is a convex combination. ",
   "[[\"header\",3,[[\"normal\",\"Pigeonhole (probabilistic-method form)\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Codebooks are drawn from \"],[\"code\",[\"codebookMeasure p M n\"]],[\"normal\",\" rather than uniformly over\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"Codebook M n α\"]],[\"normal\",\". The pigeonhole: if the expectation\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"∑ codebook, μ_codebook · f(codebook) ≤ B\"]],[\"normal\",\", then some \"],[\"code\",[\"codebook\"]],[\"normal\",\" in the support\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"has \"],[\"code\",[\"f(codebook) ≤ B\"]],[\"normal\",\". The proof uses the fact that the codebook measure is a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"probability measure (mass sums to \"],[\"code\",[\"1\"]],[\"normal\",\" over the finite space) so the weighted\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"average is a convex combination.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.random_codebook_average_le", 8044,
   "Random codebook average (probabilistic-method form). With each codeword\x0adrawn i.i.d. from `p^n` (so the codebook law is `codebookMeasure p M n`), the\x0acodebook-average of the (uniform-over-message) error probability decomposes via\x0aFubini into the \"joint typical event probability\" (E1) plus `(M - 1) ·` the\x0aindependent-pair bound (E2).\x0a\x0aThe structural backbone (per-codebook bound via `errorProbAt_le_E1_plus_E2`,\x0asum / swap arithmetic) is assembled here from the two Fubini swap ingredients\x0a`random_codebook_E1_swap` and `random_codebook_E2_swap` (private lemmas above). ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Random codebook average (probabilistic-method form). With each codeword\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"drawn i.i.d. from \"],[\"code\",[\"p^n\"]],[\"normal\",\" (so the codebook law is \"],[\"code\",[\"codebookMeasure p M n\"]],[\"normal\",\"), the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"codebook-average of the (uniform-over-message) error probability decomposes via\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Fubini into the \\\"joint typical event probability\\\" (E1) plus \"],[\"code\",[\"(M - 1) ·\"]],[\"normal\",\" the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"independent-pair bound (E2).\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The structural backbone (per-codebook bound via \"],[\"code\",[\"errorProbAt_le_E1_plus_E2\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"sum / swap arithmetic) is assembled here from the two Fubini swap ingredients\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"random_codebook_E1_swap\"]],[\"normal\",\" and \"],[\"code\",[\"random_codebook_E2_swap\"]],[\"normal\",\" (private lemmas above).\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.jointlyTypicalSet_indep_prob_le", 8044,
   "Bound (c): independent-pair probability. The probability under the product\x0ameasure `μX^n × μY^n` (where `μX^n := μ.map (jointRV Xs n)` and similarly for `Y`) that\x0a`(X̃, Y)` lies in the jointly typical set is bounded by `exp(-n(I - 3ε))` (in the\x0alog form: `exp(n · (H(X,Y) - H(X) - H(Y) + 3ε))`).\x0a\x0aMutual independence (`iIndepFun`) along each of the `X` and `Y` axes is required\x0ato factorise the block laws `μ.map (jointRV Xs n) = Measure.pi (μ.map (Xs ·))`. The\x0ajoint axis identification (`hidentZ`) is not required for this bound (it is\x0arequired only by the random-codebook average downstream of this lemma). ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Bound (c): independent-pair probability. The probability under the product\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"measure \"],[\"code\",[\"μX^n × μY^n\"]],[\"normal\",\" (where \"],[\"code\",[\"μX^n := μ.map (jointRV Xs n)\"]],[\"normal\",\" and similarly for \"],[\"code\",[\"Y\"]],[\"normal\",\") that\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"(X̃, Y)\"]],[\"normal\",\" lies in the jointly typical set is bounded by \"],[\"code\",[\"exp(-n(I - 3ε))\"]],[\"normal\",\" (in the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"log form: \"],[\"code\",[\"exp(n · (H(X,Y) - H(X) - H(Y) + 3ε))\"]],[\"normal\",\").\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Mutual independence (\"],[\"code\",[\"iIndepFun\"]],[\"normal\",\") along each of the \"],[\"code\",[\"X\"]],[\"normal\",\" and \"],[\"code\",[\"Y\"]],[\"normal\",\" axes is required\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"to factorise the block laws \"],[\"code\",[\"μ.map (jointRV Xs n) = Measure.pi (μ.map (Xs ·))\"]],[\"normal\",\". The\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"joint axis identification (\"],[\"code\",[\"hidentZ\"]],[\"normal\",\") is not required for this bound (it is\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"required only by the random-codebook average downstream of this lemma).\"]]]]"),
