  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ChannelCoding.channelCoding_average_success_le", 8044,
   "Average-codeword Verdú-Han bound:\x0aAverage the per-codeword decomposition over the uniform message distribution\x0ato get the strong-converse-style lower bound on success probability `1 - avgPe`:\x0a\x0a```\x0a1 - avgPe ≤ exp(threshold) / M + (1 / M) · ∑_m P_m^n(highLLR_m)\x0a```\x0a\x0aThe decoding regions form a measurable partition of `Fin n → β`, so summing\x0a`Q.real (decodingRegion m)` gives `Q.real univ ≤ 1` (since `Q` is a probability\x0ameasure), and the first term collapses to `exp(threshold)/M`. ",
