  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ConditionalMethodOfTypes module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Conditional method of types — `conditionalStronglyTypicalSlice_mass_ge`\x0a\x0aCover-Thomas 10.6.1: for a fixed X-strongly-typical `x : Fin n → α`, lower-bound the\x0aY-product mass of the conditional strongly-typical slice\x0a`{y | (x, y) ∈ jointStronglyTypicalSet μ Xs Ys n ε}` under `μ_Y^n`:\x0a\x0a  `exp(-n · (entropy μ Z₀ - entropy μ X₀ + slack))\x0a     ≤ (Measure.pi (μ.map (Ys 0))^n).real (conditionalStronglyTypicalSlice ...)`\x0a\x0awhere `entropy μ Z₀ - entropy μ X₀ = H(Y|X)` (conditional entropy in chain-rule form)\x0aand `slack = O(ε)`.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0a`H(Y|X)` is expressed as `entropy μ Z₀ - entropy μ X₀` (chain-rule form), matching\x0awhat the rate-distortion achievability consumer expects. The `mutualInfoOfChannel`\x0areshape is a separate concern and is avoided here.\x0a",
