   "Tower of conditional entropy: disintegrating the joint conditioner `(Y, Z)` into\x0a`Z` given `Y` followed by `Y`,\x0a`H(X | Y, Z) = ∫ y, ∫ z, Σ x, negMulLog (condDistrib X (Y,Z) μ (y,z) {x})\x0a                d(condDistrib Z Y μ y) d P_Y`.\x0a\x0aThe inner expression `Σ x, negMulLog (condDistrib X (Y,Z) μ (y,z) {x})` is the slice-wise\x0aShannon entropy of `X` conditioned on the simultaneous value of `Y` and `Z`. The two\x0aouter integrals build back up to `H(X | Y, Z)`. Required as a lemma for the middle\x0aresult `condMutualInfo_eq_condEntropy_sub_condEntropy`. ",
