  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPICase1RatioLimit.entropyPower_add_ge_case1_of_regular", 8044,
   "The classical entropy power inequality `N(law(X+Y)) ≥ N(law X) + N(law Y)` for\x0aabsolutely continuous inputs, proved with auxiliary Gaussian noise and without an entropic\x0aCLT, under heat-flow and scaling regularity preconditions. It is assembled from the two\x0apillars:\x0a\x0a* `csiszarLogRatioGap_antitoneOn_Ici_zero` (`EPI/Stam/ToBridge.lean`):\x0a  the log-ratio gap `R = csiszarLogRatioGap X Y Z_X Z_Y P` is `AntitoneOn (Set.Ici 0)`.\x0a* `csiszarLogRatioGap_tendsto_zero_atTop` (§4): `R t → 0` as `t → ∞`.\x0a\x0aBy the order-limit bridge §1 `epi_of_csiszarLogRatioGap_tendsto`, antitonicity +\x0a`R t → 0` force `R 0 ≥ 0`, hence EPI. No entropic CLT — the saturation `R t → 0`\x0ais the scaling squeeze of §4.\x0a\x0aAll hypotheses are regularity preconditions, the union of the two\x0apillars' preconditions: pairwise + joint independence (`hXZX`/`hYZY`/`hXYZXY`), the\x0athree `IsDeBruijnRegularityHyp` / `IsHeatFlowEndpointRegular` density-witness bundles,\x0athe per-`t` `h_pos_stam` Fisher/Stam/Blachman bundle (ratio antitone side), the noise\x0aGaussian laws + a.c. (`hZX_law`/`hZY_law`/`hZXZY_indep`/`hZX_ac`/`hZY_ac`/`hZXZY_ac`),\x0athe per-`t` scaling regularity (`h_scale_X/Y/sum`), and the per-path variance data +\x0athree `IsRescaledPathRegular` bundles (§4 side). None is load-bearing: the EPI /\x0aStam core is supplied inside the two pillars; the conclusion\x0a`N(X+Y) ≥ N(X)+N(Y)` is not encoded in any hypothesis. The `_of_regular` suffix\x0arecords that those regularity preconditions are real and not removable here.\x0a\x0a@audit:ok\x0a@audit:superseded-by(entropyPowerExt_add_ge) Superseded by the\x0aunconditional EPI; the sole consumer `entropyPower_add_ge_case1_of_methodX` is a dead leaf.\x0aRetained as proof-done. The two-time variant `entropyPower_add_ge_case1_of_regular_twotime` is\x0aseparate and live. ",
