  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.EPICase1TwoTime.matchedSum_law_eq", 8044,
   "The matched-sum law equals the single-noise heat flow of `X+Y` at `τ = s_t + r_t`.\x0a\x0aAt a single time the matched-sum perturbation\x0a`X + √(s_t)·Z_X + (Y + √(r_t)·Z_Y)` rearranges to\x0a`(X+Y) + (√(s_t)·Z_X + √(r_t)·Z_Y)`, and the noise\x0a`√(s_t)·Z_X + √(r_t)·Z_Y` — being a sum of independent centered Gaussians of\x0avariances `s_t·v_X` and `r_t·v_Y` — has law `𝒩(0, s_t·v_X + r_t·v_Y)`\x0aindependent of `X+Y`. Taking unit-variance noises (`v_X = v_Y = 1`) and\x0a`τ = s_t + r_t`, the matched-sum law equals the law of `(X+Y) + √τ·Z` for a unit\x0aGaussian `Z` independent of `X+Y`. This is the single-noise heat flow of `X+Y`\x0aat time `τ`, which lets `J_S` be pinned by the existing single-noise\x0a`IsDeBruijnRegularityHyp (X+Y) Z P`.\x0a\x0aThe hypotheses are regularity preconditions only (measurability, the unit-noise\x0alaws of `Z_X`, `Z_Y`, `Z`, and the relevant independences). The conclusion is a\x0apure measure equality; no derivative value or EPI content is bundled.\x0aBody: Gaussian convolution additivity (`gaussianReal` add of the independent\x0anoise variances) + reassociation of the `map`.\x0a\x0aThe precondition is joint independence of `X+Y` from the pair `(Z_X, Z_Y)`\x0a(`hXY_ZXZY_pair`) rather than from the unscaled sum `Z_X+Z_Y`: the matched-sum\x0anoise is the *scaled* combination `√s_t·Z_X + √r_t·Z_Y` (a different linear\x0afunctional from `Z_X+Z_Y` when `s_t ≠ r_t`), and its independence from `X+Y`\x0ais recovered by `IndepFun.comp` with the measurable map\x0a`(z₁, z₂) ↦ √s_t·z₁ + √r_t·z₂`. This is a regularity precondition, not a\x0abundling of the conclusion.\x0a\x0aClosed via `gaussianReal_map_const_mul` (scaled-noise law `√c·W ∼ 𝒩(0,c)`),\x0a`gaussianReal_add_gaussianReal_of_indepFun` (LHS noise additivity), and\x0a`IndepFun.map_add_eq_map_conv_map` (split both sides as\x0a`(P.map (X+Y)) ∗ 𝒩(0, s_t+r_t)`). `#print axioms` = sorryAx-free. ",
