  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.IsHeatFlowEndpointRegular", 8044,
   "The heat-flow endpoint regularity bundle (a precondition consumed by the EPI\x0acontinuity assembly in `EPI/Stam/ToBridge.lean`).\x0a\x0aCarries exactly the regularity / input-distribution data the density-identification\x0abridge (`pPath_eq_convDensityAdd`) and the entropy-integral machinery\x0a(`differentialEntropy_convDensity_integral_tendsto`) require, at the endpoint\x0a`t = 0⁺`:\x0a\x0a* `hX_meas` / `hZ_meas` / `hXZ_indep` — measurability + independence of the de\x0a  Bruijn pair `X ⊥ Z` (Cover–Thomas 17.7.2 standing assumptions).\x0a* `v_Z` / `hv_Z_pos` / `hZ_law` — the Gaussian noise law `P.map Z = 𝒩(0, v_Z)`\x0a  (general variance, so the sum instance `Z_X+Z_Y ∼ 𝒩(0,2)` fits).\x0a* `pX` / `hpX_nn` / `hpX_meas` / `hpX_law` — a Real density witness for `P.map X`.\x0a* `hpX_int` / `hpX_mass` / `hpX_mom` — `pX` is a probability density with finite\x0a  second moment.\x0a* `hpX_ent` — `negMulLog pX` is `volume`-integrable, i.e. the input differential\x0a  entropy `h(X)` is finite (a regularity precondition on the input distribution,\x0a  not derivable from L¹ + second moment).\x0a\x0aEvery field is a precondition (regularity / input-distribution data); none is a\x0acontinuity / L¹-convergence / density-identification conclusion. This is not a\x0aload-bearing hypothesis bundle — the analytic content is discharged genuinely by\x0a`heatFlowDifferentialEntropy_continuousWithinAt_zero`, which only consumes these\x0afields as inputs. ",
