  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.StamConditionalCauchySchwarz.IsStamScoreConvHyp", 8044,
   "The score-convolution representation (Step 1, typed). Blachman (1965): for independent `X, Y`\x0awith smooth densities, the score of `Z := X + Y` is the conditional expectation\x0a`s_Z(z) = E[λ s_X(X) + (1 - λ) s_Y(Y) | X + Y = z]` for every `λ`. This predicate reifies the\x0aoutput — the existence of the optimal `λ`-witness `λ* = J_Y / (J_X + J_Y)` in `[0, 1]`, the data\x0athe downstream `λ`-optimization consumes — rather than the derivation. It is unconditionally\x0asatisfiable (`isStamScoreConvHyp_intro`). ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The score-convolution representation (Step 1, typed). Blachman (1965): for independent \"],[\"code\",[\"X, Y\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"with smooth densities, the score of \"],[\"code\",[\"Z := X + Y\"]],[\"normal\",\" is the conditional expectation\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"s_Z(z) = E[λ s_X(X) + (1 - λ) s_Y(Y) | X + Y = z]\"]],[\"normal\",\" for every \"],[\"code\",[\"λ\"]],[\"normal\",\". This predicate reifies the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"output — the existence of the optimal \"],[\"code\",[\"λ\"]],[\"normal\",\"-witness \"],[\"code\",[\"λ* = J_Y / (J_X + J_Y)\"]],[\"normal\",\" in \"],[\"code\",[\"[0, 1]\"]],[\"normal\",\", the data\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the downstream \"],[\"code\",[\"λ\"]],[\"normal\",\"-optimization consumes — rather than the derivation. It is unconditionally\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"satisfiable (\"],[\"code\",[\"isStamScoreConvHyp_intro\"]],[\"normal\",\").\"]]]]"),
