  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.entropyPowerExt_add_ge_finite_ac", 8044,
   "The classical entropy power inequality `N(X+Y) ≥ N(X) + N(Y)` when both `P.map X` and\x0a`P.map Y` are absolutely continuous and have finite differential entropy. The proof splits on\x0awhether both inputs have finite variance: the finite-variance branch delegates to the\x0asmoothing-limit closure, the infinite-variance branch to the conditioning-truncation (route T)\x0aclosure. The hypotheses `hX_ent`/`hY_ent`/`hW_ent` are finite-differential-entropy regularity\x0apreconditions.\x0a\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The classical entropy power inequality \"],[\"code\",[\"N(X+Y) ≥ N(X) + N(Y)\"]],[\"normal\",\" when both \"],[\"code\",[\"P.map X\"]],[\"normal\",\" and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"P.map Y\"]],[\"normal\",\" are absolutely continuous and have finite differential entropy. The proof splits on\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"whether both inputs have finite variance: the finite-variance branch delegates to the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"smoothing-limit closure, the infinite-variance branch to the conditioning-truncation (route T)\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"closure. The hypotheses \"],[\"code\",[\"hX_ent\"]],[\"normal\",\"/\"],[\"code\",[\"hY_ent\"]],[\"normal\",\"/\"],[\"code\",[\"hW_ent\"]],[\"normal\",\" are finite-differential-entropy regularity\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"preconditions.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.map_add_absolutelyContinuous", 8044,
   "Convolution preserves absolute continuity: `X` a.c. and `X ⊥ Y ⟹ X+Y` a.c. The sum law factors\x0aas the convolution `μ.map X ∗ μ.map Y` (independence), and `conv_absolutelyContinuous` propagates\x0aabsolute continuity of the a.c. factor.\x0a\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Convolution preserves absolute continuity: \"],[\"code\",[\"X\"]],[\"normal\",\" a.c. and \"],[\"code\",[\"X ⊥ Y ⟹ X+Y\"]],[\"normal\",\" a.c. The sum law factors\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"as the convolution \"],[\"code\",[\"μ.map X ∗ μ.map Y\"]],[\"normal\",\" (independence), and \"],[\"code\",[\"conv_absolutelyContinuous\"]],[\"normal\",\" propagates\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"absolute continuity of the a.c. factor.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.condDistrib_ae_absolutelyContinuous_indep_add", 8044,
   "Per-fibre absolute continuity (continuous disintegration with sum structure): for `W ⊥ V`\x0aunder `Q` with `Q.map W ≪ volume`, the affine-shift fibre `(Q.map W).map (·+z)` (= the per-fibre\x0aconditional law of `W+V` given `V=z`, via `affineShiftKernel`) is a.c. w.r.t. the sum marginal\x0a`(Q.map W) ∗ (Q.map V)`\x0afor a.e. `z ∂(Q.map V)`. This is the continuous version of the general disintegration fact\x0a`condDistrib z ≪ μ.map X` (Mathlib's general/non-discrete version is absent; the in-tree\x0a`Bridge.condDistrib_ae_absolutelyContinuous_map` is `[Countable X]`-only, unusable for `X = ℝ`).\x0a\x0aThe argument uses the sum density `r(x) = ∫⁻ v, f_W(x-v) ∂μ_V` and the translate density\x0a`f_W(·-z)`: a Fubini argument gives `(μ_V × vol)({(z,x) : r(x) = 0 ∧ 0 < f_W(x-z)}) = 0`, and a swap\x0ayields `{r = 0} ⊆ {f_W(·-z) = 0}` vol-a.e. for a.e. `z`, which converts to absolute continuity\x0abetween the `withDensity` measures.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Per-fibre absolute continuity (continuous disintegration with sum structure): for \"],[\"code\",[\"W ⊥ V\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"under \"],[\"code\",[\"Q\"]],[\"normal\",\" with \"],[\"code\",[\"Q.map W ≪ volume\"]],[\"normal\",\", the affine-shift fibre \"],[\"code\",[\"(Q.map W).map (·+z)\"]],[\"normal\",\" (= the per-fibre\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"conditional law of \"],[\"code\",[\"W+V\"]],[\"normal\",\" given \"],[\"code\",[\"V=z\"]],[\"normal\",\", via \"],[\"code\",[\"affineShiftKernel\"]],[\"normal\",\") is a.c. w.r.t. the sum marginal\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"(Q.map W) ∗ (Q.map V)\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"for a.e. \"],[\"code\",[\"z ∂(Q.map V)\"]],[\"normal\",\". This is the continuous version of the general disintegration fact\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"condDistrib z ≪ μ.map X\"]],[\"normal\",\" (Mathlib's general/non-discrete version is absent; the in-tree\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"Bridge.condDistrib_ae_absolutelyContinuous_map\"]],[\"normal\",\" is \"],[\"code\",[\"[Countable X]\"]],[\"normal\",\"-only, unusable for \"],[\"code\",[\"X = ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\").\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The argument uses the sum density \"],[\"code\",[\"r(x) = ∫⁻ v, f_W(x-v) ∂μ_V\"]],[\"normal\",\" and the translate density\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"f_W(·-z)\"]],[\"normal\",\": a Fubini argument gives \"],[\"code\",[\"(μ_V × vol)({(z,x) : r(x) = 0 ∧ 0 < f_W(x-z)}) = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\", and a swap\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"yields \"],[\"code\",[\"{r = 0} ⊆ {f_W(·-z) = 0}\"]],[\"normal\",\" vol-a.e. for a.e. \"],[\"code\",[\"z\"]],[\"normal\",\", which converts to absolute continuity\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"between the \"],[\"code\",[\"withDensity\"]],[\"normal\",\" measures.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.truncW_map_negPart_lintegral_le", 8044,
   "Explicit upper bound on the negative-part `lintegral` of the truncated W-marginal: when\x0a`c_n ≠ 0`, `B(W_n) ≤ ofReal |cbar_n · log cbar_n| + ofReal cbar_n · B(W)`, where\x0a`cbar_n := ((P.map W) (Sn n))⁻¹` and `Sn n = {r | |r| ≤ n}`. Obtained from the `negMulLog`-product\x0adecomposition of the truncated density `fn = cbar_n · 1_{Sn n} · fW` and the probability\x0anormalization `∫⁻ ofReal fW = 1`.\x0a\x0a@audit:ok ",
