  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.FisherInfo.DeBruijnHeatFlow module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Fisher information V2 — de Bruijn heat flow\x0a\x0aHeat-flow scaffolding for the general-`X` de Bruijn identity (Cover–Thomas 17.7.2's\x0adifferentiate-under-the-integral via heat equation plus integration by parts), built on the\x0adefinitions of `FisherInfo/DeBruijn.lean`. The heat equation and the integration-by-parts step\x0aare exposed as predicates that compose into the de Bruijn statement.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `heatKernel t x` — the Gaussian heat kernel `(1/√(2π t)) exp(-x²/(2t))`, defined as\x0a  `gaussianPDFReal 0 ⟨t, _⟩ x` for `t > 0` and `0` otherwise.\x0a* `IsHeatFlowDensity X Z P p` — `p` is a density family for `X + √t · Z` satisfying the heat\x0a  equation `∂_t p = (1/2) Δ_x p`, bundled in statement form.\x0a* `IsIBPHypothesis X Z P p t` — the integration-by-parts conclusion at time `t`.\x0a* `IsRegularDeBruijnHypV2.ofHeatFlow` — the constructor turning an `IsHeatFlowDensity` witness\x0a  (plus a.c. and finite-second-moment regularity of `X`) into an `IsRegularDeBruijnHypV2`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `heatKernel_nonneg` / `measurable_heatKernel` — basic regularity of the heat kernel.\x0a* `deBruijn_identity_v2_of_heat_flow` — the de Bruijn identity from `IsHeatFlowDensity` plus\x0a  `IsIBPHypothesis`.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aThe predicate split follows the Mathlib-shape rule: the heat-equation field matches the\x0aconclusion of the convolution chain rule, while the integration-by-parts field matches the\x0aconclusion expected by `HasDerivAt.congr_of_eventuallyEq`, so the two compose with\x0a`deBruijn_identity_v2` without bridging lemmas.\x0a",
