  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Gambling.Basic module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Kelly gambling and the doubling rate (Cover–Thomas Theorem 6.1.2)\x0a\x0aFor a horse race on a finite alphabet `α` with true win probabilities `p : α → ℝ`,\x0abetting fractions `b : α → ℝ`, and odds `o : α → ℝ` (payoff per unit staked on `x`),\x0athe **doubling rate** of the bet `b` is the expected log-wealth growth per race,\x0a\x0a  `W(b, o, p) = ∑ x, p x · log (b x · o x)`.\x0a\x0aThe main result is that the proportional (Kelly) bet `b = p` maximizes the doubling\x0arate, and does so uniquely.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `doublingRate` — the doubling rate `∑ x, p x · log (b x · o x)`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `doublingRate_le_proportional` — Theorem 6.1.2: `W(b, o, p) ≤ W(p, o, p)` for any\x0a  full-support bet `b`, i.e. proportional betting is optimal.\x0a* `doublingRate_eq_proportional_iff` — equality holds iff `b = p`.\x0a* `doublingRate_proportional_eq` — the optimal doubling rate in closed form,\x0a  `W(p, o, p) = ∑ x, p x · log (o x) − H(p)`.\x0a* `doublingRate_proportional_add_entropy` — the conservation law\x0a  `W(p, o, p) + H(p) = ∑ x, p x · log (o x)`.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aEverything reduces to the finite-alphabet KL divergence `klDivPmf` of\x0a`InformationTheory.Shannon.CsiszarProjection`, mirroring the maximum-entropy proof\x0a`entropy_le_gibbs_of_constraints`. The key identity is\x0a\x0a  `W(p, o, p) − W(b, o, p) = ∑ x, p x · (log (p x) − log (b x)) = klDivPmf p b ≥ 0`,\x0a\x0awhere the `log (o x)` terms cancel. Non-negativity of the gap is `klDivPmf_nonneg`,\x0aand the equality condition is `klDivPmf_eq_zero_iff_pmf`.\x0a\x0aThe argument order `klDivPmf p b` (true distribution first, bet second) is load-bearing:\x0athe log-difference and vanishing lemmas require the *second* argument to be positive,\x0awhich is provided by the full-support bet hypothesis `hb_pos`, not by `p`.\x0a\x0aPositivity of `b` is a genuine correctness precondition, not a bundling of the proof\x0acore: since Lean sets `Real.log 0 = 0`, a zero bet on a live horse (`b x = 0`, `p x > 0`)\x0awould contribute `0` instead of the true `−∞` (ruin), which would make the inequality\x0afalse. It plays the same role as the full-support reference pmf in the maximum-entropy\x0atheorems.\x0a\x0a## References\x0a\x0a* T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, *Elements of Information Theory* (2nd ed.), Wiley, 2006.\x0a  Theorem 6.1.2.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Kelly gambling and the doubling rate (Cover–Thomas Theorem 6.1.2)\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"For a horse race on a finite alphabet \"],[\"code\",[\"α\"]],[\"normal\",\" with true win probabilities \"],[\"code\",[\"p : α → ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"betting fractions \"],[\"code\",[\"b : α → ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\", and odds \"],[\"code\",[\"o : α → ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\" (payoff per unit staked on \"],[\"code\",[\"x\"]],[\"normal\",\"),\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the \"],[\"strong\",[[\"normal\",\"doubling rate\"]]],[\"normal\",\" of the bet \"],[\"code\",[\"b\"]],[\"normal\",\" is the expected log-wealth growth per race,\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"W(b, o, p) = ∑ x, p x · log (b x · o x)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The main result is that the proportional (Kelly) bet \"],[\"code\",[\"b = p\"]],[\"normal\",\" maximizes the doubling\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"rate, and does so uniquely.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main definitions\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"doublingRate\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the doubling rate \"],[\"code\",[\"∑ x, p x · log (b x · o x)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"doublingRate_le_proportional\"]],[\"normal\",\" — Theorem 6.1.2: \"],[\"code\",[\"W(b, o, p) ≤ W(p, o, p)\"]],[\"normal\",\" for any\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"full-support bet \"],[\"code\",[\"b\"]],[\"normal\",\", i.e. proportional betting is optimal.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"doublingRate_eq_proportional_iff\"]],[\"normal\",\" — equality holds iff \"],[\"code\",[\"b = p\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"doublingRate_proportional_eq\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the optimal doubling rate in closed form,\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"W(p, o, p) = ∑ x, p x · log (o x) − H(p)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"doublingRate_proportional_add_entropy\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the conservation law\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"W(p, o, p) + H(p) = ∑ x, p x · log (o x)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Implementation notes\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Everything reduces to the finite-alphabet KL divergence \"],[\"code\",[\"klDivPmf\"]],[\"normal\",\" of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"InformationTheory.Shannon.CsiszarProjection\"]],[\"normal\",\", mirroring the maximum-entropy proof\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"entropy_le_gibbs_of_constraints\"]],[\"normal\",\". The key identity is\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"W(p, o, p) − W(b, o, p) = ∑ x, p x · (log (p x) − log (b x)) = klDivPmf p b ≥ 0\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"where the \"],[\"code\",[\"log (o x)\"]],[\"normal\",\" terms cancel. Non-negativity of the gap is \"],[\"code\",[\"klDivPmf_nonneg\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"and the equality condition is \"],[\"code\",[\"klDivPmf_eq_zero_iff_pmf\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The argument order \"],[\"code\",[\"klDivPmf p b\"]],[\"normal\",\" (true distribution first, bet second) is load-bearing:\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the log-difference and vanishing lemmas require the \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"second\"]]],[\"normal\",\" argument to be positive,\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"which is provided by the full-support bet hypothesis \"],[\"code\",[\"hb_pos\"]],[\"normal\",\", not by \"],[\"code\",[\"p\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Positivity of \"],[\"code\",[\"b\"]],[\"normal\",\" is a genuine correctness precondition, not a bundling of the proof\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"core: since Lean sets \"],[\"code\",[\"Real.log 0 = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\", a zero bet on a live horse (\"],[\"code\",[\"b x = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"p x > 0\"]],[\"normal\",\")\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"would contribute \"],[\"code\",[\"0\"]],[\"normal\",\" instead of the true \"],[\"code\",[\"−∞\"]],[\"normal\",\" (ruin), which would make the inequality\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"false. It plays the same role as the full-support reference pmf in the maximum-entropy\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"theorems.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"References\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"Elements of Information Theory\"]]],[\"normal\",\" (2nd ed.), Wiley, 2006.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Theorem 6.1.2.\"]]]]]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Gambling.seqLogWealth", 8044,
