  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Han.DShearer module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Han's inequality — Shearer's inequality (integer covering form)\x0a\x0aIf `S : ι → Finset (Fin n)` covers each `i : Fin n` at least `k` times, then\x0a`k · H(X_{[n]}) ≤ ∑_j H(X_{S_j})`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `shearer_inequality` — the integer-covering Shearer inequality. The proof combines the\x0a  subset chain rule `jointEntropySubset_chain_rule`, conditional-entropy monotonicity\x0a  `condEntropy_subset_anti`, and `jointEntropySubset_univ`, then swaps the double sum to\x0a  expose the covering multiplicity `cover i := #{j | i ∈ S j} ≥ k`.\x0a",
