  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Kolmogorov.EntropyRate module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Kolmogorov complexity converges to the entropy rate\x0a\x0aFor an i.i.d. source `Xs` on a finite alphabet, the expected conditional\x0aKolmogorov complexity of a length-`n` block, normalized by `n`, converges to the\x0aentropy `H(X)` re-based to bits:\x0a\x0a`(1 / n) · E[C(X^n ∣ n)] → H(X) / log 2`.\x0a\x0aThe `/ log 2` re-bases the natural-log entropy `entropy` (`Bridge.lean`, base `e`)\x0ato the bit-length complexity `condComplexity` (base `2`).\x0a\x0aThe proof is a squeeze between an upper and a lower half. The upper half encodes\x0aa typical block by its index inside the typical set (bits `≈ n(H+ε)`) on top of\x0athe conditional literal bound; the lower half combines the counting bound\x0a`#{x ∣ C(x ∣ n) < k} < 2^k` with the strong-typicality size lower bound. This\x0afile establishes the flagship statement and the plumbing lemmas the two halves\x0aconsume.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `encodeBlock` — the base-`card α` numeral encoding a length-`m` block as `ℕ`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `kolmogorov_entropy_rate` — the flagship convergence (via the two halves).\x0a* `encodeBlock_injective` — that encoding of a block as `ℕ` is injective.\x0a* `integrable_condComplexity_jointRV` — the block-complexity integrand is integrable.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Kolmogorov complexity converges to the entropy rate\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"For an i.i.d. source \"],[\"code\",[\"Xs\"]],[\"normal\",\" on a finite alphabet, the expected conditional\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Kolmogorov complexity of a length-\"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"normal\",\" block, normalized by \"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"normal\",\", converges to the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"entropy \"],[\"code\",[\"H(X)\"]],[\"normal\",\" re-based to bits:\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"(1 / n) · E[C(X^n ∣ n)] → H(X) / log 2\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The \"],[\"code\",[\"/ log 2\"]],[\"normal\",\" re-bases the natural-log entropy \"],[\"code\",[\"entropy\"]],[\"normal\",\" (\"],[\"code\",[\"Bridge.lean\"]],[\"normal\",\", base \"],[\"code\",[\"e\"]],[\"normal\",\")\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"to the bit-length complexity \"],[\"code\",[\"condComplexity\"]],[\"normal\",\" (base \"],[\"code\",[\"2\"]],[\"normal\",\").\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The proof is a squeeze between an upper and a lower half. The upper half encodes\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"a typical block by its index inside the typical set (bits \"],[\"code\",[\"≈ n(H+ε)\"]],[\"normal\",\") on top of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the conditional literal bound; the lower half combines the counting bound\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"#{x ∣ C(x ∣ n) < k} < 2^k\"]],[\"normal\",\" with the strong-typicality size lower bound. This\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"file establishes the flagship statement and the plumbing lemmas the two halves\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"consume.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main definitions\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"encodeBlock\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the base-\"],[\"code\",[\"card α\"]],[\"normal\",\" numeral encoding a length-\"],[\"code\",[\"m\"]],[\"normal\",\" block as \"],[\"code\",[\"ℕ\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"kolmogorov_entropy_rate\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the flagship convergence (via the two halves).\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"encodeBlock_injective\"]],[\"normal\",\" — that encoding of a block as \"],[\"code\",[\"ℕ\"]],[\"normal\",\" is injective.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"integrable_condComplexity_jointRV\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the block-complexity integrand is integrable.\"]]]]]]]]"),
