  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Kolmogorov.Noncomputable module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Kolmogorov complexity is not computable\x0a\x0a`complexity` grows unboundedly (`exists_incompressible`) yet, were it computable, one\x0acould search for the least string whose complexity reaches a given bound `k`. That\x0asearch is a partial recursive description of an incompressible string using only the\x0a`natLen k` bits of `k`, so the invariance theorem bounds its complexity by\x0a`natLen k + O(1)`. Since `natLen` is the binary length and grows logarithmically, the\x0atwo facts collide: the searched string has complexity at least `k` but at most\x0a`natLen k + O(1) < k` for large `k` (Berry's paradox).\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `complexity_not_computable` — `complexity` is not a computable function.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Kolmogorov complexity is not computable\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"complexity\"]],[\"normal\",\" grows unboundedly (\"],[\"code\",[\"exists_incompressible\"]],[\"normal\",\") yet, were it computable, one\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"could search for the least string whose complexity reaches a given bound \"],[\"code\",[\"k\"]],[\"normal\",\". That\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"search is a partial recursive description of an incompressible string using only the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"natLen k\"]],[\"normal\",\" bits of \"],[\"code\",[\"k\"]],[\"normal\",\", so the invariance theorem bounds its complexity by\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"natLen k + O(1)\"]],[\"normal\",\". Since \"],[\"code\",[\"natLen\"]],[\"normal\",\" is the binary length and grows logarithmically, the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"two facts collide: the searched string has complexity at least \"],[\"code\",[\"k\"]],[\"normal\",\" but at most\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"natLen k + O(1) < k\"]],[\"normal\",\" for large \"],[\"code\",[\"k\"]],[\"normal\",\" (Berry's paradox).\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"complexity_not_computable\"]],[\"normal\",\" — \"],[\"code\",[\"complexity\"]],[\"normal\",\" is not a computable function.\"]]]]]]]]"),
