  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Kolmogorov.PrefixComputability module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Computability of the self-delimiting machine\x0a\x0aThe self-delimiting machine `prefixUniversalEval` is a partial recursive\x0afunction, and its halting set is undecidable. The first statement assembles the\x0amachine from the primitive recursive parser `parseUnary` and the partial\x0arecursive payload decoder `decodePayload`. The second reduces the halting\x0aproblem of Mathlib's universal interpreter to it along the interpret-mode entry\x0a`prefixInterpretProg`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `prefixUniversalEval_partrec` — the machine is partial recursive.\x0a* `prefixUniversalEval_dom_not_computablePred` — its halting set is undecidable.\x0a",
