  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.LZ78.AsymptoticOptimality module doc 0", 8044,
   "# LZ78 greedy-parse encoding length + asymptotic-optimality bridge\x0a\x0aThe genuine longest-prefix-match greedy LZ78 parse itself lives in\x0a`InformationTheory/Shannon/LZ78/GreedyLongestPrefix.lean` as\x0a`lz78PhraseStrings` (the ordered list of emitted phrase strings, with the\x0adistinct-phrase invariants `lz78PhraseStrings_nodup` /\x0a`lz78PhraseStrings_count_le`). This file builds the **encoding-length and\x0aparent-theorem bridge** on top of that genuine parse:\x0a\x0a* `lz78GreedyEncodingLength n x` charges `c · bitLength c |α|` bits\x0a  against the genuine distinct phrase count\x0a  `c = (lz78PhraseStrings (List.ofFn x)).length` (each of the `c` phrases\x0a  costs at most `bitLength c |α|` bits at the final dictionary size);\x0a* the Cover–Thomas Lemma 13.5.2 bit-length upper bound\x0a  `n · (log(n+1) + log|α| + 2)` holds via `c ≤ n` and\x0a  `bitLength`-monotonicity;\x0a* the encoding length plugs into the parent\x0a  `lz78_asymptotic_optimality` parameter slot, publishing the main theorem\x0a  as `lz78_asymptotic_optimality_with_greedy`.\x0a\x0aThe two a.s.-eventual halves of the sandwich are the converse lower bound and\x0athe Ziv achievability upper bound; both carry genuine ergodic content.\x0a\x0a## File layout\x0a\x0a* §1. Encoding length + parent-theorem bridge —\x0a  `lz78GreedyEncodingLength`, its distinct-phrase count bound, and the\x0a  Cover–Thomas bit-length / per-symbol-rate bounds.\x0a* §2. `IsLZ78EncodingLengthBoundPassthrough` — the\x0a  upper-bound pass-through predicate and its canonical discharge.\x0a* §3. Parent-theorem bridge — the two a.s.-eventual halves and the\x0a  `lz78_asymptotic_optimality_with_greedy` headline.\x0a\x0a## Pattern source\x0a\x0aThe per-phrase bit cost is reused from `LZ78/GreedyParsing.lean`\x0a(`LZ78Phrase.bitLength`); the parent-theorem bridge instantiates the\x0ageneric sandwich combinator `lz78_asymptotic_optimality` with the\x0agenuine greedy encoding length and discharges its two a.s.-eventual\x0ahalves.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"LZ78 greedy-parse encoding length + asymptotic-optimality bridge\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The genuine longest-prefix-match greedy LZ78 parse itself lives in\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"InformationTheory/Shannon/LZ78/GreedyLongestPrefix.lean\"]],[\"normal\",\" as\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"lz78PhraseStrings\"]],[\"normal\",\" (the ordered list of emitted phrase strings, with the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"distinct-phrase invariants \"],[\"code\",[\"lz78PhraseStrings_nodup\"]],[\"normal\",\" /\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"lz78PhraseStrings_count_le\"]],[\"normal\",\"). This file builds the \"],[\"strong\",[[\"normal\",\"encoding-length and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"parent-theorem bridge\"]]],[\"normal\",\" on top of that genuine parse:\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"lz78GreedyEncodingLength n x\"]],[\"normal\",\" charges \"],[\"code\",[\"c · bitLength c |α|\"]],[\"normal\",\" bits\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"against the genuine distinct phrase count\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"c = (lz78PhraseStrings (List.ofFn x)).length\"]],[\"normal\",\" (each of the \"],[\"code\",[\"c\"]],[\"normal\",\" phrases\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"costs at most \"],[\"code\",[\"bitLength c |α|\"]],[\"normal\",\" bits at the final dictionary size);\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"the Cover–Thomas Lemma 13.5.2 bit-length upper bound\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"n · (log(n+1) + log|α| + 2)\"]],[\"normal\",\" holds via \"],[\"code\",[\"c ≤ n\"]],[\"normal\",\" and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"bitLength\"]],[\"normal\",\"-monotonicity;\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"the encoding length plugs into the parent\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"lz78_asymptotic_optimality\"]],[\"normal\",\" parameter slot, publishing the main theorem\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"as \"],[\"code\",[\"lz78_asymptotic_optimality_with_greedy\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The two a.s.-eventual halves of the sandwich are the converse lower bound and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the Ziv achievability upper bound; both carry genuine ergodic content.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"File layout\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"§1. Encoding length + parent-theorem bridge —\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"lz78GreedyEncodingLength\"]],[\"normal\",\", its distinct-phrase count bound, and the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Cover–Thomas bit-length / per-symbol-rate bounds.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"§2. \"],[\"code\",[\"IsLZ78EncodingLengthBoundPassthrough\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"upper-bound pass-through predicate and its canonical discharge.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"§3. Parent-theorem bridge — the two a.s.-eventual halves and the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"lz78_asymptotic_optimality_with_greedy\"]],[\"normal\",\" headline.\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Pattern source\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The per-phrase bit cost is reused from \"],[\"code\",[\"LZ78/GreedyParsing.lean\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(\"],[\"code\",[\"LZ78Phrase.bitLength\"]],[\"normal\",\"); the parent-theorem bridge instantiates the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"generic sandwich combinator \"],[\"code\",[\"lz78_asymptotic_optimality\"]],[\"normal\",\" with the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"genuine greedy encoding length and discharges its two a.s.-eventual\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"halves.\"]]]]"),
