   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Factorial-power decay \"],[\"code\",[\"c! · 2^c ≤ (c+1)^c\"]],[\"normal\",\" (real form). The per-\"],[\"code\",[\"c\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"structure-Kraft term \"],[\"code\",[\"c!/(c+1)^c\"]],[\"normal\",\" is geometrically small. Proved by induction;\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the step uses Bernoulli \"],[\"code\",[\"2·(c+1)^(c+1) ≤ (c+2)^(c+1)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.LZ78Parsing.inRange", 8044,
   "Structural invariant: every parent reference points to an earlier\x0aphrase index. The invariant is stated via `List.get ⟨i, h⟩` (the\x0atotal bounded-index accessor) so that the back-pointer constraint\x0a`parent_i = some k → k < i` is captured at the type level. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Structural invariant: every parent reference points to an earlier\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"phrase index. The invariant is stated via \"],[\"code\",[\"List.get ⟨i, h⟩\"]],[\"normal\",\" (the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"total bounded-index accessor) so that the back-pointer constraint\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"parent_i = some k → k < i\"]],[\"normal\",\" is captured at the type level.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.LZ78.ConverseAsymptotic module doc 0", 8044,
   "# LZ78 converse — asymptotic body extension\x0a\x0aThis file publishes the asymptotic-body layer on top of the\x0acombinatorial `ZivCountingBound` predicate already published in\x0a`InformationTheory/Shannon/LZ78/ZivInequality.lean`. It is a *predicate-level*\x0aextension: the per-`n` real-valued bound `(p.count : ℝ) ≤ B` is lifted\x0ato families `(p : ℕ → LZ78Parsing α)` indexed by the block length, and\x0athe asymptotic shape `c(n) · log c(n) ≤ n · log b + O(1)` (Cover–Thomas\x0aEq. 13.124, the Ziv-counting asymptotic) is exposed as a hypothesis\x0apass-through `IsLZ78PhraseCountAsymptotic` that future discharges can\x0aplug in. The genuine a.s. achievability residual is scoped out as\x0a`lz78Greedy_achievability_ae` in `AsymptoticOptimality.lean`.\x0a\x0a## Scope\x0a\x0a* (engaged) — `IsLZ78PhraseCountAsymptotic` predicate\x0a  shaped on `Asymptotics.IsBigO atTop`, plus a `.trivial` constructor.\x0a* (engaged) — `IsZivCountingAsymptoticBound` per-`n`\x0a  bound aggregator with `.refl`, `.mono`, `.add_nonneg`, and\x0a  `.of_pointwise_count` constructors.\x0a* (engaged) — bridge theorems showing how a uniform\x0a  per-`n` Ziv counting bound implies the asymptotic predicate.\x0a* (deferred) — the *concrete* derivation of\x0a  `c(n) ≤ n / log_b n · (1 + o(1))` from Cover–Thomas Eq. 13.122–13.124\x0a  is supplied as hypothesis; the numerical asymptotic\x0a  `c(n) · log c(n) − n · log b = o(n)` is the Cover–Thomas Lemma 13.5.5\x0a  body and remains out of scope here.\x0a\x0a## Pattern source\x0a\x0aFollows the same \"predicate + .trivial + bridge\" pattern as\x0a`ZivInequality.lean`. The asymptotic\x0alayer is wrapped in `Asymptotics.IsBigO` notation so downstream callers can\x0aplug `Mathlib.Analysis.Asymptotics` lemmas directly without re-shaping.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"LZ78 converse — asymptotic body extension\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"This file publishes the asymptotic-body layer on top of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"combinatorial \"],[\"code\",[\"ZivCountingBound\"]],[\"normal\",\" predicate already published in\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"InformationTheory/Shannon/LZ78/ZivInequality.lean\"]],[\"normal\",\". It is a \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"predicate-level\"]]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"extension: the per-\"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"normal\",\" real-valued bound \"],[\"code\",[\"(p.count : ℝ) ≤ B\"]],[\"normal\",\" is lifted\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"to families \"],[\"code\",[\"(p : ℕ → LZ78Parsing α)\"]],[\"normal\",\" indexed by the block length, and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the asymptotic shape \"],[\"code\",[\"c(n) · log c(n) ≤ n · log b + O(1)\"]],[\"normal\",\" (Cover–Thomas\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Eq. 13.124, the Ziv-counting asymptotic) is exposed as a hypothesis\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"pass-through \"],[\"code\",[\"IsLZ78PhraseCountAsymptotic\"]],[\"normal\",\" that future discharges can\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"plug in. The genuine a.s. achievability residual is scoped out as\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"lz78Greedy_achievability_ae\"]],[\"normal\",\" in \"],[\"code\",[\"AsymptoticOptimality.lean\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Scope\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"(engaged) — \"],[\"code\",[\"IsLZ78PhraseCountAsymptotic\"]],[\"normal\",\" predicate\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"shaped on \"],[\"code\",[\"Asymptotics.IsBigO atTop\"]],[\"normal\",\", plus a \"],[\"code\",[\".trivial\"]],[\"normal\",\" constructor.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"(engaged) — \"],[\"code\",[\"IsZivCountingAsymptoticBound\"]],[\"normal\",\" per-\"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"bound aggregator with \"],[\"code\",[\".refl\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\".mono\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\".add_nonneg\"]],[\"normal\",\", and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\".of_pointwise_count\"]],[\"normal\",\" constructors.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"(engaged) — bridge theorems showing how a uniform\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"per-\"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"normal\",\" Ziv counting bound implies the asymptotic predicate.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"(deferred) — the \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"concrete\"]]],[\"normal\",\" derivation of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"c(n) ≤ n / log_b n · (1 + o(1))\"]],[\"normal\",\" from Cover–Thomas Eq. 13.122–13.124\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"is supplied as hypothesis; the numerical asymptotic\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"c(n) · log c(n) − n · log b = o(n)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is the Cover–Thomas Lemma 13.5.5\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"body and remains out of scope here.\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Pattern source\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Follows the same \\\"predicate + .trivial + bridge\\\" pattern as\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"ZivInequality.lean\"]],[\"normal\",\". The asymptotic\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"layer is wrapped in \"],[\"code\",[\"Asymptotics.IsBigO\"]],[\"normal\",\" notation so downstream callers can\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"plug \"],[\"code\",[\"Mathlib.Analysis.Asymptotics\"]],[\"normal\",\" lemmas directly without re-shaping.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.IsLZ78PhraseCountAsymptotic", 8044,
   "The asymptotic phrase-count predicate.\x0a\x0aFor a family of LZ78 parsings `p : ℕ → LZ78Parsing α` and a reference\x0aenvelope function `B : ℕ → ℝ` (in the textbook this is\x0a`n ↦ n / Real.log n` or similar), this predicate asserts that the\x0aphrase-count sequence `n ↦ ((p n).count : ℝ)` is `O[atTop]` of `B`.\x0a\x0aCover–Thomas Eq. 13.124 reads\x0a`c(n) ≤ n / log_b(c(n)) ≤ n / log_b n · (1 + o(1))`,\x0aand this predicate captures exactly the `IsBigO` half: the\x0a`(1 + o(1))` slack is absorbed into the constant of `IsBigO`. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The asymptotic phrase-count predicate.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"For a family of LZ78 parsings \"],[\"code\",[\"p : ℕ → LZ78Parsing α\"]],[\"normal\",\" and a reference\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"envelope function \"],[\"code\",[\"B : ℕ → ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\" (in the textbook this is\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"n ↦ n / Real.log n\"]],[\"normal\",\" or similar), this predicate asserts that the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"phrase-count sequence \"],[\"code\",[\"n ↦ ((p n).count : ℝ)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is \"],[\"code\",[\"O[atTop]\"]],[\"normal\",\" of \"],[\"code\",[\"B\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Cover–Thomas Eq. 13.124 reads\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"c(n) ≤ n / log_b(c(n)) ≤ n / log_b n · (1 + o(1))\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"and this predicate captures exactly the \"],[\"code\",[\"IsBigO\"]],[\"normal\",\" half: the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"(1 + o(1))\"]],[\"normal\",\" slack is absorbed into the constant of \"],[\"code\",[\"IsBigO\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.IsLZ78PhraseCountSandwich", 8044,
   "Combine an upper-bound predicate\x0a`IsLZ78PhraseCountAsymptotic p B_upper` and a lower-bound predicate\x0a`B_lower =O[atTop] (p.count)` (i.e. the phrase count *dominates*\x0a`B_lower`) into a sandwich. This is the predicate-level analogue of the\x0aCover–Thomas Eq. 13.124 ⟺ Eq. 13.130 sandwich. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Combine an upper-bound predicate\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"IsLZ78PhraseCountAsymptotic p B_upper\"]],[\"normal\",\" and a lower-bound predicate\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"B_lower =O[atTop] (p.count)\"]],[\"normal\",\" (i.e. the phrase count \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"dominates\"]]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"B_lower\"]],[\"normal\",\") into a sandwich. This is the predicate-level analogue of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Cover–Thomas Eq. 13.124 ⟺ Eq. 13.130 sandwich.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.lz78TokenCode_entropyD_le_expectedLength", 8044,
   "The expectation-level source-coding converse for the LZ78 token code.\x0a\x0aFor any probability measure `P` (full support) on the LZ78 token alphabet, the\x0abinary entropy is bounded by the (constant) token code length:\x0a\x0a```\x0aentropyD 2 P ≤ E[L] = bitLength c |α|.\x0a```\x0a\x0aThis is the Cover–Thomas 5.4 converse, instantiated at the LZ78\x0a`(parent, symbol)` token code via the McMillan bridge. The block-rate form\x0a(Cover–Thomas Eq. 13.130, `lz78Greedy_converse_ae`) needs the averaged ⟶ a.s.\x0alift and is not addressed here. ",
