  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.MaxEntropyConstrainedKKT.expFamilyDist", 8044,
   "Exponential family pmf, Lagrangian / KKT-canonical form:\x0a\x0aexpFamilyDist λ f x := exp (⟨λ, f x⟩ - ψ(λ))\x0a\x0awhere `⟨λ, f x⟩ = ∑ i, λ i · f i x`. This is the saddle-point optimizer of the\x0aLagrangian `L(p, λ) = H(p) + ∑ i, λ i (𝔼_p[f i] - c i)`. By\x0a`expFamilyDist_eq_gibbsPmf` it agrees pointwise with `gibbsPmf f λ`, so all\x0apositivity / pmf properties transfer. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Exponential family pmf, Lagrangian / KKT-canonical form:\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"expFamilyDist λ f x := exp (⟨λ, f x⟩ - ψ(λ))\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"where \"],[\"code\",[\"⟨λ, f x⟩ = ∑ i, λ i · f i x\"]],[\"normal\",\". This is the saddle-point optimizer of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Lagrangian \"],[\"code\",[\"L(p, λ) = H(p) + ∑ i, λ i (𝔼_p[f i] - c i)\"]],[\"normal\",\". By\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"expFamilyDist_eq_gibbsPmf\"]],[\"normal\",\" it agrees pointwise with \"],[\"code\",[\"gibbsPmf f λ\"]],[\"normal\",\", so all\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"positivity / pmf properties transfer.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.MaxEntropyConstrainedKKT.entropy_expFamilyDist_eq_legendre", 8044,
   "Legendre / saddle-point identity for the exponential family. With KKT\x0asolution `(λ, moment_match)` for constraints `c`, the entropy of the\x0aexponential-family optimum has the closed form\x0a\x0aH(p*) = ψ(λ) - ⟨λ, c⟩.\x0a\x0aThis is the KKT duality: at the saddle point of the Lagrangian, the primal value\x0aequals the dual value `ψ(λ) - ⟨λ, c⟩`. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Legendre / saddle-point identity for the exponential family. With KKT\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"solution \"],[\"code\",[\"(λ, moment_match)\"]],[\"normal\",\" for constraints \"],[\"code\",[\"c\"]],[\"normal\",\", the entropy of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"exponential-family optimum has the closed form\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"H(p*) = ψ(λ) - ⟨λ, c⟩.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"This is the KKT duality: at the saddle point of the Lagrangian, the primal value\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"equals the dual value \"],[\"code\",[\"ψ(λ) - ⟨λ, c⟩\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ShannonCode.zpow_neg_natCast_eq_one_div_pow", 8044,
