  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.MultipleAccess.Converse module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Multiple access channel — converse (outer bound)\x0a\x0aThe converse to the MAC coding theorem (Cover–Thomas Thm 15.3.1, eq. 15.85–15.90):\x0afor uniformly distributed, independent messages decoded by a joint decoder, the rate pair\x0asatisfies the three corner-point inequalities of `InMACCapacityRegion`.\x0a\x0aEach of the three bounds is the **message-level Fano converse**, obtained from the\x0aencoder-free single-shot converse `shannon_converse_single_shot` by placing the\x0aconditioning message in the *output* slot:\x0a\x0a* user 1: `log |M₁| ≤ I(M₁; (M₂, Yⁿ)) + h(Pe₁) + Pe₁ log(|M₁| − 1)`\x0a* user 2: `log |M₂| ≤ I(M₂; (M₁, Yⁿ)) + h(Pe₂) + Pe₂ log(|M₂| − 1)`\x0a* sum:    `log |M₁| + log |M₂| ≤ I((M₁, M₂); Yⁿ) + h(Pe) + Pe log(|M₁·M₂| − 1)`\x0a\x0aHere `I(M₁; (M₂, Yⁿ)) = I(M₁; Yⁿ | M₂)` under message independence, the standard converse\x0aintermediate. Single-letterizing these bounds to the per-letter channel quantities\x0a`I(X₁; Y | X₂)` etc. is carried out in the second half of the file.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `mac_converse_bound₁` / `mac_converse_bound₂` / `mac_converse_bound_sum` — the three\x0a  corner-point inequalities.\x0a* `mac_converse_message_level` — the packaged `InMACCapacityRegion` outer bound.\x0a* `mac_converse` — the single-letterized outer bound, whose information slots are the\x0a  per-letter channel sums `∑ᵢ I(X₁ᵢ; Yᵢ | X₂ᵢ)` etc.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Multiple access channel — converse (outer bound)\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The converse to the MAC coding theorem (Cover–Thomas Thm 15.3.1, eq. 15.85–15.90):\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"for uniformly distributed, independent messages decoded by a joint decoder, the rate pair\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"satisfies the three corner-point inequalities of \"],[\"code\",[\"InMACCapacityRegion\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Each of the three bounds is the \"],[\"strong\",[[\"normal\",\"message-level Fano converse\"]]],[\"normal\",\", obtained from the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"encoder-free single-shot converse \"],[\"code\",[\"shannon_converse_single_shot\"]],[\"normal\",\" by placing the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"conditioning message in the \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"output\"]]],[\"normal\",\" slot:\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"user 1: \"],[\"code\",[\"log |M₁| ≤ I(M₁; (M₂, Yⁿ)) + h(Pe₁) + Pe₁ log(|M₁| − 1)\"]]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"user 2: \"],[\"code\",[\"log |M₂| ≤ I(M₂; (M₁, Yⁿ)) + h(Pe₂) + Pe₂ log(|M₂| − 1)\"]]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"sum:    \"],[\"code\",[\"log |M₁| + log |M₂| ≤ I((M₁, M₂); Yⁿ) + h(Pe) + Pe log(|M₁·M₂| − 1)\"]]]]]]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Here \"],[\"code\",[\"I(M₁; (M₂, Yⁿ)) = I(M₁; Yⁿ | M₂)\"]],[\"normal\",\" under message independence, the standard converse\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"intermediate. Single-letterizing these bounds to the per-letter channel quantities\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"I(X₁; Y | X₂)\"]],[\"normal\",\" etc. is carried out in the second half of the file.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"mac_converse_bound₁\"]],[\"normal\",\" / \"],[\"code\",[\"mac_converse_bound₂\"]],[\"normal\",\" / \"],[\"code\",[\"mac_converse_bound_sum\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the three\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"corner-point inequalities.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"mac_converse_message_level\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the packaged \"],[\"code\",[\"InMACCapacityRegion\"]],[\"normal\",\" outer bound.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"mac_converse\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the single-letterized outer bound, whose information slots are the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"per-letter channel sums \"],[\"code\",[\"∑ᵢ I(X₁ᵢ; Yᵢ | X₂ᵢ)\"]],[\"normal\",\" etc.\"]]]]]]]]"),
