   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The per-coordinate MAC joint law on \"],[\"code\",[\"α₁ × α₂ × β\"]],[\"normal\",\": the channel-coding joint\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"(p₁ ⊗ p₂) ⊗ₘ W\"]],[\"normal\",\" on \"],[\"code\",[\"(α₁ × α₂) × β\"]],[\"normal\",\" reshaped to the right-nested triple.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.MultipleAccess.Reconciliation module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Multiple access channel — converse/achievability reconciliation bridge\x0a\x0aUnder the independent product input `p₁ ⊗ p₂`, the achievability rate quantities\x0a`macInfo₁` / `macInfo₂` / `macInfoBoth` (entropy differences, `ℝ`-valued) of\x0a`InformationTheory.Shannon.MultipleAccess.Achievability` coincide with the converse\x0ainformation quantities (`condMutualInfo` / `mutualInfo`, `klDiv`-based, `ℝ≥0∞`-valued)\x0ataken on the per-coordinate joint law `macJointDistribution p₁ p₂ W`:\x0a\x0a* `macInfo₁ = (I(X₁; Y | X₂))` ,\x0a* `macInfo₂ = (I(X₂; Y | X₁))` ,\x0a* `macInfoBoth = (I((X₁, X₂); Y))` .\x0a\x0aThe crux is that the input coordinates `X₁`, `X₂` are independent under `p₁ ⊗ p₂`, so the\x0achain rule `I(X₁; (X₂, Y)) = I(X₁; Y | X₂)` (and its user-2 mirror) closes the gap between\x0athe achievability corner informations and the textbook conditional informations of the\x0aMAC capacity region.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `macInfo₁_eq_condMutualInfo_toReal` / `macInfo₂_eq_condMutualInfo_toReal` /\x0a  `macInfoBoth_eq_mutualInfo_toReal` — the three corner-information equivalences.\x0a* `mac_capacity_region_reconciliation` — the achievability-region predicate equals the\x0a  converse-region predicate after substituting the three equivalences.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Multiple access channel — converse/achievability reconciliation bridge\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Under the independent product input \"],[\"code\",[\"p₁ ⊗ p₂\"]],[\"normal\",\", the achievability rate quantities\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"macInfo₁\"]],[\"normal\",\" / \"],[\"code\",[\"macInfo₂\"]],[\"normal\",\" / \"],[\"code\",[\"macInfoBoth\"]],[\"normal\",\" (entropy differences, \"],[\"code\",[\"ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\"-valued) of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"InformationTheory.Shannon.MultipleAccess.Achievability\"]],[\"normal\",\" coincide with the converse\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"information quantities (\"],[\"code\",[\"condMutualInfo\"]],[\"normal\",\" / \"],[\"code\",[\"mutualInfo\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"klDiv\"]],[\"normal\",\"-based, \"],[\"code\",[\"ℝ≥0∞\"]],[\"normal\",\"-valued)\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"taken on the per-coordinate joint law \"],[\"code\",[\"macJointDistribution p₁ p₂ W\"]],[\"normal\",\":\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"macInfo₁ = (I(X₁; Y | X₂))\"]],[\"normal\",\" ,\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"macInfo₂ = (I(X₂; Y | X₁))\"]],[\"normal\",\" ,\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"macInfoBoth = (I((X₁, X₂); Y))\"]],[\"normal\",\" .\"]]]]]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The crux is that the input coordinates \"],[\"code\",[\"X₁\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"X₂\"]],[\"normal\",\" are independent under \"],[\"code\",[\"p₁ ⊗ p₂\"]],[\"normal\",\", so the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"chain rule \"],[\"code\",[\"I(X₁; (X₂, Y)) = I(X₁; Y | X₂)\"]],[\"normal\",\" (and its user-2 mirror) closes the gap between\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the achievability corner informations and the textbook conditional informations of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"MAC capacity region.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"macInfo₁_eq_condMutualInfo_toReal\"]],[\"normal\",\" / \"],[\"code\",[\"macInfo₂_eq_condMutualInfo_toReal\"]],[\"normal\",\" /\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"macInfoBoth_eq_mutualInfo_toReal\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the three corner-information equivalences.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"mac_capacity_region_reconciliation\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the achievability-region predicate equals the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"converse-region predicate after substituting the three equivalences.\"]]]]]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.MultipleAccess.TimeSharing module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Multiple access channel — time-sharing achievability (full convex-hull form)\x0a\x0aOperational time-sharing for the two-user MAC (Cover–Thomas Theorem 15.3.1, convex-hull\x0aform).  The single-input corner-point achievability `mac_achievability` is the input; this\x0afile lifts it to the convex hull of the per-input pentagons via block concatenation.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `MACAchievable W R₁ R₂` — the operational achievability predicate for the rate pair\x0a  `(R₁, R₂)`: for every target error `ε' > 0`, eventually (in the block length `n`) there is\x0a  a length-`n` two-user code with at least `⌈exp (n R₁)⌉` / `⌈exp (n R₂)⌉` messages per user\x0a  and average error probability `< ε'`.  This is exactly the conclusion of\x0a  `mac_achievability`, abstracted over `ε'`.\x0a* `macPentagon p₁ p₂ W` — the corner-point pentagon of the independent product input\x0a  `p₁ ⊗ p₂`: rate pairs bounded by `macInfo₁`, `macInfo₂`, `macInfoBoth`.\x0a* `macCapacityRegion W` — the operational capacity region, the topological closure of the\x0a  achievable set.  (The exact-rate achievable set is not closed — boundary Pareto faces\x0a  enter only in the closure — so the region is defined as its closure.)\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `mac_achievability_region` — the closed convex hull of the pentagons of the full-support\x0a  product inputs is contained in the operational capacity region.\x0a* `mac_achievability_region_allprob` — the same inclusion for the pentagons of *all*\x0a  probability product inputs, obtained by smoothing an arbitrary input toward a uniform\x0a  anchor and passing to the limit.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Multiple access channel — time-sharing achievability (full convex-hull form)\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Operational time-sharing for the two-user MAC (Cover–Thomas Theorem 15.3.1, convex-hull\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"form).  The single-input corner-point achievability \"],[\"code\",[\"mac_achievability\"]],[\"normal\",\" is the input; this\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"file lifts it to the convex hull of the per-input pentagons via block concatenation.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main definitions\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"MACAchievable W R₁ R₂\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the operational achievability predicate for the rate pair\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"(R₁, R₂)\"]],[\"normal\",\": for every target error \"],[\"code\",[\"ε' > 0\"]],[\"normal\",\", eventually (in the block length \"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"normal\",\") there is\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"a length-\"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"normal\",\" two-user code with at least \"],[\"code\",[\"⌈exp (n R₁)⌉\"]],[\"normal\",\" / \"],[\"code\",[\"⌈exp (n R₂)⌉\"]],[\"normal\",\" messages per user\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"and average error probability \"],[\"code\",[\"< ε'\"]],[\"normal\",\".  This is exactly the conclusion of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"mac_achievability\"]],[\"normal\",\", abstracted over \"],[\"code\",[\"ε'\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"macPentagon p₁ p₂ W\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the corner-point pentagon of the independent product input\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"p₁ ⊗ p₂\"]],[\"normal\",\": rate pairs bounded by \"],[\"code\",[\"macInfo₁\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"macInfo₂\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"macInfoBoth\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"macCapacityRegion W\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the operational capacity region, the topological closure of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"achievable set.  (The exact-rate achievable set is not closed — boundary Pareto faces\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"enter only in the closure — so the region is defined as its closure.)\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"mac_achievability_region\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the closed convex hull of the pentagons of the full-support\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"product inputs is contained in the operational capacity region.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"mac_achievability_region_allprob\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the same inclusion for the pentagons of \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"all\"]]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"probability product inputs, obtained by smoothing an arbitrary input toward a uniform\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"anchor and passing to the limit.\"]]]]]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.MAC.mac_mem_closure_of_strictly_below", 8044,
