  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.MAC.mac_converse_from_code", 8044,
   "The MAC converse instantiated at a bare code: for any two-user MAC block code `c` and\x0aMarkov channel `W`, the canonical ambient measure `macConverseAmbient c W` discharges every\x0ahypothesis of the floating converse `mac_converse`, so the rate pair `(log M₁, log M₂)` lies\x0ain the corner-point region determined by the per-letter conditional and joint mutual\x0ainformations.  The Fano slack is still carried here; it vanishes only in the `n → ∞` limit.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The MAC converse instantiated at a bare code: for any two-user MAC block code \"],[\"code\",[\"c\"]],[\"normal\",\" and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Markov channel \"],[\"code\",[\"W\"]],[\"normal\",\", the canonical ambient measure \"],[\"code\",[\"macConverseAmbient c W\"]],[\"normal\",\" discharges every\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"hypothesis of the floating converse \"],[\"code\",[\"mac_converse\"]],[\"normal\",\", so the rate pair \"],[\"code\",[\"(log M₁, log M₂)\"]],[\"normal\",\" lies\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"in the corner-point region determined by the per-letter conditional and joint mutual\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"informations.  The Fano slack is still carried here; it vanishes only in the \"],[\"code\",[\"n → ∞\"]],[\"normal\",\" limit.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.pi_withDensity_fin", 8044,
   "`pi_withDensity` (Mathlib absent, built by `piFinSuccAbove` induction).\x0aThe product measure of `withDensity` factors is the `withDensity` of the product\x0ameasure with the product density `z ↦ ∏ᵢ fᵢ (z i)`. Specialized to `Fin n → ℝ`\x0a(all factors on `ℝ`), the form the `n`-variable density split requires.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"pi_withDensity\"]],[\"normal\",\" (Mathlib absent, built by \"],[\"code\",[\"piFinSuccAbove\"]],[\"normal\",\" induction).\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"The product measure of \"],[\"code\",[\"withDensity\"]],[\"normal\",\" factors is the \"],[\"code\",[\"withDensity\"]],[\"normal\",\" of the product\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"measure with the product density \"],[\"code\",[\"z ↦ ∏ᵢ fᵢ (z i)\"]],[\"normal\",\". Specialized to \"],[\"code\",[\"Fin n → ℝ\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(all factors on \"],[\"code\",[\"ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\"), the form the \"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"normal\",\"-variable density split requires.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.llr_split_from_density_factorize", 8044,
   "Log-likelihood ratio split for the 2-variable joint (a.e.[μ]).\x0a\x0aThe LLR of `μ` against the product of its marginals equals\x0a`log(joint density) − log(marginal_X density on z.1) − log(marginal_Y density on z.2)`\x0aalmost-everywhere wrt `μ`. ",
