  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ParallelGaussian.Converse module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Parallel Gaussian converse (correlated input)\x0a\x0aThe converse pieces feeding the `bddAbove` and `max_ent` fields of the regularity bundle\x0a`IsParallelGaussianPerCoordRegularity`, lifting the single-coordinate AWGN converse to the\x0a`Fin n → ℝ` parallel channel.\x0a\x0aThe supporting development lives in the `Converse.*` submodules:\x0a\x0a* `Converse.Core` — the channel↔RV mutual-information decomposition lift\x0a  (`parallel_mutualInfoOfChannel_toReal_eq_diffEntropyPi_sub`) and the product-measure\x0a  absolute-continuity / entropy helpers.\x0a* `Converse.Regularity` — the correlated-output regularity preconditions (absolute\x0a  continuity, marginal-as-convolution, log-density integrabilities).\x0a* `Converse.MixtureDensity` — the joint mixture output density, the per-input max-entropy\x0a  split `parallel_per_input_mi_le_sum`, and the boundedness reduction\x0a  `parallel_bddAbove_miImage`.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aThe per-input bound `parallel_per_input_mi_le_sum` requires `0 ≤ P`: the constraint set is\x0anon-empty for `P < 0` (it contains the Dirac at 0, since `ENNReal.ofReal P = 0`), yet\x0a`∑ P'ᵢ ≤ P < 0` with `P'ᵢ ≥ 0` is unsatisfiable, so the statement would be false there. The\x0aconstraint is threaded from the headline `parallel_gaussian_capacity_formula_minimal`.\x0a",
