  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Pinsker.Basic module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Pinsker's inequality (total variation and Kullback–Leibler divergence)\x0a\x0aFor probability measures `P, Q` on a finite alphabet `α` with `P ≪ Q`, the total-variation\x0anorm `tvNorm P Q := (1/2) * ∑ x, |P.real {x} - Q.real {x}|` is bounded by the square root of\x0athe Kullback–Leibler divergence: `tvNorm P Q ≤ √((klDiv P Q).toReal)`.\x0a\x0aThis is the weak form with constant `1`; the sharp Cover–Thomas (11.6) form\x0a`tvNorm P Q ≤ √((klDiv P Q).toReal / 2)` is proved separately in `Pinsker/Sharp.lean`.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `tvNorm` — the total-variation norm between two probability measures on a finite alphabet.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `klFun_ge_sub_sqrt_sq` — the pointwise Bretagnolle–Huber bound `(√t - 1)^2 ≤ klFun t`.\x0a* `tvNorm_le_sqrt_klDiv` — Pinsker's inequality (weak form) `tvNorm P Q ≤ √((klDiv P Q).toReal)`.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aThe proof combines the pointwise Bretagnolle–Huber bound `klFun t ≥ (√t - 1)^2` with the\x0aCauchy–Schwarz factorization `|p - q| = |√p - √q| · (√p + √q)`, bounding `∑ (√p + √q)^2 ≤ 4`.\x0a\x0a## References\x0a\x0a* T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, *Elements of Information Theory* (2nd ed.),\x0a  Wiley, 2006. Section 11.6.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Pinsker's inequality (total variation and Kullback–Leibler divergence)\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"For probability measures \"],[\"code\",[\"P, Q\"]],[\"normal\",\" on a finite alphabet \"],[\"code\",[\"α\"]],[\"normal\",\" with \"],[\"code\",[\"P ≪ Q\"]],[\"normal\",\", the total-variation\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"norm \"],[\"code\",[\"tvNorm P Q := (1/2) * ∑ x, |P.real {x} - Q.real {x}|\"]],[\"normal\",\" is bounded by the square root of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the Kullback–Leibler divergence: \"],[\"code\",[\"tvNorm P Q ≤ √((klDiv P Q).toReal)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"This is the weak form with constant \"],[\"code\",[\"1\"]],[\"normal\",\"; the sharp Cover–Thomas (11.6) form\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"tvNorm P Q ≤ √((klDiv P Q).toReal / 2)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is proved separately in \"],[\"code\",[\"Pinsker/Sharp.lean\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main definitions\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"tvNorm\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the total-variation norm between two probability measures on a finite alphabet.\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"klFun_ge_sub_sqrt_sq\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the pointwise Bretagnolle–Huber bound \"],[\"code\",[\"(√t - 1)^2 ≤ klFun t\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"tvNorm_le_sqrt_klDiv\"]],[\"normal\",\" — Pinsker's inequality (weak form) \"],[\"code\",[\"tvNorm P Q ≤ √((klDiv P Q).toReal)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Implementation notes\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The proof combines the pointwise Bretagnolle–Huber bound \"],[\"code\",[\"klFun t ≥ (√t - 1)^2\"]],[\"normal\",\" with the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Cauchy–Schwarz factorization \"],[\"code\",[\"|p - q| = |√p - √q| · (√p + √q)\"]],[\"normal\",\", bounding \"],[\"code\",[\"∑ (√p + √q)^2 ≤ 4\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"References\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"Elements of Information Theory\"]]],[\"normal\",\" (2nd ed.),\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Wiley, 2006. Section 11.6.\"]]]]]]]]"),
