  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Portfolio.seqLogWealth_div_tendsto_growthRate", 8044,
   "Operational log-optimal portfolio theorem (Cover–Thomas §16.3): for an i.i.d.\x0amarket sequence `As`, a fixed rebalanced portfolio `b` under price relatives `X`, the\x0atime-averaged log-wealth growth `(1/n)·log S_n` converges almost surely to the growth rate\x0a`growthRate (lawPmf μ (As 0)) X b`, where `lawPmf μ (As 0)` is the law of a single\x0aoutcome.\x0a@audit:ok — sorryAx-free (`[propext, Classical.choice,\x0aQuot.sound]`). `lawPmf μ (As 0)` is a genuine definitional binding (pushforward law of\x0a`As 0`), not a bundled `(h : μ[…] = growthRate …)` slot. `hAs`/`hindep`/`hident` and\x0a`[IsProbabilityMeasure μ]` are the SLLN regularity preconditions. Routes through\x0a`strong_law_ae_real` + the expectation→pmf bridge `integral_comp_law`; non-circular. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Operational log-optimal portfolio theorem (Cover–Thomas §16.3): for an i.i.d.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"market sequence \"],[\"code\",[\"As\"]],[\"normal\",\", a fixed rebalanced portfolio \"],[\"code\",[\"b\"]],[\"normal\",\" under price relatives \"],[\"code\",[\"X\"]],[\"normal\",\", the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"time-averaged log-wealth growth \"],[\"code\",[\"(1/n)·log S_n\"]],[\"normal\",\" converges almost surely to the growth rate\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"growthRate (lawPmf μ (As 0)) X b\"]],[\"normal\",\", where \"],[\"code\",[\"lawPmf μ (As 0)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is the law of a single\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"outcome.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok — sorryAx-free (\"],[\"code\",[\"[propext, Classical.choice,\",\" \",\"Quot.sound]\"]],[\"normal\",\"). \"],[\"code\",[\"lawPmf μ (As 0)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is a genuine definitional binding (pushforward law of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"As 0\"]],[\"normal\",\"), not a bundled \"],[\"code\",[\"(h : μ[…] = growthRate …)\"]],[\"normal\",\" slot. \"],[\"code\",[\"hAs\"]],[\"normal\",\"/\"],[\"code\",[\"hindep\"]],[\"normal\",\"/\"],[\"code\",[\"hident\"]],[\"normal\",\" and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"[IsProbabilityMeasure μ]\"]],[\"normal\",\" are the SLLN regularity preconditions. Routes through\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"strong_law_ae_real\"]],[\"normal\",\" + the expectation→pmf bridge \"],[\"code\",[\"integral_comp_law\"]],[\"normal\",\"; non-circular.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Portfolio.StationaryWinfty module doc 1", 8044,
   "## Monotone convergence of the conditional-optimal growth rate (Cover–Thomas §16.5)\x0a\x0aFor an increasing filtration `ℱ` of the market's past, the conditional log-optimal portfolio at\x0astage `k` (past-`ℱ k`-measurable) has an expected growth `condOptGrowth k`. Conditioning on more\x0apast information increases the optimal growth, so `condOptGrowth` is monotone; bounded above by a\x0amarket-regularity envelope, it converges to its supremum `condOptGrowthInfty = W_∞`. This sets up\x0athe definitions the Algoet–Cover sandwich consumes: `W_∞` is an increasing limit of\x0aintegrals `∫ log(bstar k · X) ∂μ`, each of which is a Birkhoff spatial mean.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Monotone convergence of the conditional-optimal growth rate (Cover–Thomas §16.5)\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"For an increasing filtration \"],[\"code\",[\"ℱ\"]],[\"normal\",\" of the market's past, the conditional log-optimal portfolio at\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"stage \"],[\"code\",[\"k\"]],[\"normal\",\" (past-\"],[\"code\",[\"ℱ k\"]],[\"normal\",\"-measurable) has an expected growth \"],[\"code\",[\"condOptGrowth k\"]],[\"normal\",\". Conditioning on more\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"past information increases the optimal growth, so \"],[\"code\",[\"condOptGrowth\"]],[\"normal\",\" is monotone; bounded above by a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"market-regularity envelope, it converges to its supremum \"],[\"code\",[\"condOptGrowthInfty = W_∞\"]],[\"normal\",\". This sets up\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the definitions the Algoet–Cover sandwich consumes: \"],[\"code\",[\"W_∞\"]],[\"normal\",\" is an increasing limit of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"integrals \"],[\"code\",[\"∫ log(bstar k · X) ∂μ\"]],[\"normal\",\", each of which is a Birkhoff spatial mean.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Portfolio.condOptGrowthInfty_eq_integral_infPast", 8044,
   "Gateway identity for the stationary-market `W_∞` AEP (Cover–Thomas §16.5): the growth-rate\x0aintegral of the infinite-past (`⨆ k, ℱ k`) conditional log-optimal portfolio `bstarInf` equals the\x0aincreasing limit `W_∞ = condOptGrowthInfty` of the stagewise conditional-optimal growths. This is\x0athe identity that lets the Algoet–Cover sandwich for `(1/n) log S*_n → W_∞` reduce to a direct\x0aBirkhoff application.\x0a\x0aTwo inclusions bracket the value. The upper inclusion `condOptGrowthInfty ≤ ∫ log (bstarInf · X)`\x0auses that each `bstar k` is `⨆ j, ℱ j`-measurable (the filtration is increasing) and hence a legal\x0acompetitor against `bstarInf` at the infinite-past level; integrating the conditional dominance\x0acollapses both conditional expectations to their integrals. The lower inclusion\x0a`∫ log (bstarInf · X) ≤ condOptGrowthInfty` approximates `bstarInf` by its stagewise conditional\x0aexpectations `c_k := μ[bstarInf | ℱ k]` (coordinatewise), which are `ℱ k`-measurable and a.e.\x0asimplex-valued (conditional expectation preserves nonnegativity and the unit coordinate sum);\x0apatched to be everywhere simplex-valued they are legal stage-`k` competitors, so\x0a`∫ log (c_k · X) ≤ condOptGrowth k ≤ condOptGrowthInfty`. Lévy's upward theorem\x0a(`Integrable.tendsto_ae_condExp`) gives `c_k → bstarInf` a.e., and dominated convergence (envelope\x0a`∑ⱼ |log Xⱼ|`) passes the bound to the limit.\x0a\x0a`bstarInf` and its `⨆ j, ℱ j`-conditional dominance are received as hypotheses (constructed\x0aseparately, e.g. by instantiating `exists_condLogOptimalSeq` at the constant filtration\x0a`fun _ ↦ ⨆ j, ℱ j`); this proves only the identity, not the existence. The `hpos`/`hint`\x0ahypotheses are market-regularity preconditions.\x0a\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Gateway identity for the stationary-market \"],[\"code\",[\"W_∞\"]],[\"normal\",\" AEP (Cover–Thomas §16.5): the growth-rate\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"integral of the infinite-past (\"],[\"code\",[\"⨆ k, ℱ k\"]],[\"normal\",\") conditional log-optimal portfolio \"],[\"code\",[\"bstarInf\"]],[\"normal\",\" equals the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"increasing limit \"],[\"code\",[\"W_∞ = condOptGrowthInfty\"]],[\"normal\",\" of the stagewise conditional-optimal growths. This is\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the identity that lets the Algoet–Cover sandwich for \"],[\"code\",[\"(1/n) log S*_n → W_∞\"]],[\"normal\",\" reduce to a direct\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Birkhoff application.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Two inclusions bracket the value. The upper inclusion \"],[\"code\",[\"condOptGrowthInfty ≤ ∫ log (bstarInf · X)\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"uses that each \"],[\"code\",[\"bstar k\"]],[\"normal\",\" is \"],[\"code\",[\"⨆ j, ℱ j\"]],[\"normal\",\"-measurable (the filtration is increasing) and hence a legal\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"competitor against \"],[\"code\",[\"bstarInf\"]],[\"normal\",\" at the infinite-past level; integrating the conditional dominance\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"collapses both conditional expectations to their integrals. The lower inclusion\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"∫ log (bstarInf · X) ≤ condOptGrowthInfty\"]],[\"normal\",\" approximates \"],[\"code\",[\"bstarInf\"]],[\"normal\",\" by its stagewise conditional\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"expectations \"],[\"code\",[\"c_k := μ[bstarInf | ℱ k]\"]],[\"normal\",\" (coordinatewise), which are \"],[\"code\",[\"ℱ k\"]],[\"normal\",\"-measurable and a.e.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"simplex-valued (conditional expectation preserves nonnegativity and the unit coordinate sum);\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"patched to be everywhere simplex-valued they are legal stage-\"],[\"code\",[\"k\"]],[\"normal\",\" competitors, so\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"∫ log (c_k · X) ≤ condOptGrowth k ≤ condOptGrowthInfty\"]],[\"normal\",\". Lévy's upward theorem\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(\"],[\"code\",[\"Integrable.tendsto_ae_condExp\"]],[\"normal\",\") gives \"],[\"code\",[\"c_k → bstarInf\"]],[\"normal\",\" a.e., and dominated convergence (envelope\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"∑ⱼ |log Xⱼ|\"]],[\"normal\",\") passes the bound to the limit.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"bstarInf\"]],[\"normal\",\" and its \"],[\"code\",[\"⨆ j, ℱ j\"]],[\"normal\",\"-conditional dominance are received as hypotheses (constructed\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"separately, e.g. by instantiating \"],[\"code\",[\"exists_condLogOptimalSeq\"]],[\"normal\",\" at the constant filtration\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"fun _ ↦ ⨆ j, ℱ j\"]],[\"normal\",\"); this proves only the identity, not the existence. The \"],[\"code\",[\"hpos\"]],[\"normal\",\"/\"],[\"code\",[\"hint\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"hypotheses are market-regularity preconditions.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
