   "# Rate-distortion convexity\x0a\x0aConvexity of the rate-distortion function in the distortion threshold\x0a(Cover–Thomas, Theorem 10.4): for all `D₁ D₂ : ℝ` and `λ ∈ [0, 1]`,\x0a`R(λ D₁ + (1-λ) D₂) ≤ λ R(D₁) + (1-λ) R(D₂)`.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `mixtureMeasure` — the convex combination of two joint measures at weight `λ`.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `rateDistortionFunction_convexOn` — convexity of the rate-distortion function.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aThe joint convexity of `klDiv` (Cover–Thomas 2.7.2) is not available directly in\x0aMathlib, so it is derived along the data-processing route in three layers:\x0a`klDiv_joint_convex` (a selector-extension on `Bool × Ω` combined with the\x0apushforward DPI `klDiv_map_le` and the per-slice KL additivity of mutually\x0asingular components) → `klDiv_mixture_le` → `rateDistortionFunction_convexOn`.\x0aThe infimum over feasible joints is pressed through\x0a`ENNReal.mul_iInf_of_ne` / `iInf_add` / `add_iInf`, with the boundary weights\x0a`λ = 0, 1` handled in separate branches.\x0a\x0a## References\x0a\x0a* T. M. Cover and J. A. Thomas, *Elements of Information Theory* (2nd ed.), Wiley, 2006. Theorem 10.4.\x0a",
