  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ShannonHartley.contAwgn_log_le_waterfill", 8044,
   "Fixed-`T` converse core: for any code `c` over `[0, T]` with average error `≤ ε` and at least\x0atwo messages, `log M` is capped by the water-filling bound at threshold `c₀`. Combines the band-Gram\x0aellipsoid, the prolate count domination, and the head/tail water-filling split, then the Fano\x0arearrangement `(1-ε)·log M ≤ [waterfill] + log 2`. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Fixed-\"],[\"code\",[\"T\"]],[\"normal\",\" converse core: for any code \"],[\"code\",[\"c\"]],[\"normal\",\" over \"],[\"code\",[\"[0, T]\"]],[\"normal\",\" with average error \"],[\"code\",[\"≤ ε\"]],[\"normal\",\" and at least\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"two messages, \"],[\"code\",[\"log M\"]],[\"normal\",\" is capped by the water-filling bound at threshold \"],[\"code\",[\"c₀\"]],[\"normal\",\". Combines the band-Gram\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"ellipsoid, the prolate count domination, and the head/tail water-filling split, then the Fano\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"rearrangement \"],[\"code\",[\"(1-ε)·log M ≤ [waterfill] + log 2\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ShannonHartley.contAwgn_ge_shannonHartley", 8044,
   "The operational capacity is at least the Shannon-Hartley closed form (achievability, `≥`).\x0a\x0aThe infimum over `ε` reduces (via `le_ciInf` over the phantom-free subtype `↥(Set.Ioo 0 1)`) to\x0athe per-`ε` bound `sh_le_contAwgnRate`, which builds continuous-time band-limited codewords out of\x0aa discrete `AwgnCode` on `prolateCount T W c` observations (`contAwgnMaxMessages_ge_of_awgnCode`)\x0afed by the block `awgn_channel_coding_theorem`, and reads off the `≈ 2WT` degrees-of-freedom count\x0a`prolateCount_div_tendsto` (from `le_prolateCount` / `prolateCount_le`) through a `limsup`\x0acomparison.\x0a\x0aThe achievability half needs only that `prolateCount T W c / T` converges to `2W` (the crude\x0atwo-sided count), not the tight Landau-Pollak-Slepian concentration. The infimum is taken over the\x0aphantom-free subtype `↥(Set.Ioo 0 1)`: the bounded binder `⨅ ε ∈ Set.Ioo 0 1` would instead pick\x0aup the phantom `sInf ∅ = 0` from every `ε ∉ (0,1)` on the conditionally-complete `ℝ`, collapsing\x0athe capacity to `0`.\x0a\x0aHypotheses `hW`/`hN₀`/`hP` are regularity-only (not load-bearing).\x0a\x0a@audit:ok (sorryAx-free; signature scan regularity-only, no load-bearing hyp. The block\x0a`awgn_channel_coding_theorem`'s only non-rate hypothesis `h_meas` is discharged by the theorem\x0a`AWGN.isAwgnChannelMeasurable N`, not leaked into this signature; the load-bearing\x0a`awgn_capacity_closed_form` (`h_bridge_gauss`/`h_bdd`/`h_max_ent`) is off-path — 0 transitive\x0areferences from this headline.) ",
