  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.ShannonHartley.Rotation module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Shannon–Hartley converse — isotropic-Gaussian rotation invariance\x0a\x0aThe measure-theoretic crux of the Shannon–Hartley converse rotation. An isotropic\x0aGaussian on `Fin k → ℝ` with per-coordinate mean `v i` and common variance `N` is invariant under\x0aan orthogonal transformation, up to rotating the mean:\x0a\x0a`(Measure.pi (fun i => gaussianReal (v i) N)).map (O.mulVec)`\x0a` = Measure.pi (fun i => gaussianReal ((O v) i) N)`\x0a\x0afor `O ∈ Matrix.orthogonalGroup (Fin k) ℝ`. This will be consumed by the downstream `errorProbAt`\x0arotation, which rotates a code's `testFn` family by the real orthogonal eigenvector matrix of the\x0aband-Gram operator.\x0a\x0a## Approach\x0a\x0aThe proof goes through characteristic functions on `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin k)`. By\x0a`charFun_eq_pi_iff`, the product-measure equality reduces to the pointwise identity of\x0acharacteristic functions. Pushing the map through `charFun` (change of variables) plus the\x0aorthogonal-matrix adjoint identities (`x ⬝ᵥ (O *ᵥ y) = (Oᵀ *ᵥ x) ⬝ᵥ y` and `O * Oᵀ = 1`) turns\x0athe left-hand product into the right-hand one after expanding `charFun_gaussianReal` and combining\x0athe exponentials.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Shannon–Hartley converse — isotropic-Gaussian rotation invariance\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The measure-theoretic crux of the Shannon–Hartley converse rotation. An isotropic\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Gaussian on \"],[\"code\",[\"Fin k → ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\" with per-coordinate mean \"],[\"code\",[\"v i\"]],[\"normal\",\" and common variance \"],[\"code\",[\"N\"]],[\"normal\",\" is invariant under\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"an orthogonal transformation, up to rotating the mean:\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"(Measure.pi (fun i => gaussianReal (v i) N)).map (O.mulVec)\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\" = Measure.pi (fun i => gaussianReal ((O v) i) N)\"]]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"for \"],[\"code\",[\"O ∈ Matrix.orthogonalGroup (Fin k) ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\". This will be consumed by the downstream \"],[\"code\",[\"errorProbAt\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"rotation, which rotates a code's \"],[\"code\",[\"testFn\"]],[\"normal\",\" family by the real orthogonal eigenvector matrix of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"band-Gram operator.\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Approach\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The proof goes through characteristic functions on \"],[\"code\",[\"EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin k)\"]],[\"normal\",\". By\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"charFun_eq_pi_iff\"]],[\"normal\",\", the product-measure equality reduces to the pointwise identity of\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"characteristic functions. Pushing the map through \"],[\"code\",[\"charFun\"]],[\"normal\",\" (change of variables) plus the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"orthogonal-matrix adjoint identities (\"],[\"code\",[\"x ⬝ᵥ (O *ᵥ y) = (Oᵀ *ᵥ x) ⬝ᵥ y\"]],[\"normal\",\" and \"],[\"code\",[\"O * Oᵀ = 1\"]],[\"normal\",\") turns\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the left-hand product into the right-hand one after expanding \"],[\"code\",[\"charFun_gaussianReal\"]],[\"normal\",\" and combining\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the exponentials.\"]]]]"),
