  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.Stein.OptimalExponent module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Stein's lemma: the optimal type-II exponent\x0a\x0aThe achievability and converse bounds are assembled onto the optimal type-II error\x0a`steinOptimalBeta P Q n ε`. The two bounds do not coincide: the converse carries a `1/(1−ε)`\x0afactor, so the rate `-(1/n) log (steinOptimalBeta P Q n ε)` is sandwiched between\x0a`(klDiv P Q).toReal − δ` from below and `(klDiv P Q).toReal / (1−ε) + log 2 / (n(1−ε))` from\x0aabove. Letting `ε → 0⁺` collapses the upper bound back to `(klDiv P Q).toReal`.\x0a\x0a## Main definitions\x0a\x0a* `steinBetaSet P Q n ε` — the type-II error probabilities attainable by `ε`-level tests.\x0a* `steinOptimalBeta P Q n ε` — the infimum of `steinBetaSet`, the optimal type-II error.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `steinOptimalBeta_log_le_of_converse` and `steinOptimalBeta_log_ge_of_achievability` — the\x0a  converse and achievability bounds expressed on `steinOptimalBeta`.\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",1,[[\"normal\",\"Stein's lemma: the optimal type-II exponent\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The achievability and converse bounds are assembled onto the optimal type-II error\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"steinOptimalBeta P Q n ε\"]],[\"normal\",\". The two bounds do not coincide: the converse carries a \"],[\"code\",[\"1/(1−ε)\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"factor, so the rate \"],[\"code\",[\"-(1/n) log (steinOptimalBeta P Q n ε)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is sandwiched between\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"(klDiv P Q).toReal − δ\"]],[\"normal\",\" from below and \"],[\"code\",[\"(klDiv P Q).toReal / (1−ε) + log 2 / (n(1−ε))\"]],[\"normal\",\" from\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"above. Letting \"],[\"code\",[\"ε → 0⁺\"]],[\"normal\",\" collapses the upper bound back to \"],[\"code\",[\"(klDiv P Q).toReal\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main definitions\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"steinBetaSet P Q n ε\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the type-II error probabilities attainable by \"],[\"code\",[\"ε\"]],[\"normal\",\"-level tests.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"steinOptimalBeta P Q n ε\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the infimum of \"],[\"code\",[\"steinBetaSet\"]],[\"normal\",\", the optimal type-II error.\"]]]]]]],[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Main statements\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"steinOptimalBeta_log_le_of_converse\"]],[\"normal\",\" and \"],[\"code\",[\"steinOptimalBeta_log_ge_of_achievability\"]],[\"normal\",\" — the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"converse and achievability bounds expressed on \"],[\"code\",[\"steinOptimalBeta\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]]]]]"),
