  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.TimeBandLimiting.timeBandLimitingOp_isCompact", 8044,
   "The time-and-band limiting operator is compact: `A = P_W ∘ C` with `C = Q_T ∘ P_W` compact\x0a(the sinc integral operator) and `P_W` bounded, so `A` is compact by `clm_comp`.\x0a\x0aUnconditional: the signature carries no hypothesis on `T` or `W`, and both degenerate parameter\x0aranges are discharged by real proofs rather than assumed away — `W < 0` via\x0a`bandLimitSubspace_eq_bot_of_nonpos` (`P_W = 0`, so `C = 0`), `T < 0` via the empty `[0,T]`\x0a(`Q_T = 0`), and `W = 0` inside `bandLimitProj_apply_ae` as a null-band case.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The time-and-band limiting operator is compact: \"],[\"code\",[\"A = P_W ∘ C\"]],[\"normal\",\" with \"],[\"code\",[\"C = Q_T ∘ P_W\"]],[\"normal\",\" compact\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(the sinc integral operator) and \"],[\"code\",[\"P_W\"]],[\"normal\",\" bounded, so \"],[\"code\",[\"A\"]],[\"normal\",\" is compact by \"],[\"code\",[\"clm_comp\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Unconditional: the signature carries no hypothesis on \"],[\"code\",[\"T\"]],[\"normal\",\" or \"],[\"code\",[\"W\"]],[\"normal\",\", and both degenerate parameter\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"ranges are discharged by real proofs rather than assumed away — \"],[\"code\",[\"W < 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" via\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"bandLimitSubspace_eq_bot_of_nonpos\"]],[\"normal\",\" (\"],[\"code\",[\"P_W = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\", so \"],[\"code\",[\"C = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\"), \"],[\"code\",[\"T < 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" via the empty \"],[\"code\",[\"[0,T]\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(\"],[\"code\",[\"Q_T = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\"), and \"],[\"code\",[\"W = 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" inside \"],[\"code\",[\"bandLimitProj_apply_ae\"]],[\"normal\",\" as a null-band case.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.TimeBandLimiting.l2KernelOp", 8044,
   "The kernel-to-operator map `κ ↦ (f ↦ ∫ κ(·,s) f(s) ds)`, as a continuous linear map. Its\x0acontinuity is exactly the Hilbert–Schmidt bound `‖l2KernelOp κ‖ ≤ ‖κ‖`.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The kernel-to-operator map \"],[\"code\",[\"κ ↦ (f ↦ ∫ κ(·,s) f(s) ds)\"]],[\"normal\",\", as a continuous linear map. Its\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"continuity is exactly the Hilbert–Schmidt bound \"],[\"code\",[\"‖l2KernelOp κ‖ ≤ ‖κ‖\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.TimeBandLimiting.l2KernelApply", 8044,
   "The integral operator attached to a kernel, at the level of raw functions:\x0a`f ↦ (t ↦ ∫ k(t,s) f(s) ds)`. ",
