  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.TimeBandLimiting.bandKernelLp_mem_bandLimitSubspace", 8044,
   "The reproducing kernel is itself band-limited. Its Fourier transform is the spectral boxcar\x0a`specBoxcar t (1/(2W))` (`fourier_shiftSinc_toLp`), whose support `[-1/(2Δ), 1/(2Δ)]` is exactly the\x0aband `[-W,W]` at `Δ = 1/(2W)`; membership in `bandLimitSubspace W` is then the definition of that\x0asubspace as a Fourier comap. This is what lets `P_W Q_T k_t` be read as `A k_t` below.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The reproducing kernel is itself band-limited. Its Fourier transform is the spectral boxcar\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"specBoxcar t (1/(2W))\"]],[\"normal\",\" (\"],[\"code\",[\"fourier_shiftSinc_toLp\"]],[\"normal\",\"), whose support \"],[\"code\",[\"[-1/(2Δ), 1/(2Δ)]\"]],[\"normal\",\" is exactly the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"band \"],[\"code\",[\"[-W,W]\"]],[\"normal\",\" at \"],[\"code\",[\"Δ = 1/(2W)\"]],[\"normal\",\"; membership in \"],[\"code\",[\"bandLimitSubspace W\"]],[\"normal\",\" is then the definition of that\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"subspace as a Fourier comap. This is what lets \"],[\"code\",[\"P_W Q_T k_t\"]],[\"normal\",\" be read as \"],[\"code\",[\"A k_t\"]],[\"normal\",\" below.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.TimeBandLimiting.orthonormal_countable", 8044,
   "An orthonormal family in a separable inner-product space is countable.\x0a\x0aDistinct members sit at distance `√2`, so the open balls of radius `1/2` around them are pairwise\x0adisjoint, and a separable space admits only countably many pairwise-disjoint nonempty open sets\x0a(`Pairwise.countable_of_isOpen_disjoint`). Mathlib has no such lemma\x0a(loogle `Orthonormal, Countable` = `Found 0`), so it is built here; it is what lets\x0a`tsum_inner_timeBandLimitingOp_eq`\x0a*derive* the countability its Tonelli step needs instead of assuming it.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"An orthonormal family in a separable inner-product space is countable.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Distinct members sit at distance \"],[\"code\",[\"√2\"]],[\"normal\",\", so the open balls of radius \"],[\"code\",[\"1/2\"]],[\"normal\",\" around them are pairwise\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"disjoint, and a separable space admits only countably many pairwise-disjoint nonempty open sets\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(\"],[\"code\",[\"Pairwise.countable_of_isOpen_disjoint\"]],[\"normal\",\"). Mathlib has no such lemma\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(loogle \"],[\"code\",[\"Orthonormal, Countable\"]],[\"normal\",\" = \"],[\"code\",[\"Found 0\"]],[\"normal\",\"), so it is built here; it is what lets\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"tsum_inner_timeBandLimitingOp_eq\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"derive\"]]],[\"normal\",\" the countability its Tonelli step needs instead of assuming it.\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.TimeBandLimiting.tsum_eigen_eq_tsum_prolateEigenvalues", 8044,
   "The multiplicity bridge: the eigenvalue sum along the eigenbasis equals the sum over the\x0adecreasing enumeration `prolateEigenvalues`, since both nonnegative families share the super-level\x0acounts `#{· > c} = prolateCount T W c` (the eigenbasis vectors above `c` span\x0a`prolateEigenspaceSup T W c`, whose `finrank` *is* `prolateCount` — `ncard_setOf_lt_lam`; the\x0aenumeration exceeds `c` on the initial segment `{0, …, prolateCount T W c − 1}` —\x0a`setOf_lt_prolateEigenvalues_eq_Iio`), transported through the layer-cake identity\x0a`lintegral_eq_lintegral_meas_lt`: both `ℝ≥0∞` sums equal `∫⁻ t ∈ Ioi 0, prolateCount T W t`.\x0aSummability of both families (`summable_of_sum_le` from the Bessel bound, then\x0a`ENNReal.summable_toReal`) converts the `ℝ≥0∞` equality back to `ℝ`.\x0a\x0a`heig`/`hnn`/`hspan` are structural preconditions\x0adescribing an abstract eigenbasis, not the conclusion in disguise — the multiplicity core\x0a(layer-cake `lintegral_eq_lintegral_meas_lt`, Bessel summability, the `Measure.count` distribution\x0afunctions) is carried by the body. They are discharged by feeding `exists_eigen_hilbertBasis`'s\x0aoutput at the headline `tsum_prolateEigenvalues_eq`, which therefore assumes none of them (no\x0aload-bearing bundle).\x0asorryAx-free (`#print axioms` = `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`).\x0a@audit:ok ",
