,[\"lintegral_eq_lintegral_meas_lt\"]],[\"normal\",\", Bessel summability, the \"],[\"code\",[\"Measure.count\"]],[\"normal\",\" distribution\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"functions) is carried by the body. They are discharged by feeding \"],[\"code\",[\"exists_eigen_hilbertBasis\"]],[\"normal\",\"'s\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"output at the headline \"],[\"code\",[\"tsum_prolateEigenvalues_eq\"]],[\"normal\",\", which therefore assumes none of them (no\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"load-bearing bundle).\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"sorryAx-free (\"],[\"code\",[\"#print axioms\"]],[\"normal\",\" = \"],[\"code\",[\"[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\"]],[\"normal\",\").\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.TimeBandLimiting.inner_timeBandLimitingOp_self_eq", 8044,
   "The quadratic form of `A` is the energy of `P_W f` observed through the window `[0,T]`:\x0a`⟪A f, f⟫ = ∫_[0,T] |⟪k_t, f⟫|² dt`. Self-adjointness of `P_W` moves one copy across the pairing,\x0aand `timeLimitProj_apply_ae` turns `Q_T` into multiplication by `𝟙_[0,T]`.\x0a@audit:ok ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The quadratic form of \"],[\"code\",[\"A\"]],[\"normal\",\" is the energy of \"],[\"code\",[\"P_W f\"]],[\"normal\",\" observed through the window \"],[\"code\",[\"[0,T]\"]],[\"normal\",\":\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"⟪A f, f⟫ = ∫_[0,T] |⟪k_t, f⟫|² dt\"]],[\"normal\",\". Self-adjointness of \"],[\"code\",[\"P_W\"]],[\"normal\",\" moves one copy across the pairing,\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"and \"],[\"code\",[\"timeLimitProj_apply_ae\"]],[\"normal\",\" turns \"],[\"code\",[\"Q_T\"]],[\"normal\",\" into multiplication by \"],[\"code\",[\"𝟙_[0,T]\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok\"]]]]"),
