  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.WynerZiv.Achievability module doc 0", 8044,
   "# Wyner–Ziv operational achievability (binning + covering)\x0a\x0aThis file assembles the operational achievability leg of the Wyner–Ziv theorem\x0a(Cover–Thomas Theorem 15.9.1): a rate `R` above the information-theoretic rate\x0a`wynerZivRate` is achievable at distortion `D` for the i.i.d. source `P_XY` with\x0adecoder side information `Y`.\x0a\x0a## Approach\x0a\x0aWyner–Ziv achievability is a two-layer hybrid: **rate-distortion covering** on the\x0a`X → U` side and **Slepian–Wolf binning** on the side-information `Y` side.\x0a\x0a* the encoder covers `X^n` by a codeword `U^n` drawn from an i.i.d. codebook\x0a  (rate-distortion covering, `jointTypicalLossyEncoder`), then bins the codeword\x0a  index (Slepian–Wolf binning, `binningMeasure`) down to rate `R ≈ I(X;U) −\x0a  I(Y;U)`;\x0a* the decoder receives `(bin index, Y^n)` and searches its bin for the unique\x0a  codeword conditionally typical with `Y^n`.\x0a\x0aThe two error mechanisms decouple cleanly (see the *gateway atoms* below), each\x0aliving on its own conditional-typicality slice under the **common** alphabet\x0aassignment \"covering codeword `U` in the source role, side information `Y` as the\x0aconditioning variable\":\x0a\x0a* **decoder confusion** — a wrong binned codeword `U'^n` shares the true bin and\x0a  is conditionally typical with `Y^n`. Its expected mass over the random binning\x0a  is bounded by (slice cardinality) `/` (bin count), via the Slepian–Wolf alias\x0a  bound `swError_EX_expectation_le` (itself `binning_collision_prob` ∘\x0a  `conditionalTypicalSlice_card_le`). This is the `Y`-fixed, `U`-counted slice.\x0a* **covering acceptance** — the true covering codeword is itself conditionally\x0a  typical with `Y^n` (not rejected), via the strong conditional-slice mass bound\x0a  `conditionalStronglyTypicalSlice_mass_ge`. This is the `U`-fixed, `Y`-measured\x0a  slice.\x0a\x0aThese are transposed fibers of the same joint typicality relation, but they never\x0aneed to be reconciled into one statement: they bound *independent* error events.\x0aThe apparent transposition between the strong slice (`conditionalStronglyTypical`,\x0a`U`-fixed) and the weak slice (`conditionalTypical`, `Y`-fixed) is therefore not\x0aan obstruction — it is exactly the decomposition the error analysis wants.\x0a\x0a## Main statements\x0a\x0a* `wyner_ziv_achievability` — the operational achievability headline.\x0a\x0a## Gateway atoms (both reuse existing, proved in-project atoms)\x0a\x0a* `wz_sideInfo_decoder_confusion_expectation_le` — the decoder-confusion bound,\x0a  by instantiating the Slepian–Wolf alias bound with the covering codeword in the\x0a  source role.\x0a* `wz_covering_sideInfo_mass_ge` — the covering-acceptance mass bound, by\x0a  instantiating the strong conditional-slice mass bound with the same alphabet\x0a  assignment.\x0a\x0a## Implementation notes\x0a\x0aThe construction threads these two exponents through the Wyner–Ziv error\x0adecomposition, splits the rate as `R = I(X;U) − I(Y;U)`, and extracts a good\x0acodebook by the pigeonhole averaging `exists_codebook_low_avg`. The headline\x0ais proved sorry-free (`#print axioms wyner_ziv_achievability` =\x0a`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`).\x0a\x0a## Module structure\x0a\x0aUmbrella of the `Shannon/WynerZiv/Achievability/` family, re-exporting (in dependency order):\x0a\x0a* `Achievability.Covering` — the gateway atoms, the covering + binning construction skeleton and\x0a  its leaf atoms, the two-ambient regularity section, and the hoisted Markov-core helpers.\x0a* `Achievability.Concentration` — the band-concentration sub-lemmas for the Markov-lemma\x0a  covering bound.\x0a* `Achievability.MarkovCore` — the Markov core and Gateway atom 3 (covering side-information\x0a  acceptance).\x0a* `Achievability.ChosenWord` — covering chosen-word side-information typicality and the joint\x0a  lossy code existence.\x0a* `Achievability.Decomposition` — the Steps 3–7 distortion decomposition and the pmf-side\x0a  product bounds.\x0a* `Achievability.SourceTransport` — the source-measure change of variables and the\x0a  distortion-decomposition bridge.\x0a* `Achievability.MassBound` — the source→ambient AEP mass transport and the entropy helpers.\x0a* `Achievability.Headline` — the per-slack good codes and the operational achievability headline\x0a  `wyner_ziv_achievability`.\x0a",
