  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.WynerZiv.Achievability.MarkovCore module doc 1", 8044,
   "## Covering chosen-word side-information acceptance (Markov lemma)\x0a\x0aFor the covering `LossyCode` `c`, the *correlated joint source* mass of the acceptance-failure\x0aevent `wzCoveringAcceptFailSet` — the event that the chosen covering word `c.decoder (c.encoder x)`\x0ais not jointly typical with the side information `y` (with `(x, y)` drawn from the true joint\x0a`P_XY`, so `x` and `y` are correlated) — is small, given only the covering-typicality success\x0aprecondition (the chosen word covers the source `x`, a regularity precondition on the constructed\x0acode, not the acceptance conclusion).\x0a\x0aIts analytic core is the **Markov lemma**: if the chosen word `u = c.decoder (c.encoder x)`\x0atypically covers `x` and the source pair `(x, y)` is jointly typical, then `(u, y)` is jointly\x0atypical — so acceptance fails only off the (exp-small) covering-failure ∪ source-atypicality set.\x0aThe measure is the *correlated* joint source\x0a`Measure.pi (pmfToMeasure (fun (x', y) ↦ P_XY{(x'.1, y)}))`; crucially the covering word\x0a`c.decoder (c.encoder x)` is a function of the source `x`, so the `u`–`y` correlation that makes\x0aacceptance likely is inherited from the `x`–`y` correlation and is destroyed by fixing `u`\x0aindependently. The lemma `wz_covering_sideInfo_mass_ge` (a *lower* bound on the *independent*\x0aproduct-`Y`-law slice mass) and the broadcast confusion bound `bc_conditional_slice_prob_le`\x0a(an *upper* bound on a *conditional-product* typical slice, the confusion/wrong-codeword direction)\x0aare on the wrong measure/direction and do not supply this. ",
