g word\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"c.decoder (c.encoder x)\"]],[\"normal\",\" is a function of the source \"],[\"code\",[\"x\"]],[\"normal\",\", so the \"],[\"code\",[\"u\"]],[\"normal\",\"–\"],[\"code\",[\"y\"]],[\"normal\",\" correlation that makes\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"acceptance likely is inherited from the \"],[\"code\",[\"x\"]],[\"normal\",\"–\"],[\"code\",[\"y\"]],[\"normal\",\" correlation and is destroyed by fixing \"],[\"code\",[\"u\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"independently. The lemma \"],[\"code\",[\"wz_covering_sideInfo_mass_ge\"]],[\"normal\",\" (a \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"lower\"]]],[\"normal\",\" bound on the \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"independent\"]]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"product-\"],[\"code\",[\"Y\"]],[\"normal\",\"-law slice mass) and the broadcast confusion bound \"],[\"code\",[\"bc_conditional_slice_prob_le\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(an \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"upper\"]]],[\"normal\",\" bound on a \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"conditional-product\"]]],[\"normal\",\" typical slice, the confusion/wrong-codeword direction)\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"are on the wrong measure/direction and do not supply this.\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.WynerZiv.Achievability.SourceTransport module doc 2", 8044,
   "### Source-measure change of variables `α' → α`\x0a\x0aThe covering `LossyCode` (hypothesis `hcov₁`) measures its block distortion under the\x0ai.i.d. covering ambient `(rdAmbient qStar).map (iidXs 0)` on the source-support subtype\x0a`α' := {x // 0 < P_X x}`, whereas the Wyner–Ziv conclusion measures the lifted code under\x0a`Measure.pi P_XY` on `α × β`. This block reconciles the *source* side of that change of\x0avariables: the covering ambient's `X`-marginal, pushed from `α'` back to the full alphabet\x0a`α` by `Subtype.val`, is exactly the source `X`-marginal `P_XY.map Prod.fst`. On the\x0asupport the covering `X`-marginal singleton is `∑_u qStar(⟨a,·⟩, u) = ∑_y P_XY{(a,y)}` (by\x0a`hqStar_eq` and `hκ'sum`); off the support both sides carry zero mass. This is pure\x0asource-measure transport — no decoder, error event, or distortion function enters — the\x0asource-measure companion of the null-set decoder transport\x0a`wz_expectedBlockDistortion_source_agree`. ",
