  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.WynerZiv.Basic module doc 3", 8044,
   "## Wyner–Ziv constraint set\x0a\x0aThe decoder `f : U × β → γ` is carried as an *external* second component, so\x0athe constraint set lives on the product `(α × β × U → ℝ) × (U × β → γ)`. The\x0aMarkov constraint `U − X − Y` is encoded in cross-product form, well-defined\x0aeven where marginals vanish (inventory §6.5).\x0a",
   "[[\"header\",2,[[\"normal\",\"Wyner–Ziv constraint set\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"The decoder \"],[\"code\",[\"f : U × β → γ\"]],[\"normal\",\" is carried as an \"],[\"em\",[[\"normal\",\"external\"]]],[\"normal\",\" second component, so\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the constraint set lives on the product \"],[\"code\",[\"(α × β × U → ℝ) × (U × β → γ)\"]],[\"normal\",\". The\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Markov constraint \"],[\"code\",[\"U − X − Y\"]],[\"normal\",\" is encoded in cross-product form, well-defined\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"even where marginals vanish (inventory §6.5).\"]]]]"),
