  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.negMulLog_marginal_gap_le_joint_gap", 8044,
   "Refinement / coarsening inequality (the DPI core).  For two\x0anon-negative joint slices `r₁, r₂ : α × β → ℝ` and weights `a, b ≥ 0` with\x0a`a + b = 1`, writing the mixture `m = a • r₁ + b • r₂`, the convexity of the\x0a`Y`-marginal-vs-joint entropy gap holds:\x0a`∑_y [neg(∑_x m(x,y)) − a·neg(∑_x r₁(x,y)) − b·neg(∑_x r₂(x,y))]`\x0a  `≤ ∑_y ∑_x [neg(m(x,y)) − a·neg(r₁(x,y)) − b·neg(r₂(x,y))]`.\x0a\x0aThis is the data-processing inequality for the Jensen–Shannon gap under the\x0acoarsening `(x,y) ↦ y`, proved per `y` by `log_sum_inequality_negMulLog`\x0awith the two mixture components as the log-sum \"fiber\". ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Refinement / coarsening inequality (the DPI core).  For two\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"non-negative joint slices \"],[\"code\",[\"r₁, r₂ : α × β → ℝ\"]],[\"normal\",\" and weights \"],[\"code\",[\"a, b ≥ 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" with\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"a + b = 1\"]],[\"normal\",\", writing the mixture \"],[\"code\",[\"m = a • r₁ + b • r₂\"]],[\"normal\",\", the convexity of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"Y\"]],[\"normal\",\"-marginal-vs-joint entropy gap holds:\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"∑_y [neg(∑_x m(x,y)) − a·neg(∑_x r₁(x,y)) − b·neg(∑_x r₂(x,y))]\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"≤ ∑_y ∑_x [neg(m(x,y)) − a·neg(r₁(x,y)) − b·neg(r₂(x,y))]\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"This is the data-processing inequality for the Jensen–Shannon gap under the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"coarsening \"],[\"code\",[\"(x,y) ↦ y\"]],[\"normal\",\", proved per \"],[\"code\",[\"y\"]],[\"normal\",\" by \"],[\"code\",[\"log_sum_inequality_negMulLog\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"with the two mixture components as the log-sum \\\"fiber\\\".\"]]]]"),
