  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.wz_support_reduce", 8044,
   "Carathéodory support reduction. Any feasible factorizable kernel at\x0aan arbitrary finite auxiliary alphabet `Fin k` reduces to a feasible kernel at the fixed\x0aalphabet `Fin (|α| + 3)` with objective `≤` the original.\x0a\x0aEncode each auxiliary letter `u` with `P_U(u) > 0`\x0aby the vector `Φ_u = (P_{X|U=u}, g_u, δ_u) ∈ ℝ^{|α|+2}` (coordinates indexed by `α ⊕ Bool`),\x0awhere `P_{X|U=u}(x) = m_XU(x,u)/P_U(u)`, the objective density `g_u = block_u(κ)/P_U(u)` with\x0a`block_u(κ) = ∑_y neg(m_YU(y,u)) − ∑_x neg(m_XU(x,u))`, and the distortion density\x0a`δ_u = dist_u/P_U(u)`. The `P_U`-weighted mixture `M = ∑_u P_U(u) Φ_u =\x0a(P_X, objective−(H(X)−H(Y)), distortion)` lies in `convexHull (range Φ) ⊆ ℝ^{|α|+2}`, so by\x0abare Carathéodory (`eq_pos_convex_span_of_mem_convexHull` + `card_le_finrank_succ`, with\x0a`finrank ℝ (α ⊕ Bool → ℝ) = |α|+2`) it is a convex combination of at most `|α|+3` of the\x0a`Φ_u`. This deliberately relaxes the target size to `|α|+3` (rather than the tighter `|α|+2`,\x0awhich would need the vectorSpan hyperplane refinement `∑ P_{X|U=u} = 1`, or the\x0aFenchel–Eggleston `|α|+1` improvement absent from Mathlib): the K-agnostic endpoint assembly\x0a(`wynerZivRate_le_of_forall_pos_add_endpoint`) makes this non-load-bearing, and a\x0alarger-than-tight `K` only eases the ∃-claim, never falsifies it.\x0a\x0a`h_pmf` (simplex membership) and `hκ` (the input feasible kernel — the data being reduced)\x0aare preconditions, not a `*Hypothesis`/`*Reduction` predicate bundling the reduction's core.\x0a\x0aProof: assembled from four pieces.\x0a* Entropy-mixture identity `wzKernelObjective_eq_blockSum`:\x0a  `wzKernelObjective V P_XY κ = (H(X) − H(Y)) + ∑_u block_u(κ)`.\x0a* Mass equality: both letter marginals total `P_U u` (`∑_x m_XU(x,u) = P_U u = ∑_y m_YU(y,u)`),\x0a  the identity that makes the block-scaling corrections cancel.\x0a* Convex geometry `wz_caratheodory_reduce` (bare Carathéodory + zero-padding reindex\x0a  `wz_fin_pad_sum`): reduces `M ∈ convexHull (range Φ)` to weights `λ_j` on letters `u_j = σ j`.\x0a* Kernel reconstruction — `κ'(x,j) = (λ_j/P_U(u_j))·κ(x,u_j)` on `P_X(x) > 0` rows (with a\x0a  fixed-pmf override on `P_X(x)=0` rows, invisible since `P_XY(x,·)=0` there); decoder slice\x0a  `f'(j,·) = f(u_j,·)`. Feasibility (`distortion' = distortion ≤ D`, via the `δ`-coordinate)\x0a  and objective equality (`objective' = objective`, via the `g`-coordinate + the block-scaling\x0a  `block_j(κ') = (λ_j/P_U(u_j))·block_{u_j}(κ)` from `Real.negMulLog_mul` + mass equality) are\x0a  proved directly, so `objective' = objective`, whence `≤`.\x0a@audit:ok (non-circular and non-bundled: `h_pmf` is simplex regularity, `hκ` the input datum\x0abeing reduced, and the conclusion `∃ κ' : Fin (|α|+3)` feasible with objective ≤ is not a\x0ahypothesis restated; the objective is proven equal — stronger than ≤ — and distortion\x0apreserved exactly, so the reduction genuinely follows.) ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Carathéodory support reduction. Any feasible factorizable kernel at\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"an arbitrary finite auxiliary alphabet \"],[\"code\",[\"Fin k\"]],[\"normal\",\" reduces to a feasible kernel at the fixed\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"alphabet \"],[\"code\",[\"Fin (|α| + 3)\"]],[\"normal\",\" with objective \"],[\"code\",[\"≤\"]],[\"normal\",\" the original.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Encode each auxiliary letter \"],[\"code\",[\"u\"]],[\"normal\",\" with \"],[\"code\",[\"P_U(u) > 0\"]],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"by the vector \"],[\"code\",[\"Φ_u = (P_{X|U=u}, g_u, δ_u) ∈ ℝ^{|α|+2}\"]],[\"normal\",\" (coordinates indexed by \"],[\"code\",[\"α ⊕ Bool\"]],[\"normal\",\"),\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"where \"],[\"code\",[\"P_{X|U=u}(x) = m_XU(x,u)/P_U(u)\"]],[\"normal\",\", the objective density \"],[\"code\",[\"g_u = block_u(κ)/P_U(u)\"]],[\"normal\",\" with\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"block_u(κ) = ∑_y neg(m_YU(y,u)) − ∑_x neg(m_XU(x,u))\"]],[\"normal\",\", and the distortion density\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"δ_u = dist_u/P_U(u)\"]],[\"normal\",\". The \"],[\"code\",[\"P_U\"]],[\"normal\",\"-weighted mixture \"],[\"code\",[\"M = ∑_u P_U(u) Φ_u =\",\" \",\"(P_X, objective−(H(X)−H(Y)), distortion)\"]],[\"normal\",\" lies in \"],[\"code\",[\"convexHull (range Φ) ⊆ ℝ^{|α|+2}\"]],[\"normal\",\", so by\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"bare Carathéodory (\"],[\"code\",[\"eq_pos_convex_span_of_mem_convexHull\"]],[\"normal\",\" + \"],[\"code\",[\"card_le_finrank_succ\"]],[\"normal\",\", with\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"finrank ℝ (α ⊕ Bool → ℝ) = |α|+2\"]],[\"normal\",\") it is a convex combination of at most \"],[\"code\",[\"|α|+3\"]],[\"normal\",\" of the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"Φ_u\"]],[\"normal\",\". This deliberately relaxes the target size to \"],[\"code\",[\"|α|+3\"]],[\"normal\",\" (rather than the tighter \"],[\"code\",[\"|α|+2\"]],[\"normal\",\",\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"which would need the vectorSpan hyperplane refinement \"],[\"code\",[\"∑ P_{X|U=u} = 1\"]],[\"normal\",\", or the\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Fenchel–Eggleston \"],[\"code\",[\"|α|+1\"]],[\"normal\",\" improvement absent from Mathlib): the K-agnostic endpoint assembly\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"(\"],[\"code\",[\"wynerZivRate_le_of_forall_pos_add_endpoint\"]],[\"normal\",\") makes this non-load-bearing, and a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"larger-than-tight \"],[\"code\",[\"K\"]],[\"normal\",\" only eases the ∃-claim, never falsifies it.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"h_pmf\"]],[\"normal\",\" (simplex membership) and \"],[\"code\",[\"hκ\"]],[\"normal\",\" (the input feasible kernel — the data being reduced)\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"are preconditions, not a \"],[\"code\",[\"*Hypothesis\"]],[\"normal\",\"/\"],[\"code\",[\"*Reduction\"]],[\"normal\",\" predicate bundling the reduction's core.\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Proof: assembled from four pieces.\"]]],[\"ul\",true,\"*\",[[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Entropy-mixture identity \"],[\"code\",[\"wzKernelObjective_eq_blockSum\"]],[\"normal\",\":\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"wzKernelObjective V P_XY κ = (H(X) − H(Y)) + ∑_u block_u(κ)\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Mass equality: both letter marginals total \"],[\"code\",[\"P_U u\"]],[\"normal\",\" (\"],[\"code\",[\"∑_x m_XU(x,u) = P_U u = ∑_y m_YU(y,u)\"]],[\"normal\",\"),\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the identity that makes the block-scaling corrections cancel.\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Convex geometry \"],[\"code\",[\"wz_caratheodory_reduce\"]],[\"normal\",\" (bare Carathéodory + zero-padding reindex\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"wz_fin_pad_sum\"]],[\"normal\",\"): reduces \"],[\"code\",[\"M ∈ convexHull (range Φ)\"]],[\"normal\",\" to weights \"],[\"code\",[\"λ_j\"]],[\"normal\",\" on letters \"],[\"code\",[\"u_j = σ j\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]],[false,null,null,[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Kernel reconstruction — \"],[\"code\",[\"κ'(x,j) = (λ_j/P_U(u_j))·κ(x,u_j)\"]],[\"normal\",\" on \"],[\"code\",[\"P_X(x) > 0\"]],[\"normal\",\" rows (with a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"fixed-pmf override on \"],[\"code\",[\"P_X(x)=0\"]],[\"normal\",\" rows, invisible since \"],[\"code\",[\"P_XY(x,·)=0\"]],[\"normal\",\" there); decoder slice\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"f'(j,·) = f(u_j,·)\"]],[\"normal\",\". Feasibility (\"],[\"code\",[\"distortion' = distortion ≤ D\"]],[\"normal\",\", via the \"],[\"code\",[\"δ\"]],[\"normal\",\"-coordinate)\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"and objective equality (\"],[\"code\",[\"objective' = objective\"]],[\"normal\",\", via the \"],[\"code\",[\"g\"]],[\"normal\",\"-coordinate + the block-scaling\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"block_j(κ') = (λ_j/P_U(u_j))·block_{u_j}(κ)\"]],[\"normal\",\" from \"],[\"code\",[\"Real.negMulLog_mul\"]],[\"normal\",\" + mass equality) are\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"proved directly, so \"],[\"code\",[\"objective' = objective\"]],[\"normal\",\", whence \"],[\"code\",[\"≤\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"@audit:ok (non-circular and non-bundled: \"],[\"code\",[\"h_pmf\"]],[\"normal\",\" is simplex regularity, \"],[\"code\",[\"hκ\"]],[\"normal\",\" the input datum\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"being reduced, and the conclusion \"],[\"code\",[\"∃ κ' : Fin (|α|+3)\"]],[\"normal\",\" feasible with objective ≤ is not a\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"hypothesis restated; the objective is proven equal — stronger than ≤ — and distortion\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"preserved exactly, so the reduction genuinely follows.)\"]]]]]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.WynerZiv.Converse.Prelim module doc 3", 8044,
   "### Local finite pmf → measure realization (for the DPI gateway)\x0a\x0a`wzPmfMeasure p = ∑ t, ENNReal.ofReal (p t) • δ_t` realizes a finite pmf vector as\x0aa measure; on `stdSimplex` members it is a probability measure with\x0a`.real {t} = p t`. Mirrors `ChannelCoding.pmfToMeasure` (kept local to avoid a heavy\x0a`ShannonTheorem` import). ",
   "[[\"header\",3,[[\"normal\",\"Local finite pmf → measure realization (for the DPI gateway)\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"code\",[\"wzPmfMeasure p = ∑ t, ENNReal.ofReal (p t) • δ_t\"]],[\"normal\",\" realizes a finite pmf vector as\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"a measure; on \"],[\"code\",[\"stdSimplex\"]],[\"normal\",\" members it is a probability measure with\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\".real {t} = p t\"]],[\"normal\",\". Mirrors \"],[\"code\",[\"ChannelCoding.pmfToMeasure\"]],[\"normal\",\" (kept local to avoid a heavy\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"ShannonTheorem\"]],[\"normal\",\" import).\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.wynerZivRate_le_of_code", 8044,
   "Per-code converse bound (i.i.d.-source realization). For a single block\x0aWyner–Ziv code `c : WynerZivCode M n α β γ` with expected block distortion at most\x0a`D`, the reshaped Wyner–Ziv rate is bounded by the block log-cardinality rate\x0a`(1/n) · log M`.\x0a\x0aThis is the i.i.d.-source plumbing of the converse: the canonical i.i.d. source is\x0athe product measure `Measure.pi (fun _ ↦ P_XY)` on `(α × β)^n` with coordinate\x0aprojections `Xs i ω := (ω i).1`, `Ys i ω := (ω i).2`, whose independence and\x0aidentical marginals (`= P_XY`) are supplied by `iIndepFun_iff_map_fun_eq_pi_map` and\x0a`Measure.pi_map_eval`. The bound is then the `n`-letter single-letterized converse\x0a`wyner_ziv_converse_n_letter_singleLetter`. ",
   "[[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"Per-code converse bound (i.i.d.-source realization). For a single block\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"Wyner–Ziv code \"],[\"code\",[\"c : WynerZivCode M n α β γ\"]],[\"normal\",\" with expected block distortion at most\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"D\"]],[\"normal\",\", the reshaped Wyner–Ziv rate is bounded by the block log-cardinality rate\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"(1/n) · log M\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]],[\"p\",[[\"normal\",\"This is the i.i.d.-source plumbing of the converse: the canonical i.i.d. source is\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"the product measure \"],[\"code\",[\"Measure.pi (fun _ ↦ P_XY)\"]],[\"normal\",\" on \"],[\"code\",[\"(α × β)^n\"]],[\"normal\",\" with coordinate\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"projections \"],[\"code\",[\"Xs i ω := (ω i).1\"]],[\"normal\",\", \"],[\"code\",[\"Ys i ω := (ω i).2\"]],[\"normal\",\", whose independence and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"normal\",\"identical marginals (\"],[\"code\",[\"= P_XY\"]],[\"normal\",\") are supplied by \"],[\"code\",[\"iIndepFun_iff_map_fun_eq_pi_map\"]],[\"normal\",\" and\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"Measure.pi_map_eval\"]],[\"normal\",\". The bound is then the \"],[\"code\",[\"n\"]],[\"normal\",\"-letter single-letterized converse\"],[\"softbr\",\"\\n\"],[\"code\",[\"wyner_ziv_converse_n_letter_singleLetter\"]],[\"normal\",\".\"]]]]"),
  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.WynerZiv.FactorizableRate module doc 7", 8044,
