  ("InformationTheory.Shannon.wynerZivRate_convex_in_D", 8044,
   "The reshaped Wyner–Ziv rate is convex in `D`. This follows directly from the\x0atime-sharing closure `wzRateValueSet_timeShare_mem`: every mixture `a·v₁ + b·v₂`\x0alies in the value set at the mixed budget, so its infimum is bounded above by\x0a`a·v₁ + b·v₂` for all attainable `v₁, v₂`; taking nested infima gives the convex\x0abound. The `Nonempty` side conditions feed `le_csInf` (via `le_mul_csInf`) and\x0a`BddBelow` at the mixed budget feeds `csInf_le`; both are standard regularity\x0apreconditions, not load-bearing core.\x0a\x0a@audit:ok sorryAx-free, `#print axioms` = [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Signature\x0ahonest: `h_ne₁`/`h_ne₂` are the `Nonempty` side conditions of `le_csInf` (via\x0a`le_mul_csInf`), `h_bdd_mix` is the `BddBelow` side condition of `csInf_le` — both\x0astandard infimum regularity (side conditions of the sInf lemmas, NOT the theorem's\x0aasserted value, mirroring the already-audited `wynerZivRate_antitone`). `h_pmf`\x0afeeds `wzRateValueSet_timeShare_mem`; `ha`/`hb`/`hab` are convex weights. The\x0aconvexity content is proven in-body via the time-sharing closure + nested infima,\x0anot bundled. Convexity direction and coefficients verified correct; `a=1,b=0`\x0aboundary reduces to reflexivity (alive), stated over the reshaped `wynerZivRate`. ",
